en implements to ensure State Farm Machinery business growth.\\\\nLiaison with Government officials (Agriculture officials.identify Dealerships/Distributors and Retailers to develop a channel network to increase coverage as well as business.\\\\nConduct detailed competition analysis, identify gaps at Dealer/Distributor level and designing specific action plan against competition in those markets.\\\\nAppointment of new Dealership/Distributor who can bring business and are financially stable.\\\\nTraining the Dealerships/Distributors and his available manpower on Implements and selling.\\\\nEnhancing dealer profitability through Farm Machinery business.\\\\nTo interface with the marketing service cell and the manufacturing cell at the Head Office for speedy resolution of service issues at the area office like pending warranty claims, chronic problems etc.\\\\nTimely supply of all Farm Machinery productsservice level 90% plus against monthly demand.\\\\nCoordination with State Tractor team to ensure States Farm Machinery business targets.\\\\nTo ensure resolution of customer complains for sustainable Farm Machinery business.Positioning of New Agricultural Equipment in buoyant market\\\", \\\"System Generated Secondary Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nEngineer, Engineering\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Pune, Pune, IN','Regional Manager - Implements'),(5350,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_4273b438227b','Section Head - Assembly',NULL,NULL,'Mohali, Mohali-Plant 2, IN','Mohali-Plant 2','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nDrive achievement of daily, monthly, and annual production targets by closely monitoring output and proactively addressing gaps.\nEnhance Overall Equipment Effectiveness (OEE) and foster increased efficiency in assembly and painting departments through best practices and innovative approaches.\nResponsible for managing SPQRCE metrics (Safety, Productivity, Quality, Cost, Environment) on the shop floor, providing consistent updates and taking corrective measures as needed.\nImplement and oversee daily work management routines, applying the Plan-Do-Check-Act (PDCA) methodology to control and improve critical process parameters.\nLead detailed root cause analyses and resolve complex issues related to quality, cost overruns, and productivity shortcomings, ensuring sustainable improvements.\nCoach and mentor assembly cell members, nurturing a culture that prioritizes safety, efficiency, and Total Productive Maintenance (TPM).\nChampion Lean manufacturing principles and drive initiatives that leverage technology and process innovation for enhanced operational excellence.\nManage comprehensive tractor assembly processes from planning through execution, guaranteeing seamless workflows and minimal downtime.\nLead manufacturing excellence programs and reinforce quality management systems to uphold the highest product standards.\nDevelop and manage annual departmental budgets, with a focus on optimizing operational expenditures and identifying cost-saving opportunities.\nPromote and enforce The Mahindra Safety Way standards, steering safety committee activities, and striving for an accident-free workplace.\nDrive environmental sustainability efforts by implementing robust Environment Management Systems (EMS) in line with regulatory requirements.\nEnsure strict compliance with statutory obligations as dictated by the Plant Compliance Committee, maintaining legal and regulatory adherence throughout assembly operations.\nEffectively manage employee relations across a diverse workforce, fostering an inclusive and collaborative environment.\nFacilitate productivity enhancements through Lean tools such as MOST (Maynard Operation Sequence Technique) and oversee manpower planning aligned with production needs.\nLead digitization initiatives on the shop floor, utilizing data analytics to support problem-solving and drive informed decision-making.\nPlan, coordinate, and deliver training and development programs targeting officers and managers to build capability and succession planning.\nCollaborate with Product Quality teams to implement and review Manufacturing Quality Plans that ensure consistent product excellence and reduce defects.\nMonitor and enhance internal quality metrics while undertaking improvement projects that raise external customer satisfaction.\nDevelop corrective and preventive action plans to address product and process quality concerns, ensuring continuous improvement.\nFacilitate smooth launch and ramp-up of new product manufacturing, ensuring readiness and capability to meet market demands.\nThis role demands a proactive mindset, strong leadership, and collaboration to achieve operational goals while upholding the reputation of Mahindra & Mahindra as a leader in manufacturing excellence.','',NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mohali-Section-Head-Assembly-Moha/1329288400','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=80','2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','d87ecb44f62c97a4f2e13150391aea6fab5ef8b1b062762292367c9be045ff18','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mohali-Section-Head-Assembly-Moha/1329288400','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Section Head - Assembly\", \"location\": \"Mohali, Mohali-Plant 2, IN\", \"external_id\": \"1329288400\", \"raw_evidence\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Section Head - Assembly\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1329288400\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Mohali-Section-Head-Assembly-Moha/1329288400/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mohali, Mohali-Plant 2, IN\\\"}\"}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:07:58.069585',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:07.672116',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:07.672116',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html cl