space aftermarket automotive boats brand brands business businesses careers change channels clean companies company connect contact contacts counts cultural culture defence directors equipment estate facebook farm finance financial followers formula global good googleapis graph group growth history http https india industry information innovation instagram investors jobs know leadership learn listed mahindra mahindrarise marazzo marketplace media mobility motor news october outreach overview people performance plant presence press previous programmes purpose read real releases reports resources responsibility results rise room services social sport statistics steel stories sustainability tech technology trails twitter users valley video views visit watch wheelers work world youtube\" />\n\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n                <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/fed09ea3-5cdb-4e2b-a362-c.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/customHeader.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/sitebuilderframework.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/BS3ColumnizedSearch.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/fontawesome4.7/css/font-awesome-4.7.0.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n<style>\nbody > .modal-backdrop {\n    display: none !important;\n}\n.menu.desktop .nav > li .dropdown-menu li a{ color : white !important}\n#header .links a{ color: white !important;}\n.dropdown-menu.company-dropdown.headerdropdown.backgroundcolordc8b140b5a119dc3 .menu{ color : black !important}\n.custom-header-menu .nav.nav-pills{ width: 807px !important; }\n.custom-header-signinLanguage .inner.limitwidth{ max-width: 1200px; }\n.customPlugin{ margin-bottom: 0 !important; }\n\n</style>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\"></script></body>\n\n        \n        <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/9349339a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'Mohali',1,'2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','1329288400',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Drive achievement of daily, monthly, and annual production targets by closely monitoring output and proactively addressing gaps.\nEnhance Overall Equipment Effectiveness (OEE) and foster increased efficiency in assembly and painting departments through best practices and innovative approaches.\nResponsible for managing SPQRCE metrics (Safety, Productivity, Quality, Cost, Environment) on the shop floor, providing consistent updates and taking corrective measures as needed.\nImplement and oversee daily work management routines, applying the Plan-Do-Check-Act (PDCA) methodology to control and improve critical process parameters.\nLead detailed root cause analyses and resolve complex issues related to quality, cost overruns, and productivity shortcomings, ensuring sustainable improvements.\nCoach and mentor assembly cell members, nurturing a culture that prioritizes safety, efficiency, and Total Productive Maintenance (TPM).\nChampion Lean manufacturing principles and drive initiatives that leverage technology and process innovation for enhanced operational excellence.\nManage comprehensive tractor assembly processes from planning through execution, guaranteeing seamless workflows and minimal downtime.\nLead manufacturing excellence programs and reinforce quality management systems to uphold the highest product standards.\nDevelop and manage annual departmental budgets, with a focus on optimizing operational expenditures and identifying cost-saving opportunities.\nPromote and enforce The Mahindra Safety Way standards, steering safety committee activities, and striving for an accident-free workplace.\nDrive environmental sustainability efforts by implementing robust Environment Management Systems (EMS) in line with regulatory requirements.\nEnsure strict compliance with statutory obligations as dictated by the Plant Compliance Committee, maintaining legal and regulatory adherence throughout assembly operations.\nEffectively manage employee relations across a diverse workforce, fostering an inclusive and collaborative environment.\nFacilitate productivity enhancements through Lean tools such as MOST (Maynard Operation Sequence Technique) and oversee manpower planning aligned with production needs.\nLead digitization initiatives on the shop floor, utilizing data analytics to support problem-solving and drive informed decision-making.\nPlan, coordinate, and deliver training and development programs targeting officers and managers to build capability and succession planning.\nCollaborate with Product Quality teams to implement and review Manufacturing Quality Plans that ensure consistent product excellence and reduce defects.\nMonitor and enhance internal quality metrics while undertaking improvement projects that raise external customer satisfaction.\nDevelop corrective and preventive action plans to address product and process quality concerns, ensuring continuous improvement.\nFacilitate smooth launch and ramp-up of new product manufacturing, ensuring readiness and capability to meet market demands.\nThis role demands a proactive mindset, strong leadership, and collaboration to achieve operational goals while upholding the reputation of Mahindra & Mahindra as a leader in manufacturing excellence.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"The Section Head - Assembly will take a central role in overseeing all facets of tractor and transmission assembly operations within the Swaraj Division at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd. This leadership position demands strategic planning, operational execution, and continuous improvement initiatives to ensure outstanding performance across safety, quality, productivity, delivery, cost control, and environmental sustainability.\\\\nKey Responsibilities:\\\", \\\"Key Responsibilities\\\": \\\"Drive achievement of daily, monthly, and annual production targets by closely monitoring output and proactively addressing gaps.\\\\nEnhance Overall Equipment Effectiveness (OEE) and foster increased efficiency in assembly and painting departments through best practices and innovative approaches.\\\\nResponsible for managing SPQRCE metrics (Safety, Productivity, Quality, Cost, Environment) on the shop floor, providing consistent updates and taking corrective measures as needed.\\\\nImplement and oversee daily work management routines, applying the Plan-Do-Check-Act (PDCA) methodology to control and improve critical process parameters.\\\\nLead detailed root cause analyses and resolve complex issues related to quality, cost overruns, and productivity shortcomings, ensuring sustainable improvements.\\\\nCoach and mentor assembly cell members, nurturing a culture that prioritizes safety, efficiency, and Total Productive Maintenance (TPM).\\\\nChampion Lean manufacturing principles and drive initiatives that leverage technology and process innovation for enhanced operational excellence.\\\\nManage comprehensive tractor assembly processes from planning through execution, guaranteeing seamless workflows and minimal downtime.\\\\nLead manufacturing excellence programs and reinforce quality management systems to uphold the highest product standards.\\\\nDevelop and manage annual departmental budgets, with a focus on optimizing operational expenditures and identifying cost-saving opportunities.\\\\nPromote and enforce The Mahindra Safety Way standards, steering safety committee activities, and striving for an accident-free workplace.\\\\nDrive environmental sustainability efforts by implementing robust Environment Management Systems (EMS) in line with regulatory requirements.\\\\nEnsure strict compliance with statutory obligations as dictated by the Plant Compliance Committee, maintaining legal and regulatory adherence throughout assembly operations.\\\\nEffectively manage employee relations across a diverse workforce, fostering an inclusive and collaborative environment.\\\\nFacilitate productivity enhancements through Lean tools such as MOST (Maynard Operation Sequence Technique) and oversee manpower planning aligned with production needs.\\\\nLead digitization initiatives on the shop floor, utilizing data analytics to support problem-solving and drive informed decision-making.\\\\nPlan, coordinate, and deliver training and development programs targeting officers and managers to build capability and succession planning.\\\\nCollaborate with Product Quality teams to implement and review Manufacturing Quality Plans that ensure consistent product excellence and reduce defects.\\\\nMonitor and enhance internal quality metrics while undertaking improvement projects that raise external customer satisfaction.\\\\nDevelop corrective and preventive action plans to address product and process quality concerns, ensuring continuous improvement.\\\\nFacilitate smooth launch and ramp-up of new product manufacturing, ensuring readiness and capability to meet market demands.\\\\nThis role demands a proactive mindset, strong leadership, and collaboration to achieve operational goals while upholding the reputation of Mahindra & Mahindra as a leader in manufacturing excellence.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"The ideal candidate will hold a\\\\nBachelor of Technology (B.Tech) or Bachelor of Engineering (B.E.)\\\\ndegree specialising in Mechanical, Automobile, Production, or Industrial Engineering. This strong technical foundation is essential to comprehend complex manufacturing processes and drive advancements in assembly operations.\\\\nAdditionally, possessing a\\\\nMaster of Business Administration (MBA)\\\\nis highly valued to equip the candidate with strategic management, leadership, and business acumen skills required for this senior role.\\\\nEducational qualifications should reflect a commitment to continuous learning, with an openness to advanced certifications or training in Lean Manufacturing, TPM, Quality Management Systems, and Industry 4.0 technologies considered advantageous.\\\\nCandidates who have pursued additional professional development courses relevant to safety management, environmental standards, and labour law will be especially well-suited to meet the multi-dimensional demands of this position.\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"We seek professionals with extensive industry experience ranging between\\\\n15 to 20 years\\\\nin manufacturing operations, particularly within automotive and tractor assembly environments. A candidate profile typically aligns with an age range near to 40 years, representing a blend of maturity and dynamic leadership potential.\\\\nExperience must encompass multi-disciplinary collaboration involving stakeholders across Product Quality, Supplier Quality, Manufacturing Engineering, Research & Development (R&D), Sourcing, Supply Chain Management, Employee Relations, Finance, Maintenance, Sales, and Customer Service. This exposure ensures holistic understanding of manufacturing ecosystems and fosters seamless integration of assembly operations with other functional areas.\\\\nDemonstrated history of managing large teams and complex projects in high-volume production settings is essential, alongside a proven track record of meeting stringent performance metrics and operational KPIs.\\\\nThe ability to adapt and lead through change in a fast-paced environment, while maintaining employee engagement and operational excellence, is critical for success in this role.\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"The candidate must possess robust expertise in strategic execution and possess exceptional leadership capabilities to steer cross-functional teams towards achieving manufacturing objectives. Advanced communication skills are crucial, bridging technical and managerial domains to ensure clear, effective stakeholder engagement.\\\\nIn-depth knowledge of operation management with a focus on transmission assembly processes is mandatory, including familiarity with the end-to-end production cycle and equipment capabilities.\\\\nMastery of advanced problem-solving techniques and Lean manufacturing principles, combined with hands-on experience in implementing Total Productive Maintenance (TPM), forms the backbone of the critical experience required.\\\\nThe role demands a strong drive for results, coupled with an understanding of Industry 4.0 technologies to integrate digital transformation and data-driven decision-making into production workflows.\\\\nExpertise in stakeholder management, legal compliance including labour laws, and environment, health, and safety management systems underscores the candidate\\\\u2019s ability to navigate regulatory landscapes and maintain operational integrity.\\\\nEssential behavioural competencies include collaboration, agility, and bold decision-making, supporting a culture that embraces innovation and continuous improvement. Knowledge of methodologies such as MOST and compliance frameworks like the International Labour Organization (ILO) standards will be beneficial to effectively manage manpower and operational practices.\\\", \\\"System Generated Secondary Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nR&D Engineer, Industrial Engineer, Manufacturing Engineer, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mohali, Mohali-Plant 2, IN','Section Head - Assembly'),(5353,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_b199964c2fe2','Assistant Manager - Maintenance (ETA)',NULL,NULL,'Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-AD, IN','Zaheerabad-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Siemens PLC, HMI & SCADA, Servo Drives & Servo Motors, CNC Machine Maintenance (Mazak Preferred), Electrical Troubleshooting, Pneumatics & Hydraulics, Engine Test Bed Maintenance, Fixturized Torquing System Maintenance, Leak Test Equipment Maintenance, Sealant Dispensing System Maintenance, VFD Programming & Maintenance, Preventive & Predictive Maintenance, Root Cause Analysis',NULL,'TECHNICAL SKILLS / KNOWLEDGE:\nSiemens PLC, HMI & SCADA\nServo Drives & Servo Motors\nCNC Machine Maintenance (Mazak Preferred)\nElectrical Troubleshooting\nPneumatics & Hydraulics\nEngine Test Bed Maintenance\nFixturized Torquing System Maintenance\nLeak Test Equipment Maintenance\nSealant Dispensing System Maintenance\nVFD Programming & Maintenance\nPreventive & Predictive Maintenance\nRoot Cause Analysis',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Zaheerabad-Assistant-Manager-Maintenance-%28ETA%29-Zahe/1438573100','ht