 breakdowns, Tools and equipment problems.Ensure that Daily production formats are filled as actuals.Verify cleaning of plant, machinery and equipment and fixture as per the cleaning schedule.\\\\nResponsible to achieve required targets on Productivity, Quality and Safety for Respective Production Line.\\\\nCoordination with sheet metal as a Supplier and with Assembly shop as an Internal Customer for Quality and Quantity.Interaction with other sections of the Paint shop- Technical Support, planning, Process, Maintenance and QA to improve and achieve the required targets.\\\\nEnsure that Actions are planned and taken without undue delay for the Issues raised during Product Audit, Process Audits and Internal Audits for ISO 9001:2008 and ISO 14001:2004 and Monitor the Effectiveness of The actions through audit trends.\\\\nCoordination for the Production trials for new model launch.\\\\nHandling internal customer quality concerns.Initiate the Continual Improvement Project/Action through KVP for Productivity Improvement, Quality Improvement, Cost reduction, Safety Enhancement Etc.\\\\nEnsure compliance to ISO 9001:2008 and ISO 14001:2004 and safety requirements\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"Be/Btech Chemical/Paint\\\", \\\"System Generated Core Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nIndustrial, Painter, Manufacturing\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mohali, Mohali-Plant 1, IN','AM/Deputy Mgr. Paint Shop'),(5361,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_423149b77fae','Medical Officer',NULL,NULL,'Rudrapur, Rudrapur Plant, IN','Rudrapur Plant','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\n1) Management of medical emergencies injuries\n2) Handling of day to day OPD treatment for walk in patients in OHC\n3) Complete coordination and execution of Statutory  Health check-up\n4)  Deriving Health Index of all permanent employees of the plant as per H and W policy\n5) Implementation of measures to improve health index of all the employees\n6) Implementation of all statutory requirements of OHC and OHSAS audit preparation\n7) Handling  of  all medical administration activities\n8) To train OHC staff to upgrade their functional competencies\n9) Medical budget related activities\nLeadership Competencies –\n1) Result Orientation with Execution Excellence\n2) Customer Focus\n3) Weaving Passion and Energy at work\n4) Leveraging Human Capital\nFunctional Competencies –\n1) Thorough clinical knowledge with strong inclination to upgrade the same\n2) Good knowledge of Occupational health management\n3) Expert in software skills like medical software management ,\n4) Excellent  Communication Skills\nExperience\n5 Years of Industry Experience\nIndustry Preferred\nQualifications\nMBBS AFIH\nGeneral Requirements\nOur commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\nAt Mahindra and Mahindra Limited, we believe that diversity drives innovation, and inclusion is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to cultivating a workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to age, caste, race, religion, color, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital or domestic partnership status, pregnancy or childbirth, veteran status, citizenship status, ancestry, financial status, or any other personal characteristic protected by applicable law.\nWe actively encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply and bring their unique perspectives to our teams. We are committed to ensuring an accessible and inclusive experience for all applicants.\nTogether, we rise by embracing di