o SOP, achieving cost, weight, quality, performance, craftsmanship and timing targets.\\\", \\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"\\\\u2022 Lead system delivery against cost, weight, quality, performance, craftsmanship and timing targets.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Drive status reviews, milestone tracking, risk identification and timely escalation.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Lead engineering feasibility assessments and robust design-change management.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Coordinate tooling development, manufacturing readiness and launch execution.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Ensure process capability, product quality and smooth SOP delivery.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Guide Styling, Product Planning and Platform teams through benchmarking and feasibility inputs.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Drive technology evaluation, proof-of-concept development and future interior roadmaps.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Manage DVP&R risks across regulatory, functional, durability, NVH, safety and perceived quality.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Track regulations, emerging technologies, sustainable materials and customer expectations.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Drive value engineering, material optimization and continuous improvement\\\\n\\\\u2022 Align Suppliers, Purchasing, Manufacturing, Validation and Product Planning on program targets.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Lead CAE, NVH, BSR, STA, DE, Validation, PQ, Manufacturing Engineering and PVT interfaces.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Mentor engineering teams through structured problem-solving and knowledge sharing.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Promote technical excellence and adherence to engineering best practices.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Interior trim packaging, vehicle integration and system engineering expertise.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Knowledge of IS/AIS, ECE, ADR and FMVSS standards and DVP requirements.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Strong project management, risk management and problem-solving capability.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Knowledge of automotive trends and emerging technologies.\\\", \\\"Behavioural Fit\\\": \\\"\\\\u2022 Strong leadership and team-building skills.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Customer-centric thinking and idea generation.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Effective stakeholder communication and escalation discipline.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Ability to anticipate trends and drive innovation.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"7 to 13 years of Experience.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Extensive experience in automotive interior trim design and development.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Expertise in end-to-end trim delivery from concept to SOP.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Proven cross-functional leadership and program target achievement.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Strong focus on customer experience, perceived quality, comfort, convenience and aesthetics.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Hard Trims: Door Trims, Console, Pillars and Garnishes.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Soft Trims: Headliner, Sun Visors, Parcel Shelf and Wrapped Components.\\\\n\\\\u2022 NVH Components and Trim / Closure Interfaces.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Decorative and Premium Finish Systems.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Interior Perceived Quality and Craftsmanship.\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"BE/M.Tech\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nManufacturing Engineer, Systems Engineer, Engineer, Engineering Manager, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Chennai\", \"title\": \"Lead Engineer - Trims Engineering CoE\", \"location\": \"Chennai, Nashik Ambad-AD, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=300\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Lead Engineer - Trims Engineering CoE\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1436606200\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Chennai-Lead-Engineer-Trims-Engineering-CoE-Nash/1436606200/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Chennai, Nashik Ambad-AD, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Lead-Engineer-Trims-Engineering-CoE-Nash/1436606200/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1436606200\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','a