LL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"The ideal candidate will be responsible for ensuring efficient and effective management of all warehouse activities, including inventory management, order fulfilment. The role requires a strong leader with excellent organizational skills, a keen eye for detail, and the ability to optimize warehouse operations.\\\\nKey Responsibilities:\\\", \\\"Key Responsibilities\\\": \\\"Warehouse Operations Management:\\\\nOversee and manage daily warehouse operations, ensuring smooth and efficient processes.\\\\nDevelop and implement standard operating procedures (SOPs) for receiving, handling, storing, and dispatching automotive spare parts.\\\\nMonitor and manage warehouse layout and space utilization to maximize operational efficiency.\\\\nEnsure timely and accurate processing of orders, from receipt to dispatch.\\\\nCoordinate with various stakeholder & ensure alignment of warehouse activities with business needs.\\\\nInventory Control:\\\\nImplement and maintain robust inventory management systems to track stock levels, turnover rates, and order accuracy.\\\\nConduct regular inventory audits and cycle counts to ensure data accuracy.\\\\nIdentify and manage slow-moving and obsolete inventory to optimize stock levels.\\\\nPeople Management:\\\\nLead, train, and develop a team of warehouse onrole & offrole staff\\\\nSet performance goals, conduct regular performance reviews, and provide feedback and coaching.\\\\nEnsure adherence to safety protocols and compliance with company policies.\\\\nHealth and Safety:\\\\nEnsure that all warehouse operations comply with health and safety regulations.\\\\nConduct regular safety audits and implement corrective actions as needed.\\\\nPromote a culture of safety awareness and continuous improvement among warehouse staff.\\\\nTechnology and Systems:\\\\nOversee the implementation and utilization of warehouse management systems (WMS) and other relevant technology.\\\\nOperating knowledge of various automation eg- Conveyors (WCS), sorters etc\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"BE/B.Tech/MBA\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"Minimum 5-8 years of experience in warehouse management, preferably in the automotive spare parts sector.\\\\nProven track record of managing large-scale warehouses\\\\nStrong understanding of inventory management systems, WMS.\\\\nExcellent leadership and team management skills.\\\\nStrong analytical and problem-solving abilities.\\\\nAbility to work under pressure and meet tight deadlines.\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"Key Competencies:\\\", \\\"Key Competencies\\\": \\\"Leadership and People Management\\\\nInventory and Warehouse Management\\\\nLean Management, TPM\\\\nProblem Solving and Decision Making\\\\nCommunication and Collaboration\\\\nSystems/ SAP knowledge:\\\\nMS Office & Hands on experience with SAP/SAP-EWM\\\\nAny Additional Knowledge:\\\\nHands on experience on AI, Automation, Access, PowerBi, Qlik shall have added advantage\\\", \\\"Systems/ SAP knowledge\\\": \\\"MS Office & Hands on experience with SAP/SAP-EWM\\\", \\\"Any Additional Knowledge\\\": \\\"Hands on experience on AI, Automation, Access, PowerBi, Qlik shall have added advantage\\\", \\\"System Generated Secondary Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nWarehouse, Warehouse Manager, Automotive, Manufacturing\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kanhe, Kanhe, IN','Dy. Manager - Warehouse Operations'),(5392,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_f6deba9185cd','MANAGER WAREHOUSE OPERATIONS',NULL,NULL,'Nashik, Nas Plant I-AD, IN','Nas Plant I-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nCoordinate between inbound, outbound and Inventory teams for any operational issues and effective team performanc