ss Audit\nCompliance to legal & Statutory norms\nAdequate Training of team\nSLA assessment\nDeliverables-\nFast Fill Rate as per targets\nAlignment of Internal business processes for achieving revenue & service level target\nDiscrepancy Control & Resolution\n5S, Kaizen & Lean\nInventory accuracy, Stock to Dock & Dock to Stock',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Coordinate between inbound, outbound and Inventory teams for any operational issues and effective team performance.\\\\nWork closely with the customer care, BA (or any other third party vendor), Demand planning, Sourcing, Quality, Packaging and his team for attainment of KPI\\\\u2019s.\\\\nMonitoring MIS & KPI\\\\u2019s and taking corrective measures in case of non-attainment.\\\\nResponsible for overall inventory accuracy, process adherence and 5S for the site .\\\\nDriving process improvement / cost saving / productivity improvement projects.\\\\nCustomer Management and working towards increase in customer satisfaction index.\\\\nMonitoring operating cost for his location and ensures within defined limit\\\\nRegular Process Audit\\\\nCompliance to legal & Statutory norms\\\\nAdequate Training of team\\\\nSLA assessment\\\\nDeliverables-\\\\nFast Fill Rate as per targets\\\\nAlignment of Internal business processes for achieving revenue & service level target\\\\nDiscrepancy Control & Resolution\\\\n5S, Kaizen & Lean\\\\nInventory accuracy, Stock to Dock & Dock to Stock\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"BE/B.Tech/MBA\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"Min 4-7 Yrs\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"Systems/ SAP knowledge:\\\", \\\"Systems/ SAP knowledge\\\": \\\"MS Office & Hands on experience with SAP/Equivalent ERP\\\\nAny Additional Knowledge:\\\", \\\"Any Additional Knowledge\\\": \\\"MM Module & SD Module, Access, PowerBi\\\", \\\"System Generated Secondary Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nWarehouse Manager, Warehouse, Manufacturing\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nashik, Nas Plant I-AD, IN','MANAGER WAREHOUSE OPERATIONS'),(5393,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_ee05f793a6c2','Mgr Digital Projects & Transformation',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai-Goregaon, Kandvali - corp, IN','Kandvali - corp','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Job Description: Digital Projects & Transformation Manager\nDigital Projects & Transformation Manager\nLocation: Mumbai\nExperience: 5–10 years\nThe Opportunity\nMahindra Agri Business has a diversified presence across five businesses – Seeds, Seed Potato, Crop Care, Fruits and Micro Irrigation. Digital initiatives are an important enabler of simpler processes, operational effectiveness, and better customer and stakeholder experiences.\nWe are looking for a Digital Projects & Transformation Manager to drive priority initiatives from definition through implementation, adoption and value realization, working closely with business teams, internal IT teams and external partners.\nThe Role\nAs a member of the central team, the individual will coordinate a portfolio of digital projects across Mahindra Agri. The role requires strong program and stakeholder management, an understanding of business processes, technology fluency, and the ability to bring structure, momentum and follow-through to multiple initiatives.\nKey Responsibilities\nDrive priority digital initiatives across the five Mahindra Agri businesses, bringing structure, momentum and program management discipline through the project lifecycle.\nManage projects through implementation, ensuring clarity on requirements, scope, ownership, timelines, dependencies and expected business outcomes.\nWork with business stakeholders to understand, challenge and refine requirements, and translate them into clear Business Requirement Documents (BRDs) and functional requirements for technology teams and partners.\nAct as the interface between business teams, internal IT teams and external vendors, ensuring alignment and timely issue resolution.\nAssess appropriate delivery approaches and partners based on business requirements.\nLead initiatives across process and workflow automation, customer- and dealer-facing solutions, business applications, data insights and dashboards, custom developments, and AI-enabled use cases.\nMaintain awareness of emerging AI capabilities and relevant technology and vendor ecosystems.\nSupport user adoption and track whether implemented initiatives deliver the intended business outcomes and value.\nMaintain portfolio visibility for management, highlighting key risks, dependencies and areas requiring intervention.\nCandidate Profile\n5–10 years of relevant experience, with strong exposure to implementing and managing IT or digital projects.\nStrong project and program management capability, with the ability to independently drive multiple initiatives.\nStrong stakeholder management and influencing skills, with the ability to work effectively across business teams, internal IT teams and external vendors.\nAbility to understand business processes, challenge and refine requirements, and prepare or validate BRDs and functional requirements.\nWorking knowledge of IT concepts, business applications, and process or workflow automation.\nExperience working with technology vendors and implementation partners; familiarity with the relevant application vendor ecosystem would be an advantage.\nExposure to AI-enabled projects and evolving AI tools and applications would be valuable.\nExperience in an in-house transformation or digital role within an Indian enterprise would be valuable.\nExposure to agriculture, chemicals, manufacturing or adjacent industries would be preferred, though not mandatory.\nEntrepreneurial, agile and comfortable working in a fast-paced, exciting and evolving environment.\nBachelor’s or Master’s degree in Engineering, Technology, Management or a related discipline.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-Goregaon-Mgr-Digital-Projects-&-Transformation-Kand/1436602200','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=180','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','b027e42536f338aae19433ddc41c5c8623fba15a24ccfaae211e750dd3754aa5','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-Goregaon-Mgr-Digital-Projects-&-Transformation-Kand/1436602200','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Mgr Digital Projects & Transformation\", \"location\": \"Mumbai-Goregaon, Kandvali - corp, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Job Description: Digital Projects & Transformation Manager\", \"Digital Projects & Transformation Manager\", \"The Opportunity\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:13.484653',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:22.980805',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platform/bootstrap/3.4.8_NES/css/bootstrap.min.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/bootstrapV3.global.responsive.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel