Plant, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=300\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"CKD Officer\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1436604200\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Nagpur-CKD-Officer-Nagp/1436604200/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-CKD-Officer-Nagp/1436604200/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1436604200\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN','CKD Officer'),(5395,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_0604710df855','Senior Engineer - Concept Engineering & Analysis',NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV(FD), IN','Chennai-MRV(FD)','India',NULL,NULL,'Experience in drafting performance specifications for new tractor programs.','BE',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nVehicle Performance Definition & Analysis:\nEstablish vehicle speed targets for various operating conditions and applications.\nDefine engine torque and power curves based on intended tractor application and market requirements.\nDefine drivetrain performance targets including:\nDrawbar performance\nPTO performance\nTransport performance\nGradability\nAcceleration capability\nDevelop and monitor vehicle power loss targets across engine, transmission, hydraulic, and driveline systems.\nConduct concept-level performance simulations and trade-off studies.\nBenchmark competitor tractors and derive performance targets.\nSystem-Level Engineering Analysis:\nAnalyze interactions between:\nEngine\nTransmission\nAxles\nHydraulics\nPTO systems\nVehicle electronics\nSupport selection of gear ratios and transmission architectures to achieve optimum vehicle performance.\nEvaluate tractor architecture impacts on performance, fuel efficiency, and productivity.\nIdentify performance gaps and recommend corrective actions during development.\nCalibration & Electronic Features Support:\nSupport performance tuning and calibration activities of electronically controlled tractor features.\nReview calibration requirements affecting:\nVehicle productivity\nFuel economy\nDrivability\nOperator comfort\nWork with calibration teams to define target operating strategies.\nField Performance Data Analysis:\nAnalyze field test data, customer usage data, validation test reports, and telemetry data to identify performance gaps.\nCorrelate field issues with vehicle subsystems such as engine, transmission, hydraulics, PTO, and electronic control systems.\nPerform root cause analysis for productivity, fuel consumption, drivability, and performance-related concerns.\nQuickly convert field observations into actionable engineering recommendations.\nSupport field investigation activities and provide technical guidance for issue resolution.\nDevelop data-driven corrective action proposals and improvement plans.\nTractor Architecture & Hard Point Engineering:\nDevelop strong understanding of complete tractor architecture.\nDefine and evaluate critical hard points related to:\nEngine integration\nTransmission layout\nWheelbase\nGround clearance\nHitch geometry\nPTO location\nHydraulic interfaces\nOperator station\nSupport concept packaging and platform development activities.\nCross-Functional Collaboration:\nCoordinate with Engine, Transmission, Hydraulics, Vehicle Integration, and Validation teams.\nSupport target cascading from customer requirements to subsystem requirements.\nParticipate in design reviews and concept feasibility studies.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nLogical\nPositive attitude\nCollaborative\nWorking beyond boundaries\nProblem Solving Skill\nAbility to work in a team\nBasic understanding of tractors and its subsystem.\nHands-on understanding of tractor field applications.\nExperience in drafting performance specifications for new tractor programs.\nInterest in field testing, customer interaction, and future product concept development.\nStrong understanding of tractor powertrain, vehicle architecture, and agricultural mechanization.\nFunctional Competencies:',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Senior-Engineer-Concept-Engineering-&-Analysis-Chen/1436114200','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=200','2026-10-13T12:15:13.525085+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','e1b8fe7fd5d5d1047891beab78f9750c436e7a8b82784aff78ed978f9cd46b0f','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Senior-Engineer-Concept-Engineering-&-Analysis-Chen/1436114200','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Senior Engineer - Concept Engineering & Analysis\", \"location\": \"Chennai, Chennai-MRV(FD), IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\", \"General Requirements\", \"Functional Competencies\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:13.719269',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:23.231377',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:23.231377',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platform/bootstrap/3.4.8_NES/css/bootstrap.min.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"styles