ta-driven corrective action proposals and improvement plans.\\\\nTractor Architecture & Hard Point Engineering:\\\\nDevelop strong understanding of complete tractor architecture.\\\\nDefine and evaluate critical hard points related to:\\\\nEngine integration\\\\nTransmission layout\\\\nWheelbase\\\\nGround clearance\\\\nHitch geometry\\\\nPTO location\\\\nHydraulic interfaces\\\\nOperator station\\\\nSupport concept packaging and platform development activities.\\\\nCross-Functional Collaboration:\\\\nCoordinate with Engine, Transmission, Hydraulics, Vehicle Integration, and Validation teams.\\\\nSupport target cascading from customer requirements to subsystem requirements.\\\\nParticipate in design reviews and concept feasibility studies.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"3 to 6 years\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Tractor/Automotive Transmission\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"BE / B.Tech / ME / M.Tech (Mechanical / Automobile/Mechatronics)\\\", \\\"General Requirements\\\": \\\"Logical\\\\nPositive attitude\\\\nCollaborative\\\\nWorking beyond boundaries\\\\nProblem Solving Skill\\\\nAbility to work in a team\\\\nBasic understanding of tractors and its subsystem.\\\\nHands-on understanding of tractor field applications.\\\\nExperience in drafting performance specifications for new tractor programs.\\\\nInterest in field testing, customer interaction, and future product concept development.\\\\nStrong understanding of tractor powertrain, vehicle architecture, and agricultural mechanization.\\\\nFunctional Competencies:\\\", \\\"Functional Competencies\\\": \\\"Tractor performance analysis.\\\\nDraft load estimation and application engineering.\\\\nEngine torque and power matching.\\\\nVehicle speed chart preparation.\\\\nPower loss and drivetrain efficiency calculations.\\\\nTractor architecture and vehicle layout understanding.\\\\nKnowledge of agricultural implements and field operations.\\\\nVehicle simulation and analytical tools.\\\\nStrong proficiency in Microsoft Excel, AVL concerto, data analysis tools\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nHydraulics, Application Engineering, Drafting, Electronics Engineer, Engineer, Engineering\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV(FD), IN','Senior Engineer - Concept Engineering & Analysis'),(5396,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_8735590020bd','Dy Manager - Product QA',NULL,NULL,'Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-FD, IN','Zaheerabad-FD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nYour responsibilities will be crucial in ensuring the quality of tractors through product and process audits of tractor assembly, paint shop, and PTCED shop.\nYou will utilize your expertise in sheet metal and plastic components, support continuous process improvements, handle new product and process implementation, and resolve concerns reported in new products. Additionally, you will be responsible for engine and transmission aggregate assembly functional knowledge, customer complaint analysis, and quality assurance functions in the assembly plant.\nYou will play a key role in analysing customer complaints, assembly line rejections, supplier parts, and taking corrective actions to standardize all quality procedures.\nYour experience in quality management systems like ISO 9001, TS 16949, and TPM will be valuable in implementing best practices and achieving consistent product quality.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Zaheerabad-Dy-Manager-Product-QA-Zahe/1413609100','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=200','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','2cfebc362cefe0c1fe4824294fe9d86d5a39cda73ed0304b3b5baa4034ce0b61','COMP_TOP200_011','h