sis & Preventive Actions\n•Conduct detailed RCA for major escalations.\n•Identify recurring concerns and systemic gaps.\n•Recommend corrective and preventive actions to reduce complaint recurrence.\n•Track implementation of action plans across stakeholders.\n7) Governance & Performance Monitoring\n•Monitor complaint ageing and escalation pendency.\n•Drive adherence to resolution TAT and quality standards.\n•Present periodic escalation dashboards to leadership.\n•Highlight emerging customer risks, dealer risks, and process gaps.\n8) Dealer Capability & Compliance\n•Coach dealers and field teams on escalation handling.\n•Identify dealer-specific complaint patterns.\n•Recommend interventions for improving dealer customer experience performance.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Purpose of the Role:\\\", \\\"Purpose of the Role\\\": \\\"To lead the resolution of critical customer complaints and escalations arising from vehicle sales, delivery, product quality, service, dealer operations, and customer handling. The role is responsible for restoring customer confidence through timely intervention, cross-functional coordination, effective communication, and sustainable closure of high-impact customer issues while driving systemic improvements through root cause analysis.\\\\nKey Accountabilities:\\\", \\\"Key Accountabilities\\\": \\\"1) Customer Escalation Management\\\\n\\\\u2022Own end-to-end resolution of critical customer complaints received through:\\\\n-MD/ED/CEO Office\\\\n-Social Media\\\\n-Regulatory Authorities\\\\n-Consumer Forums\\\\n-Senior Management Escalations\\\\n-CRM & Contact Centre\\\\n\\\\u2022Ensure immediate customer contact and acknowledgement within defined SLA.\\\\n\\\\u2022Drive timely closure of escalations with clear communication and customer alignment.\\\\n\\\\u2022Handle dissatisfied and repeat-escalation customers with empathy and professionalism.\\\\n2) Sales Experience Escalations\\\\n\\\\u2022Resolve complaints related to:\\\\n-Vehicle booking and delivery delays\\\\n-Sales commitments mismatch\\\\n-Documentation issues\\\\n-Exchange and finance concerns\\\\n-Dealer sales process violations\\\\n\\\\u2022Coordinate with dealers, regional sales teams, and zonal teams for prompt resolutions.\\\\n3) Service Experience Escalations\\\\n\\\\u2022Resolve complaints related to:\\\\n-Vehicle breakdowns\\\\n-Repeat repairs\\\\n-Workshop delays\\\\n-Parts non-availability\\\\n-Warranty disputes\\\\n-Technical diagnosis delays\\\\n-Service quality concerns\\\\n\\\\u2022Work closely with workshop teams, technical support groups, RSA teams, parts teams, and regional service teams.\\\\n4) Cross Functional Coordination\\\\n\\\\u2022Act as a single point of accountability for critical complaint resolution.\\\\n\\\\u2022Escalate bottlenecks to functional heads wherever required.\\\\n\\\\u2022Ensure stakeholder alignment between:\\\\n-Sales\\\\n-Service\\\\n-Parts\\\\n-Warranty\\\\n-Technical Support\\\\n-RSA\\\\n-Dealer Management\\\\n5) Customer Recovery & Retention\\\\n\\\\u2022Lead customer recovery plans for high-risk customers.\\\\n\\\\u2022Drive retention actions for potential vehicle buyback, legal, media, or social media escalation cases.\\\\n\\\\u2022Ensure customer trust restoration through proactive engagement.\\\\n6) Root Cause Analysis & Preventive Actions\\\\n\\\\u2022Conduct detailed RCA for major escalations.\\\\n\\\\u2022Identify recurring concerns and systemic gaps.\\\\n\\\\u2022Recommend corrective and preventive actions to reduce complaint recurrence.\\\\n\\\\u2022Track implementation of action plans across stakeholders.\\\\n7) Governance & Performance Monitoring\\\\n\\\\u2022Monitor complaint ageing and escalation pendency.\\\\n\\\\u2022Drive adherence to resolution TAT and quality standards.\\\\n\\\\u2022Present periodic escalation dashboards to leadership.\\\\n\\\\u2022Highlight emerging customer risks, dealer risks, and process gaps.\\\\n8) Dealer Capability & Compliance\\\\n\\\\u2022Coach dealers and field teams on escalation handling.\\\\n\\\\u2022Identify dealer-specific complaint patterns.\\\\n\\\\u2022Recommend interventions for improving dealer customer experience performance.\\\", \\\"8) Dealer Capability & Compliance\\\": \\\"\\\\u2022Coach dealers and field teams on escalation handling. \\\\u2022Identify dealer-specific complaint patterns. \\\\u2022Recommend interventions for improving dealer customer experience performance.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"Bachelor of Engineering; MBA\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"15+ Years in Automobile Industry (CRM Profiles), Airlines, Hospitality\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"Handling high-value and sensitive customer complaints.\\\\nManaging cross-functional teams without direct reporting relationships.\\\\nDealing with social media and reputation-sensitive cases.\\\\nLeading customer recovery initiatives.\\\\nExposure to field sales and service operations.\\\\nExperience in automotive dealership ecosystem and customer lifecycle management.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nEngineer, Automotive, Engineering\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Mumbai\", \"title\": \"GM - Customer Experience\", \"location\": \"Mumbai, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=320\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"GM - Customer Experience\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1435689900\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Mumbai-GM-Customer-Experience-MUM/1435689900/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mumbai, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-GM-Customer-Experience-MUM/1435689900/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1435689900\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mumbai, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN','GM - Customer Experience'),(5402,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_0a3c5f311e26','Area Sales Manager',NULL,NULL,'Lucknow, Lucknow, IN','Lucknow','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\nRetail Sales - Manage E-T-B-R (Enquiry, Test Drive, Booking, Retail.Plan and execute activations for enquiry generation.Ensure quality and quantity of test drive (from all enquiry sources.Ensure accuracy and authenticity of booking data.Achieve retail as per targets, VDN (Vehicle delivery note) vs Retail ratio.Focus on processes to improve conversion ratio (CVR.Ensure accuracy and authenticity of DMS data.Plan for sales for \'N\' Month.Manpower Productivity - Identify training needs and ensure effectiveness.Motivate and retain manpower by rewards and incentives.Ensure Adherence to Sales story.Digital Conversion - Ensure adoption of digital tools :Test Drive anytime anywhere (TDAA), Personal voice assistant (PVA), Bring Showroom Home (BSH), Virtual Reality (VR) and Tablets to maximise CVR.Ensure adequacy and quality of Digital engagement managers.Dealer working capital rotation.Ageing of stock- Ensure dealer market outstanding reduction, Aging stock liquidation, forecasting for N+1 monthPlan and execute activations for enquiry generation\nPreferred Industries\nConsumer FMCG / Food\nAutomotive Industry\nEducation Qualification\nMBA; Post Graduate Dip in Mgmt\nGeneral Experience\nCore Automotive Sales/ FMCG sales,Experience of 3- 8 years\nCritical Experience\nSystem Generated Core Skills\nCredit Management\nConsumer Focus\nManpower Management\nDealer Relationship Management\nManpower Planning\nMarket Acumen\nSales Planning\nCapability Building\nSystem Generated Secondary Skills\nCapability Building\nChange Management\nConsultative Selling\nStatutory Compliance\nDesigning Customer Experience\nFi