ve the critical customer complaints and measure of customer satisfaction level.\nTo work towards and increase dealer profitability by service schemes like service packages, service coverage improvements, free services, post warranty jobs, annual maintenance contracts.Ensure meeting spare targets of all channel partners and company promoted oil targets.\nEnsure coordination for timely spare parts orders execution for channel partners.Ensure dealer CSI score targets are met by driving improvement action plans.To provide feedback on competition new service schemes launched to the head of service and the Zonal/ Regional Customer Care Manager.To provide timely and qualitative Product feedback about critical and new defects to HO Product Monitoring Cell.Ensure warranty claims process adherence at the channel partners level.To ensure installation and establishing the entire service infrastructure, systems and processes at new dealerships.Conducting service audits periodically as per the company norms.Ensure Product training of the dealer, workshop manager and service mechanics',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Overall Responsibility of Customer Care processes related activities- Dealer Management, On-field Service Delivery, Spares/Lubes/Warranty Management.\\\\nImplementation of all processes and systems related to the service function at channel partners level.\\\\nEnsuring standardized Service Infrastructure, facilities, quality manpower at channel partners level.To guide and conduct on the job training of the Service Mechanics for technical problem solving and debottlenecking at the dealerships.\\\\nTo attend and resolve the critical customer complaints and measure of customer satisfaction level.\\\\nTo work towards and increase dealer profitability by service schemes like service packages, service coverage improvements, free services, post warranty jobs, annual maintenance contracts.Ensure meeting spare targets of all channel partners and company promoted oil targets.\\\\nEnsure coordination for timely spare parts orders execution for channel partners.Ensure dealer CSI score targets are met by driving improvement action plans.To provide feedback on competition new service schemes launched to the head of service and the Zonal/ Regional Customer Care Manager.To provide timely and qualitative Product feedback about critical and new defects to HO Product Monitoring Cell.Ensure warranty claims process adherence at the channel partners level.To ensure installation and establishing the entire service infrastructure, systems and processes at new dealerships.Conducting service audits periodically as per the company norms.Ensure Product training of the dealer, workshop manager and service mechanics\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nEngineer, Field Service, Engineering, Manufacturing\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Lucknow\", \"title\": \"Deputy Manager - Customer Care\", \"location\": \"Lucknow, Lucknow, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=340\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Deputy Manager - Customer Care\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1396236800\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Lucknow-Deputy-Manager-Customer-Care-Luck/1396236800/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Lucknow, Lucknow, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Lucknow-Deputy-Manager-Customer-Care-Luck/1396236800/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1396236800\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Lucknow, Lucknow, IN','Deputy Manager - Customer Care'),(5405,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_e79d7cd3ace0','Manager - Sales Planning',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai A.O, MUMBAI-KND-AD, IN','MUMBAI-KND-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nDemand Planning, Sales Forecasting, Inventory management, Order and Billing Management, Product Launch readiness, Outlier Trend Identification & Analysis and VIP order management are key roles for Sales planners.\nTo play a key role during new product launch in Competition Mapping to arrive on bottom-up slicers wrt Transmission type, Fuel type, High/Medium/Low, Seater, etc. for an effective 6 monthly forecast to ensure “Right Product at Right Time for the Right Market in order to avoid any potential volume loss & RIGHT Inventory Management & Obsolescence\nRole is extended to derive Dealer Targets based on specific parameters like Past trend, Growth, Management directives, Optimistic projections, booking (ETBR), Market share etc. and to execute & drive month Billing volumes frozen by SOG in co-ordination with CPPC, DCM, RO team & Brand Teams.\nTo derive on “Steady State requirement plan” for products at Trim and aggregate level basis the inputs of Booking, Orders, Dealer Stocks, Bottom-Up Forecast, Dealer Stocks, Billing / Retail movements. Analytical inputs to arrive on “Capacity Enhancements” at Trim / Aggregate levels. Frequency at Monthly level with coordination with Brand & Sales Team.\nPlanning of assigned products basis Sales Operational Group meeting and CPCC.\nSales demand model mix planning and coordination with all related agencies (viz: Manufacturing, Marketing, TPDS, Accounts, IT, Field Sales) to plan in line with the sales requirement.\nSpearheading  PAN India sales billing and retails for high end SUVs.\nAnalysing regional sales performance, identifying lost opportunities and recommending improvement plans at Dealer code / pocket level analysis with Competition Benchmarking.\nSupporting business presentations and dealer communications conducted by departments of M&M.\nPreparing monthly sales summary sheets.\nData Analysis and summary for advanced planning and indicating potential sales spikes to Top management and all Area Offices for the assigned products (example – SCORPIO-N, SCORPIO Classic , Bolero etc.\nPAN India dealers’ performance analysis and bridging the gaps along with sales team for performance achievement.\nTo coordinate with Brand Team, Sales Team & CPPC team wrt Long Term Planning (LTP) @ horizon of N+2 years wrt variant wise | month wise projections\nExecuting long term variant wise product wise advance monthly projection for 6 months for material planning to the manufacturing plant with high level of precision\nUnderstanding of the Market in liaison with the field team and suggest course correction during current / upcoming month production / billing & retail cycle.\nPlanning and Execution of short term 3 Months planning at Variant / Trim Aggregate level every quarter and during festive period.\nManaging monthly allocation of vehicles as per stock availability; ensuring a uniform stock as per monthly average billing and retail.\nCoordination with Marketing team for new product and new variant launches, ensure availability.\nSingle window for field sales for de-bottlenecking and issues resolution (coordination with related departments.\nCoordination & Planning with Outbound Logistic team to ensure dispatch & Load Planning for different modes of transport viz : Rail / Trailers, etc to ensure high customer satisfaction and customer centric approach.\nProcess improvements for overall performance enhancement.\nPerforming system readiness for new launches, coordination with IT Team for automation of reports\nDrive Digitization and Simplicity for effective Execution Excellence',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-A_O-Manager-Sales-Planning-MUMB/1425229700','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=220','2026-10-13T12:15:18.226784+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','a7c4a93c0af6bc3f5086e39