url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Bangalore-Lead-Engineer-VCU-Bang/1434261200/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1434261200\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bangalore, Bangalore-AD, IN','Lead Engineer - VCU'),(5419,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_5b8211ecade9','Lead Engineer - Software and Cyber Security',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore, Bangalore-AD, IN','Bangalore-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPosition Overview\nWe are looking for an Automotive Cyber Security Testing Lead Engineer – Powertrain ECUs to\nlead cybersecurity engineering activities for safety-critical powertrain control systems,\nincluding ICE, Hybrid, and Electric powertrain ECUs. This role is responsible for ensuring that\npowertrain functions are verified and validated to protect against cyber threats while complying\nwith global automotive cybersecurity regulations throughout the product lifecycle.\nKey Responsibilities\n• Lead cybersecurity engineering activities for powertrain ECUs (Engine ECU, VCU, MCU,\nBMS, HCU, OCDC etc.)\n• Act as cybersecurity technical owner for assigned powertrain programs\n• Define and review test requirements to verify Cyber security controls (FUZZ and PEN\ntests)\n• Define and review secure architecture including secure boot, secure communication,\nOTA security, and key management\n• Perform and lead Threat Analysis and Risk Assessment (TARA) as per ISO/SAE 21434\n• Define cybersecurity goals, requirements, and mitigations for powertrain systems\n• Guide secure architecture implementation for all Cyber Security controls like secure\nboot, secure flashing, secure communication etc.\n• Ensure cybersecurity alignment with functional safety (ISO 26262) requirements\n• Support cybersecurity compliance activities for UNECE R155, AIS 189 and R156, AIS\n190.\n• Coordinate cybersecurity activities with system, software, hardware, and validation\nteams\n• Lead cybersecurity reviews with Vehicle teams, suppliers, and internal stakeholders\n• Guide and mentor cybersecurity engineers and review technical deliverables\n• Support vulnerability management, incident response, and post-SOP cybersecurity\nactivities\nPowertrain-Specific Cybersecurity Scope\n• Protection of torque, speed, propulsion, charging and energy management functions\n• Secure diagnostics and calibration access (UDS)\n• Secure production and service software updates\n• Protection against unauthorized software or calibration manipulation\nStandards & Compliance\n• ISO/SAE 21434 – Road Vehicles Cybersecurity Engineering\n• UNECE R155, AIS 189 – Cybersecurity Management System\n• UNECE R156, AIS 190 – Software Update Management System\n• ISO 26262 – Functional Safety (coordination and alignment)',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Bangalore-Lead-Engineer-Software-and-Cyber-Security-Bang/1434261300','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=260','2026-10-13T12:15:28.263895+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','bec850787783431a941b36acb2998278ddad306029b41203d3b6105a2fe9ff75','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Bangalore-Lead-Engineer-Software-and-Cyber-Security-Bang/1434261300','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Lead Engineer - Software and Cyber Security\", \"location\": \"Bangalore, Bangalore-AD, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:19.561219',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:25.776313',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:25.776313',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" conte