d review secure architecture including secure boot, secure communication,\nOTA security, and key management\n• Perform and lead Threat Analysis and Risk Assessment (TARA) as per ISO/SAE 21434\n• Define cybersecurity goals, requirements, and mitigations for powertrain systems\n• Guide secure architecture implementation for all Cyber Security controls like secure\nboot, secure flashing, secure communication etc.\n• Ensure cybersecurity alignment with functional safety (ISO 26262) requirements\n• Support cybersecurity compliance activities for UNECE R155, AIS 189 and R156, AIS\n190.\n• Coordinate cybersecurity activities with system, software, hardware, and validation\nteams\n• Lead cybersecurity reviews with Vehicle teams, suppliers, and internal stakeholders\n• Guide and mentor cybersecurity engineers and review technical deliverables\n• Support vulnerability management, incident response, and post-SOP cybersecurity\nactivities\nPowertrain-Specific Cybersecurity Scope\n• Protection of torque, speed, propulsion, charging and energy management functions\n• Secure diagnostics and calibration access (UDS)\n• Secure production and service software updates\n• Protection against unauthorized software or calibration manipulation\nStandards & Compliance\n• ISO/SAE 21434 – Road Vehicles Cybersecurity Engineering\n• UNECE R155, AIS 189 – Cybersecurity Management System\n• UNECE R156, AIS 190 – Software Update Management System\n• ISO 26262 – Functional Safety (coordination and alignment)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Position Overview\\\\nWe are looking for an Automotive Cyber Security Testing Lead Engineer \\\\u2013 Powertrain ECUs to\\\\nlead cybersecurity engineering activities for safety-critical powertrain control systems,\\\\nincluding ICE, Hybrid, and Electric powertrain ECUs. This role is responsible for ensuring that\\\\npowertrain functions are verified and validated to protect against cyber threats while complying\\\\nwith global automotive cybersecurity regulations throughout the product lifecycle.\\\\nKey Responsibilities\\\\n\\\\u2022 Lead cybersecurity engineering activities for powertrain ECUs (Engine ECU, VCU, MCU,\\\\nBMS, HCU, OCDC etc.)\\\\n\\\\u2022 Act as cybersecurity technical owner for assigned powertrain programs\\\\n\\\\u2022 Define and review test requirements to verify Cyber security controls (FUZZ and PEN\\\\ntests)\\\\n\\\\u2022 Define and review secure architecture including secure boot, secure communication,\\\\nOTA security, and key management\\\\n\\\\u2022 Perform and lead Threat Analysis and Risk Assessment (TARA) as per ISO/SAE 21434\\\\n\\\\u2022 Define cybersecurity goals, requirements, and mitigations for powertrain systems\\\\n\\\\u2022 Guide secure architecture implementation for all Cyber Security controls like secure\\\\nboot, secure flashing, secure communication etc.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Ensure cybersecurity alignment with functional safety (ISO 26262) requirements\\\\n\\\\u2022 Support cybersecurity compliance activities for UNECE R155, AIS 189 and R156, AIS\\\\n190.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Coordinate cybersecurity activities with system, software, hardware, and validation\\\\nteams\\\\n\\\\u2022 Lead cybersecurity reviews with Vehicle teams, suppliers, and internal stakeholders\\\\n\\\\u2022 Guide and mentor cybersecurity engineers and review technical deliverables\\\\n\\\\u2022 Support vulnerability management, incident response, and post-SOP cybersecurity\\\\nactivities\\\\nPowertrain-Specific Cybersecurity Scope\\\\n\\\\u2022 Protection of torque, speed, propulsion, charging and energy management functions\\\\n\\\\u2022 Secure diagnostics and calibration access (UDS)\\\\n\\\\u2022 Secure production and service software updates\\\\n\\\\u2022 Protection against unauthorized software or calibration manipulation\\\\nStandards & Compliance\\\\n\\\\u2022 ISO/SAE 21434 \\\\u2013 Road Vehicles Cybersecurity Engineering\\\\n\\\\u2022 UNECE R155, AIS 189 \\\\u2013 Cybersecurity Management System\\\\n\\\\u2022 UNECE R156, AIS 190 \\\\u2013 Software Update Management System\\\\n\\\\u2022 ISO 26262 \\\\u2013 Functional Safety (coordination and alignment)\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"\\\\u2022 10\\\\u201312+ years of experience in automotive embedded or powertrain systems\\\\n\\\\u2022 3\\\\u20136+ years of hands-on automotive cybersecurity experience\\\\n\\\\u2022 2\\\\u20133+ years of hands-on scripting and automation using languages\\\\n\\\\u2022 Strong understanding of powertrain ECU development lifecycle Technical Skills\\\\n\\\\u2022 Powertrain control systems and real-time embedded software\\\\n\\\\u2022 CAN, CAN-FD, Automotive Ethernet, UDS, and various ECU level interfaces\\\\n\\\\u2022 Cryptography fundamentals, PKI, key management\\\\n\\\\u2022 Secure boot, HSM, secure diagnostics and other Cyber Security Controls\\\\n\\\\u2022 Cybersecurity vulnerability and incident management\\\\n\\\\u2022 OTA/FOTA update security and backend interaction\\\\n\\\\u2022 Threat modelling and vulnerability analysis Soft Skills & Leadership\\\\n\\\\u2022 Strong technical leadership and ownership mindset\\\\n\\\\u2022 Effective communication with cross-functional teams\\\\n\\\\u2022 Risk-based decision making in safety-critical systems\\\\n\\\\u2022 Mentoring and guiding engineers\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"At Mahindra and Mahindra Limited, we believe that diversity drives innovation, and inclusion is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to cultivating a workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.\\\\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to age, caste, race, religion, color, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital or domestic partnership status, pregnancy or childbirth, veteran status, citizenship status, ancestry, financial status, or any other personal characteristic protected by applicable law.\\\\nWe actively encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply and bring their unique perspectives to our teams. We are committed to ensuring an accessible and inclusive experience for all applicants.\\\\nTogether, we rise by embracing differences and building a future that reflects the communities we serve.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nEngineering Manager, Engineer, Software Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bangalore, Bangalore-AD, IN','Lead Engineer - Software and Cyber Security'),(5420,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_dc493a6d7338','Assistant Manager - Production',NULL,NULL,'Haridwar, Haridwar Plant, IN','Haridwar Plant','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nResponsible with understanding of assembly line equipment’s process and parameters like wheel alignment ,Dynamometers, filling equipment’s etc\nResponsible Consistent Quality of rolled out vehicles with understanding of straight pass.\nSystematic Concern Resolution Process with understanding of Poke yoke, HEP,& QC tools\nResponsible for Develop & Deploy Quality Systems in line with focus on BIQ\nIdentifying the need, bridging ownership gaps, documenting & training\nResponsible & Monitoring SPC on line Torque control nut runner (TCNR)\nUnderstanding of torque and pneumatic tools for Calibration eg., TCNR,Battery tools\nResponsible for engineering specification test on Vehicle\nResponsible for check man(Quality Inspector) certification through MSA(measurement system analysis)\nResponsible field failure control through WRAP(warranty reduction audit process)\nUnderstandin