 and manufacturing readiness activities.\\\\nMonitor project schedules and track progress against planned milestones.\\\\nPrepare project MIS reports, presentations and progress dashboards for management review.\\\\nCoordinate with consultants, contractors and internal stakeholders for timely closure of project action items.\\\\nSupport planning and execution of equipment installation, commissioning and SOP readiness activities.\\\\nMaintain project documentation, drawing revisions and planning records.\\\\nAssist in budgeting, project cost tracking and resource planning activities.\\\\nEnsure compliance with safety, quality and project management requirements.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"5 to 8 years of work experience out of which minimum 3 years in Factory Planning of Green Field Project\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automotive OEM\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"Full Time B. Tech in Mechanical Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nManufacturing Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Engineer, Electrical, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Nagpur\", \"title\": \"Dy. Manager - Factory Planning\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=380\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Dy. Manager - Factory Planning\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1434237200\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Factory-Planning-Nagp/1434237200/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Factory-Planning-Nagp/1434237200/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1434237200\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Dy. Manager - Factory Planning'),(5422,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_5942c83ce91f','Sr Engineer - ePT System Engineering',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore, Bangalore-AD, IN','Bangalore-AD','India',NULL,NULL,'Skills- • Hands on experience in communication & diagnostic protocols (CAN, LIN, UDS).',NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n• Responsible for EPT System Integration activities for PV and CV platforms.\n• Coordinating with Internal & External stake holders for E&E interface sign off.\n• To create/write system level test case to verify logical architecture and interfaces against system architecture.\n• Execute System Integration verification test case at vehicle level at Bangalore, Chakan or MSPT.\n• To raise concern tickets and track concerns to closure.\n• To analyse concern logs from internal and external stakeholder for first level analysis and drive technical concern resolution in collaboration with project cross function team.\n• On-site technical support for Lab car set-up and deployment, proto build concern analysis at M&M plant locations, and for real world testing.\n• To execute vehicle level drivability maneuvers related to vehicle dynamics which a vehicle must go through during development.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nSkills- • Hands on experience in communication & diagnostic protocols (CAN, LIN, UDS).\n• Hands on experience in live data capturing & data analysis.\n• Sound knowledge on Battery electric vehicle system, its functions and in-Vehicle Networks.\n• Proficient in problem solving (Root cause analysis, 8D reports, FTA, why why analysis)\n• Sound knowledge on diagnostic tools and CANOe, CAN Analyser & INCA.\n• Sound knowledge on System level DFEMA, automotive product development cycle.\n• Experienced in driving light commercial vehicles for testing on road and testing track for testing purpose.\n• Knowledge of ASPICE process for system verification is an added advantage. • Knowledge of VCU interaction with ESC/ADAS for system verification is an added advantage.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Bangalore-Sr-Engineer-ePT-System-Engineering-Bang/1434261400','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=260','2026-10-13T12:15:31.836792+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','8162ba3931158f0b537bec73ec099b4a1f3884d4a59afd6242140e4a6b52d738','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Bangalore-Sr-Engineer-ePT-System-Engineering-Bang/1434261400','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Sr Engineer - ePT System Engineering\", \"location\": \"Bangalore, Bangalore-AD, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"General Requirements\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:19.965907',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:25.940261',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:25.940261',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platform/bootstrap/3.4.8_NES/css/bootstrap.min.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/bootstrapV3.global.responsive.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/navbar-fixed-top.css\" />\n                \n                <script type=\"text/javascript