tElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'Zaheerabad',1,'2026-10-13T12:15:30.835695+00:00','1434266900',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'As the Manager for Tractor PDI & Cabin Assembly at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will oversee and direct daily operations within the plant, including production, manufacturing, maintenance, engineering support, TPM activities, safety, regulatory compliance, distribution, and warehousing. Reporting to the plant general manager, your primary objective is to ensure cost-effective, timely delivery of high-quality products while maintaining a safe, secure, and sanitary work environment.\nYour critical responsibilities include managing the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of operational methods, equipment, systems, and infrastructure essential to achieving the plant\'s goals. You will lead initiatives to monitor and improve process efficiency and personnel productivity by identifying and removing operational obstacles.\nAdditional duties encompass overseeing recruitment, performance management, and comprehensive training programmes for all personnel involved in plant operations. You will develop production work schedules that meet both internal targets and customer expectations, regularly monitoring progress to ensure alignment with these goals.\nSpecifically, you will:\nDirect all facets of manufacturing operations to achieve operational excellence.\nEnsure compliance with safety regulations and company policies to create a secure workplace.\nImplement effective Total Productive Maintenance (TPM) strategies to maximise equipment availability and reliability.\nCollaborate with engineering teams to support continuous process improvements and technical problem-solving.\nLead cross-functional teams to enhance quality assurance standards and cost optimisation efforts.\nFoster a culture of accountability, collaboration, and innovation within the plant.\nAlign plant activities with Mahindra & Mahindra’s sustainability goals and strategic business objectives.\nManage distribution and warehousing logistics to guarantee efficient supply chain flow.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"As the Manager for Tractor PDI & Cabin Assembly at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will oversee and direct daily operations within the plant, including production, manufacturing, maintenance, engineering support, TPM activities, safety, regulatory compliance, distribution, and warehousing. Reporting to the plant general manager, your primary objective is to ensure cost-effective, timely delivery of high-quality products while maintaining a safe, secure, and sanitary work environment.\\\\nYour critical responsibilities include managing the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of operational methods, equipment, systems, and infrastructure essential to achieving the plant\'s goals. You will lead initiatives to monitor and improve process efficiency and personnel productivity by identifying and removing operational obstacles.\\\\nAdditional duties encompass overseeing recruitment, performance management, and comprehensive training programmes for all personnel involved in plant operations. You will develop production work schedules that meet both internal targets and customer expectations, regularly monitoring progress to ensure alignment with these goals.\\\\nSpecifically, you will:\\\\nDirect all facets of manufacturing operations to achieve operational excellence.\\\\nEnsure compliance with safety regulations and company policies to create a secure workplace.\\\\nImplement effective Total Productive Maintenance (TPM) strategies to maximise equipment availability and reliability.\\\\nCollaborate with engineering teams to support continuous process improvements and technical problem-solving.\\\\nLead cross-functional teams to enhance quality assurance standards and cost optimisation efforts.\\\\nFoster a culture of accountability, collaboration, and innovation within the plant.\\\\nAlign plant activities with Mahindra & Mahindra\\\\u2019s sustainability goals and strategic business objectives.\\\\nManage distribution and warehousing logistics to guarantee efficient supply chain flow.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"Educational qualifications for this leadership position require a\\\\nBachelor of Technology degree\\\\nin a relevant engineering discipline such as Mechanical, Electrical, or Industrial Engineering. Candidates holding a\\\\ndiploma\\\\nwith substantial equivalent experience in manufacturing management may also be considered.\\\\nThe ideal candidate should demonstrate a strong technical foundation complemented by advanced knowledge of manufacturing processes, industrial safety standards, and maintenance practices relevant to the automotive and tractor assembly sectors.\\\\nProfessional development through certifications related to Total Productive Maintenance (TPM), Quality Management (such as Six Sigma or ISO standards), and operations management is highly desirable. Continuous learning and upskilling to keep abreast of evolving industry best practices and technologies will be supported and encouraged.\\\\nAdditionally, strong proficiency in computer-aided manufacturing systems, production planning software, and data analytics tools will be advantageous for effective decision-making and operational oversight.\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"With a substantial background of 25 to 30 years in manufacturing environments, particularly in large-scale production facilities, the candidate is expected to have extensive experience managing complex operations in the automotive, farm equipment, or heavy machinery industries.\\\\nProven expertise in coordinating manufacturing operations, maintenance management, engineering support, and quality assurance is essential. Experience in steering Total Productive Maintenance (TPM) programs, ensuring regulatory compliance, and implementing continuous improvement initiatives is critical for success in this role.\\\\nThe candidate must have a track record of successfully leading diverse teams, fostering professional development, and cultivating a safety-first culture. Demonstrated experience in production planning, scheduling, and supply chain coordination is vital to consistently meet customer and business requirements.\\\\nStrong interpersonal and communication skills to collaborate effectively across departments and with external stakeholders are necessary. Experience working within multinational organizations or global business units, along with exposure to international quality and safety standards, will be viewed favourably.\\\\nFlexibility and adaptability to respond to changing production demands and technological advancements will underpin your effectiveness as a leader within Mahindra & Mahindra\'s Farm Division.\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"Critical experience for this position includes:\\\\nExpertise in\\\\nmaintenance management\\\\nwith a focus on predictive, preventive, and corrective maintenance in a manufacturing context.\\\\nProven leadership in deploying and sustaining\\\\nTotal Productive Maintenance (TPM)\\\\nmethodologies, driving operational efficiency and equipment reliability.\\\\nDeep knowledge of\\\\nregulatory compliance\\\\nstandards particularly involving occupational health and safety, environmental regulations, and industry-specific requirements relevant to tractor assembly.\\\\nStrong command of\\\\nmanufacturing operations management\\\\n, including scheduling, quality assurance, cost control, and continuous improvement strategies.\\\\nCompetence in managing cross-disciplinary teams encompassing engineering support, quality assurance, and production personnel with a focus on performance management and development.\\\\nExperience in operational excellence practices, including Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, and process optimisation techniques.\\\\nAbility to leverage advanced\\\\nequipment management\\\\nsystems and technology to enhance productivity and sustainability.\\\\nSkilled in\\\\ntalent acquisition, training, and development\\\\nensuring alignment of human capital with business goals.\\\\nStrong familiarity with production planning and scheduling software and methodologies to meet stringent delivery timelines while maintaining product quality.\\\\nProven track record of fostering innovation, driving change management, and embedding a continuous learning culture within manufacturing teams.\\\\nCollectively, this critical experience forms the foundation for ensuring the effective operation of the Tractor PDI & Cabin Assembly department while supporting Mahindra & Mahindra\\\\u2019s strategic growth and customer satisfaction aims.\\\", \\\"System Generated Secondary Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nIndustrial Engineer, Engineer, Assembly, Maintenance Engineer, Engineering, Manufacturing, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-FD, IN','Manager - Tractor PDI & Cabin Assembly'),(5427,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_4419c92d9e8d','Mgr - SQA (Electrical Comm) MTWD',NULL,NULL,'Pithampur, Pithampur, IN','Pithampur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n● To coordinate the Quality activities.\n● Understand Customer needs and latent Desires and ensure Deployment in Products\n● Benchmark Quality Parameters and Improve Product Quality of Tools and Dies.\n● Working closely with various stakeholders (Internal & External)\n● In process & Final inspection of the Panels, Dies & Fixtures.\n● Generating Quality indicator dashboard for Senior Management reviews highlighting key quality risks.\n● To carryout Different Audits like  Process Audit & GNODA-C / GNOFA-C Audit.\n● To carry MSA & SPC study.\n● To maintain the Measuring Instruments, Accessories, Material handling equipment in good working condition.\n● To maintain the safe working condition & good house keeping in the Department',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Pithampur-Mgr-SQA-%28Electrical-Comm%29-MTWD-Pith/1434219700','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=280','2026-10-13T12:15:30.961108+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','9f58047b98e7f04103c98f26dd075bc5d311fe9a5f19ec43e8f5749dd1f4aa71','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Pithampur-Mgr-SQA-%28Electrical-Comm%29-MTWD-Pith/1434219700','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Mgr - SQA (Electrical Comm) MTWD\", \"location\": \"Pithampur, Pithampur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:22.566493',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:27.354185',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:27.354185',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platform/bootstrap/3.4.8_NES/css/bootstrap.min.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/