mmitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nElectronics Engineer, Engineering Manager, Electrical Engineering, Electrical, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Lead Engineer-Electrical & Electronics'),(5448,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_12e6b70a46e2','Lead Engineer-CAE',NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Chennai-MRV-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\n(1) Should have good knowledge of Vehicle systems\n(2) Should have good fundamentals - Strength of materials, Applied mechanics and Finite element methods\n(3) Should be able to do finite element modelling of Vehicle components and Systems.\n(4) Should be able to assign thickness and material properties to components\n(5) Should be able to build finite element assemblies for Vehicle structure. Should have good understanding of different types of connections like spot and seam welding.\"\n(6) Should be able to apply loads and Boundary conditions required for linear and nonlinear Static analysis.\n(7) Should be able to carry out Modal, frequency response and transient analysis for vehicle components and systems.\"\n(8)Should be able to do Fatigue life estimation for Vehicle structure, Spot and seam welds.\n(9) Ability to post process results, make reports and present results to design team.\n(10) Should be able to recommend design modifications to meet acceptance criteria based on analysis results, manufacturing and packaging constraints.\n(11) Should have knowledge of different tests for Vehicle systems and test instrumentations.\n(12) Should be able to correlate CAE results with physical test results.\nExperience\n7 to 10 Years\nIndustry Preferred\nQualifications\nM.Tech/M.E - Machine Design (Preferred from IIT or other good institute)\nB.E Mechanical (Min First class)\nGeneral Requirements\nOur commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\nAt Mahindra and Mahindra Limited, we believe that diversity drives innovation, and inclusion is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to cultivating a workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to age, caste, race, religion, color, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital or domestic partnership status, pregnancy or childbirth, veteran status, citizenship status, ancestry, financial status, or any other personal characteristic protected by applicable law.\nWe actively encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply and bring their unique perspectives to our teams. We are committed to ensuring an accessible and inclusive experience for all applicants.\nTogether, we rise by embracing differences and building a future that reflects the communities we serve.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Lead-Engineer-CAE-Chen/1433316900','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=360','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','b10126f2cb3cd26678c456f15f931d280b5122607ffdf536966b97aff2ab5bf6','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Lead-Engineer-CAE-Chen/1433316900','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Lead Engineer-CAE\", \"location\": \"Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:32.423715',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:32.307211',NULL,NULL,'20