to ensure processes are capable of consistently meeting defined product quality requirements.\\\\nNew Product Launch Quality\\\\nEnsure quality readiness for product launch, including First Time Right (FTR) declaration and closure of critical quality issues before market introduction.\\\\nPost-Launch Quality & Customer Feedback\\\\nMonitor field quality and customer feedback after launch, identify improvement opportunities and drive corrective actions with relevant stakeholders.\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"Diploma/BE / Btech\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Apply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Chennai\", \"title\": \"Dy Manager - Quality Planning Chennai\", \"location\": \"Chennai, Chennai-MRV-FD, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=500\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Dy Manager - Quality Planning Chennai\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1432850300\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Chennai-Dy-Manager-Quality-Planning-Chennai-Chen/1432850300/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Chennai, Chennai-MRV-FD, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Dy-Manager-Quality-Planning-Chennai-Chen/1432850300/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1432850300\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-FD, IN','Dy Manager - Quality Planning Chennai'),(5459,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_ebe8e70fa500','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for Design Coordination (Electrical)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nLead electrical design coordination, engineering integration and technical governance activities for the Greenfield Automotive Manufacturing Facility and ensure successful project execution, commissioning readiness, operational efficiency and future infrastructure scalability.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\nLead electrical design coordination activities across all Greenfield project packages to ensure alignment with project timelines, operational requirements and SOP readiness.\nReview electrical layouts, load calculations, single line diagrams (SLDs), cable schedules, equipment specifications and engineering deliverables to ensure compliance with design standards and project requirements.\nCoordinate with Civil, Mechanical, Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Industrial Engineering and external consultants to ensure seamless integration of electrical infrastructure and utilities.\nManage engineering consultants, design service providers and technical agencies to achieve project objectives related to quality, cost, delivery and compliance.\nDrive design standardization, value engineering and optimization initiatives to enhance system reliability, maintainability, energy efficiency and lifecycle cost effectiveness.\nIdentify and resolve design interfaces, technical conflicts and engineering issues to support smooth project execution and timely completion of project milestones.\nEnsure timely release, control and revision management of approved drawings, specifications and engineering documents to support procurement, construction and commissioning activities.\nSupport utility integration, equipment installation, testing, commissioning and operational readiness activities to ensure successful Start of Production (SOP).\nMonitor engineering changes, maintain design documentation and ensure compliance with applicable codes, standards, statutory regulations and company engineering practices.\nSupport future facility expansion, utility augmentation, modernization and infrastructure optimization projects while promoting continuous improvement and technical excellence.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E. / B.Tech Electrical Engineering\nJob Segment:\nElectrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineer, Electrical, Industrial Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infrastructure-for-Design-Coordination-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422330200','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=420','2026-10-13T12:15:57.069427+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','aa75946f15003677adef12422be7bce945c3e312521e890ab4fc0701e42c7c76','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infrastructure-for-Design-Coordination-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422330200','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for Design Coordination (Electrical)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:36.791076',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:35.953974',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:35.953974',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platfo