anical, Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Industrial Engineering and external consultants to ensure seamless integration of electrical infrastructure and utilities.\\\\nManage engineering consultants, design service providers and technical agencies to achieve project objectives related to quality, cost, delivery and compliance.\\\\nDrive design standardization, value engineering and optimization initiatives to enhance system reliability, maintainability, energy efficiency and lifecycle cost effectiveness.\\\\nIdentify and resolve design interfaces, technical conflicts and engineering issues to support smooth project execution and timely completion of project milestones.\\\\nEnsure timely release, control and revision management of approved drawings, specifications and engineering documents to support procurement, construction and commissioning activities.\\\\nSupport utility integration, equipment installation, testing, commissioning and operational readiness activities to ensure successful Start of Production (SOP).\\\\nMonitor engineering changes, maintain design documentation and ensure compliance with applicable codes, standards, statutory regulations and company engineering practices.\\\\nSupport future facility expansion, utility augmentation, modernization and infrastructure optimization projects while promoting continuous improvement and technical excellence.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"10-15 Years in relevent field\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automotive OEM / Auto Component / Manufacturing / EPC Projects\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E. / B.Tech Electrical Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nElectrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineer, Electrical, Industrial Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for Design Coordination (Electrical)'),(5460,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_e2ad7b367a62','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for TCF & Aggregates Shop (Mechanical)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nGreenfield Project Execution, Industrial Utility Systems, Compressed Air Systems, Cooling Water Systems, Utility Piping Networks, Material Handling Utilities, TPM & Reliability Engineering, Project Management, Contractor & Vendor Management, Energy Management, Utility Commissioning, Statutory Compliance, Operational Readiness & SOP Support, Infrastructure Expansion Planning.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\nLead planning, execution and commissioning of mechanical utilities and infrastructure for TCF & Aggregates Shop during the Greenfield project phase, ensuring alignment with project timelines, budget targets and Start of Production (SOP) requirements.\nDrive development and installation of compressed air systems, cooling water systems, utility piping networks, ventilation systems, material handling utilities, HVAC Systems  and other manufacturing support infrastructure required for TCF and Aggregates operations.\nReview utility layouts, equipment utility requirements, engineering drawings and technical specifications to ensure compliance with project requirements, operational needs and future capacity expansion plans.\nCoordinate with Production, Quality, Industrial Engineering, Civil, Electrical and Manufacturing Engineering teams to ensure utility readiness for assembly lines, machining equipment, test facilities, conveyors and production ramp-up activities.\nManage consultants, contractors, vendors and service providers to achieve project objectives related to safety, quality, cost and delivery while ensuring compliance with approved engineering standards and execution schedules.\nMonitor project progress, installation quality, budget utilization and execution risks, and drive corrective actions to ensure timely completion of project milestones and operational readiness.\nEstablish preventive maintenance, TPM and reliability improvement systems for utility assets to ensure uninterrupted availability, improved equipment uptime and optimized lifecycle performance post SOP.\nMonitor utility consumption, equipment performance and asset reliability, and drive energy conservation, cost optimization and continuous improvement initiatives across TCF & Aggregates facilities.\nEnsure compliance with statutory requirements, safety standards, environmental regulations and utility-related audits throughout project and operational phases.\nSupport capacity enhancement, utility augmentation, technology upgradation, infrastructure modernization and future expansion projects in line with business growth requirements.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E./B.Tech Mechanical Engineering\nJob Segment:\nIndustrial Engineer, Manufacturing Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Engineer, Machinist, Engineering, Manufacturing\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infrastructure-for-TCF-&-Aggregates-Shop-%28Mechanical%29-Nagp/1422330400','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=400','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','d8c8f9be4f38dc853c2f3024738907fa2ff3081dbec446b74f65c0c272872318','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infrastructure-for-TCF-&-Aggregates-Shop-%28Mechanical%29-Nagp/1422330400','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for TCF & Aggregates Shop (Mechanical)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\"