on and commissioning of HT/LT systems, MCCs, PCCs, transformers and power distribution networks.\nSupport automation, robotics, welding lines and conveyor utility integration requirements.\nEstablish maintenance, reliability and TPM systems post SOP.\nMonitor power consumption, asset performance and energy efficiency initiatives.\nEnsure compliance with statutory requirements, electrical safety standards and environmental regulations.\nSupport future capacity expansion and infrastructure enhancement projects.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Purpose of the role:\\\\nLead planning, execution, commissioning and operational readiness of Electrical Infrastructure, Power Distribution Systems and Utilities for Press Shop & Body Shop during Greenfield project phase and ensure reliable electrical operations post SOP.\\\\nRoles & Responsibilities:\\\\nLead planning, execution and commissioning of Electrical Infrastructure and Utilities for Press Shop & Body Shop.\\\\nEnsure electrical readiness for equipment installation, trials, commissioning and SOP.\\\\nCoordinate with Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Quality, Civil and Mechanical teams.\\\\nManage contractors, consultants and vendors to achieve quality, cost, delivery and safety targets.\\\\nDrive installation and commissioning of HT/LT systems, MCCs, PCCs, transformers and power distribution networks.\\\\nSupport automation, robotics, welding lines and conveyor utility integration requirements.\\\\nEstablish maintenance, reliability and TPM systems post SOP.\\\\nMonitor power consumption, asset performance and energy efficiency initiatives.\\\\nEnsure compliance with statutory requirements, electrical safety standards and environmental regulations.\\\\nSupport future capacity expansion and infrastructure enhancement projects.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"10-15 Years in relevant field\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automotive OEM / Auto Component / Manufacturing / EPC Projects\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E. / B.Tech Electrical Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nElectrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineer, Welding, Electrical, Engineering, Automotive, Manufacturing\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for Press & Body Shops (Electrical)'),(5463,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_8c97d888e25a','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Press Shop (Electrical)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nSupport planning, execution, commissioning, operation and maintenance of electrical infrastructure and utilities for Press Shop to ensure project readiness during Greenfield development and reliable power availability, safety, environmental compliance and operational excellence post SOP.\nRoles and responsibilities:\nGreenfield Project Phase\nSupport execution and monitoring of electrical infrastructure activities for Press Shop, including HT/LT distribution systems, substations, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems, MCCs, PCCs, cable routing networks and electrical utility systems as per project schedules, quality standards and safety requirements.\nWork closely with Electrical, Mechanical, Production, Process Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering and contractor teams to ensure timely completion of project activities and closure of commissioning punch points.\nEnsure compliance with approved drawings, technical specifications, electrical standards, statutory requirements, environmental norms and safety regulations during project execution and commissioning activities.\nOperations & Facility Management Phase\nSupport preventive and breakdown maintenance of substations, transformers, DG sets, MCCs, PCCs, UPS systems, lighting systems and power distribution networks to ensure uninterrupted Paint Shop operations.\nMonitor power consumption, equipment health, electrical system performance and utility reliability, and support implementation of energy management, reliability improvement and cost optimization initiatives.\nCoordinate contractor and vendor activities, verify work completion and ensure adherence to quality, safety and delivery requirements for maintenance and project works.\nMaintain maintenance records, electrical asset history, statutory inspection records and MIS reports, while supporting expansion projects, infrastructure upgrades, utility enhancements and electrical safety compliance activities.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E./B.Tech Electrical Engineering\nJob Segment:\nManufacturing Engineer, Electrical Engineering, Process Engineer, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Press-Shop-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422513300','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=400','2026-10-13T12:16:00.386225+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','3a2d88cf3fae6b952203912e12849c6135e76115e204d106fbacc8875e01b3c9','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Press-Shop-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422513300','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Press Shop (Electrical)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:37.