er availability, safety, environmental compliance and operational excellence post SOP.\\\\nRoles and responsibilities:\\\\nGreenfield Project Phase\\\\nSupport execution and monitoring of electrical infrastructure activities for Press Shop, including HT/LT distribution systems, substations, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems, MCCs, PCCs, cable routing networks and electrical utility systems as per project schedules, quality standards and safety requirements.\\\\nWork closely with Electrical, Mechanical, Production, Process Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering and contractor teams to ensure timely completion of project activities and closure of commissioning punch points.\\\\nEnsure compliance with approved drawings, technical specifications, electrical standards, statutory requirements, environmental norms and safety regulations during project execution and commissioning activities.\\\\nOperations & Facility Management Phase\\\\nSupport preventive and breakdown maintenance of substations, transformers, DG sets, MCCs, PCCs, UPS systems, lighting systems and power distribution networks to ensure uninterrupted Paint Shop operations.\\\\nMonitor power consumption, equipment health, electrical system performance and utility reliability, and support implementation of energy management, reliability improvement and cost optimization initiatives.\\\\nCoordinate contractor and vendor activities, verify work completion and ensure adherence to quality, safety and delivery requirements for maintenance and project works.\\\\nMaintain maintenance records, electrical asset history, statutory inspection records and MIS reports, while supporting expansion projects, infrastructure upgrades, utility enhancements and electrical safety compliance activities.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"5+ years in electrical utilities, infrastructure or plant engineering with exposure to Greenfield automotive projects. Press Shop projects, HT/LT power distribution, PCC/MCC, press line power systems, substations\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automobile, Auto Components, Heavy Engineering, Industrial Manufacturing\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E./B.Tech Electrical Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nManufacturing Engineer, Electrical Engineering, Process Engineer, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Press Shop (Electrical)'),(5464,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_82e1f01e9b42','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Body Shop (Civil)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nSupport planning, execution, commissioning, operation, and maintenance of buildings, utilities, and related infrastructure for the Body Shop during Greenfield project implementation and plant operations, ensuring timely project delivery, operational readiness, asset reliability, safety, quality, and regulatory compliance.\nRoles and responsibilities:\nSupport execution of civil, building, utility, and infrastructure projects for Body Shop facilities in line with approved specifications, schedules, and budgets.\nMonitor construction activities, contractor performance, and work quality to ensure compliance with engineering and safety standards.\nCoordinate with project, production, utility, EHS, and vendor teams for timely completion of infrastructure and utility works.\nSupport installation readiness, equipment foundation works, and commissioning activities for Body Shop operations.\nMonitor operation and maintenance of buildings, roads, drainage systems, utility infrastructure, and other civil assets.\nEnsure availability, reliability, and upkeep of utility-related infrastructure supporting Body Shop production requirements.\nConduct routine inspections and identify corrective actions to maintain asset health, safety, and operational efficiency.\nVerify contractor measurements, work completion status, and documentation for project execution and maintenance activities.\nEnsure adherence to statutory requirements, environmental regulations, and company standards related to infrastructure facilities.\nMaintain engineering drawings, asset records, maintenance history, and project documentation.\nSupport cost optimization, energy-saving, and continuous improvement initiatives related to infrastructure and utility systems.\nAssist in troubleshooting infrastructure-related issues to minimize operational disruptions and improve facility performance.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E./B.Tech Civil Engineering\nJob Segment:\nCivil Engineer, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Body-Shop-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422511900','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=420','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','b27bce961ae64f6daa49a6cc34a73a582c622ab4c0fe2b114b63901116352430','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Body-Shop-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422511900','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Body Shop (Civil)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:39.538453',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:36.423740',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\