initiatives, and infrastructure optimization projects.\nAssist in troubleshooting infrastructure and utility-related issues to minimize operational disruptions.\nMaintain asset records, engineering documents, maintenance history, and compliance documentation.','\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Purpose of the role:\\\", \\\"Purpose of the role\\\": \\\"To Support the planning, execution, commissioning, operation, and maintenance of common infrastructure facilities across the manufacturing plant to ensure reliable utility services, operational readiness, asset reliability, safety, regulatory compliance, and sustainable plant operations throughout the facility lifecycle\\\\nRoles and responsibilities:\\\", \\\"Roles and responsibilities\\\": \\\"Support execution and monitoring of common infrastructure projects, including administrative buildings, roads, drainage systems, parking facilities, boundary walls, utility corridors, and external developments.\\\\nCoordinate installation, commissioning, and handover of common utility infrastructure such as water systems, compressed air distribution, fire protection systems, electrical networks, and sewage treatment facilities.\\\\nMonitor operation and maintenance of common infrastructure assets to ensure high availability, reliability, and performance.\\\\nConduct routine inspections and identify infrastructure deficiencies, safety risks, and maintenance requirements.\\\\nCoordinate with project teams, utility providers, contractors, vendors, consultants, and internal stakeholders for timely completion of infrastructure activities.\\\\nEnsure compliance with engineering specifications, statutory requirements, environmental regulations, and safety standards.\\\\nSupport preventive and corrective maintenance activities for common buildings and infrastructure facilities.\\\\nMonitor contractor performance, site progress, work quality, and adherence to approved schedules and budgets.\\\\nVerify measurements, contractor bills, project documentation, drawings, and maintenance records.\\\\nSupport utility consumption monitoring, energy conservation initiatives, and infrastructure optimization projects.\\\\nAssist in troubleshooting infrastructure and utility-related issues to minimize operational disruptions.\\\\nMaintain asset records, engineering documents, maintenance history, and compliance documentation.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"5+ years in experience in industrial infrastructure, facility management, utilities, civil projects, or manufacturing plant infrastructure.\\\\nExperience in Greenfield automotive, engineering, manufacturing, steel, cement, FMCG, or large industrial projects preferred.\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automobile OEMs, Industrial Construction, EPC Companies, Heavy Engineering and Manufacturing Industries\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"BE in Mechanical\\\\u00a0Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nMechanical Engineer, Wastewater, Water Treatment, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Nagpur\", \"title\": \"Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Mechanical)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=540\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Mechanical)\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1422515900\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Common-Infra-%28Mechanical%29-Nagp/1422515900/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Common-Infra-%28Mechanical%29-Nagp/1422515900/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1422515900\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Mechanical)'),(5467,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_3b84c55c1e27','Deputy Manager - Utilities',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN','Nagpur Plant','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nAs the Deputy Manager of Central Maintenance at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will play a pivotal role in ensuring operational excellence and reliability of utility systems across our manufacturing facilities. Your core responsibilities will encompass:\nOverseeing strict adherence to company policies, industry best practices, and standards to maintain regulatory compliance; actively liaising with relevant agencies and governing bodies to ensure all facility operations meet or exceed legal requirements.\nManaging the breakdown and preventive maintenance of critical utility equipment including Diesel Generator (DG) sets, compressors, air dryers, hot water generators, HVAC systems, air handling units (AHUs), and electrical panels (HT and LT).\nConducting comprehensive analysis of equipment failures and preventive maintenance schedules to optimize uptime and equipment lifespan.\nPlanning, monitoring, and controlling daily maintenance activities while maintaining accurate records of spares consumption to ensure readiness and minimize downtime.\nApplying expertise in energy-efficient equipment to direct project planning and execution aimed at improving sustainability, reducing operational costs, and enhancing facility performance.\nOverseeing water treatment operations, encompassing Effluent Treatment Plants (ETP), Sewage Treatment Plants (STP), and Reverse Osmosis (RO) plants, aligning with strict environmental and legal compliance standards.\nCoordinating installation and commissioning of new machinery, ensuring seamless integration with existing infrastructure and adherence to operational standards.\nEstimating costs for spare parts and critical components by employing Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA) to prioritize maintenance needs strategically.\nLeading initiatives for resource conservation and budget revenue control, fostering a culture of operational efficiency.\nDriving continuous improvement programs such as Kaizen, 5S, Quality Control (QC) stories, and Cross-Functional Teams (CFTs) to cultivate operational excellence and teamwork across departments.\nEnsuring compliance with international standards including ISO 14000 (Environmental Management), OHSAS 18000 (Occupational Health and Safety), TSI 6949, and ISO 27001 (Information Security) through effective calibration, creation of robust Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and work instructions.\nYour role demands a proactive approach to problem solving, leadership in maintenance planning, and fostering collaboration to uphold the highest equipment reliability and workplace safety standards.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Deputy-Manager-Utilities-Nagp/1390095500','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=420','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','e80fb406dd1c1eeebaaf4f395b44813d5b326f93e5d6c76b734a5e7aea1b99e4','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Deputy-Manager-Utilities-Nagp/1390095500','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Deputy Manager - Utilities\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Education Qualification\", \"General Experience\", \"Critical Experience\", \"System Generated Secondary Skills\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:39.931706',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:36.078055',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.26