\"keywords\" content=\"adventure aerospace aftermarket automotive boats brand brands business businesses careers change channels clean companies company connect contact contacts counts cultural culture defence directors equipment estate facebook farm finance financial followers formula global good googleapis graph group growth history http https india industry information innovation instagram investors jobs know leadership learn listed mahindra mahindrarise marazzo marketplace media mobility motor news october outreach overview people performance plant presence press previous programmes purpose read real releases reports resources responsibility results rise room services social sport statistics steel stories sustainability tech technology trails twitter users valley video views visit watch wheelers work world youtube\" />\n\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n                <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/fed09ea3-5cdb-4e2b-a362-c.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/customHeader.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/sitebuilderframework.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/BS3ColumnizedSearch.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/fontawesome4.7/css/font-awesome-4.7.0.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n<style>\nbody > .modal-backdrop {\n    display: none !important;\n}\n.menu.desktop .nav > li .dropdown-menu li a{ color : white !important}\n#header .links a{ color: white !important;}\n.dropdown-menu.company-dropdown.headerdropdown.backgroundcolordc8b140b5a119dc3 .menu{ color : black !important}\n.custom-header-menu .nav.nav-pills{ width: 807px !important; }\n.custom-header-signinLanguage .inner.limitwidth{ max-width: 1200px; }\n.customPlugin{ margin-bottom: 0 !important; }\n\n</style>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\"></script></body>\n\n        \n        <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/9349339a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur',1,'2026-10-13T12:16:01.744360+00:00','1390095500',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'As the Deputy Manager of Central Maintenance at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will play a pivotal role in ensuring operational excellence and reliability of utility systems across our manufacturing facilities. Your core responsibilities will encompass:\nOverseeing strict adherence to company policies, industry best practices, and standards to maintain regulatory compliance; actively liaising with relevant agencies and governing bodies to ensure all facility operations meet or exceed legal requirements.\nManaging the breakdown and preventive maintenance of critical utility equipment including Diesel Generator (DG) sets, compressors, air dryers, hot water generators, HVAC systems, air handling units (AHUs), and electrical panels (HT and LT).\nConducting comprehensive analysis of equipment failures and preventive maintenance schedules to optimize uptime and equipment lifespan.\nPlanning, monitoring, and controlling daily maintenance activities while maintaining accurate records of spares consumption to ensure readiness and minimize downtime.\nApplying expertise in energy-efficient equipment to direct project planning and execution aimed at improving sustainability, reducing operational costs, and enhancing facility performance.\nOverseeing water treatment operations, encompassing Effluent Treatment Plants (ETP), Sewage Treatment Plants (STP), and Reverse Osmosis (RO) plants, aligning with strict environmental and legal compliance standards.\nCoordinating installation and commissioning of new machinery, ensuring seamless integration with existing infrastructure and adherence to operational standards.\nEstimating costs for spare parts and critical components by employing Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA) to prioritize maintenance needs strategically.\nLeading initiatives for resource conservation and budget revenue control, fostering a culture of operational efficiency.\nDriving continuous improvement programs such as Kaizen, 5S, Quality Control (QC) stories, and Cross-Functional Teams (CFTs) to cultivate operational excellence and teamwork across departments.\nEnsuring compliance with international standards including ISO 14000 (Environmental Management), OHSAS 18000 (Occupational Health and Safety), TSI 6949, and ISO 27001 (Information Security) through effective calibration, creation of robust Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and work instructions.\nYour role demands a proactive approach to problem solving, leadership in maintenance planning, and fostering collaboration to uphold the highest equipment reliability and workplace safety standards.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"As the Deputy Manager of Central Maintenance at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will play a pivotal role in ensuring operational excellence and reliability of utility systems across our manufacturing facilities. Your core responsibilities will encompass:\\\\nOverseeing strict adherence to company policies, industry best practices, and standards to maintain regulatory compliance; actively liaising with relevant agencies and governing bodies to ensure all facility operations meet or exceed legal requirements.\\\\nManaging the breakdown and preventive maintenance of critical utility equipment including Diesel Generator (DG) sets, compressors, air dryers, hot water generators, HVAC systems, air handling units (AHUs), and electrical panels (HT and LT).\\\\nConducting comprehensive analysis of equipment failures and preventive maintenance schedules to optimize uptime and equipment lifespan.\\\\nPlanning, monitoring, and controlling daily maintenance activities while maintaining accurate records of spares consumption to ensure readiness and minimize downtime.\\\\nApplying expertise in energy-efficient equipment to direct project planning and execution aimed at improving sustainability, reducing operational costs, and enhancing facility performance.\\\\nOverseeing water treatment operations, encompassing Effluent Treatment Plants (ETP), Sewage Treatment Plants (STP), and Reverse Osmosis (RO) plants, aligning with strict environmental and legal compliance standards.\\\\nCoordinating installation and commissioning of new machinery, ensuring seamless integration with existing infrastructure and adherence to operational standards.\\\\nEstimating costs for spare parts and critical components by employing Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA) to prioritize maintenance needs strategically.\\\\nLeading initiatives for resource conservation and budget revenue control, fostering a culture of operational efficiency.\\\\nDriving continuous improvement programs such as Kaizen, 5S, Quality Control (QC) stories, and Cross-Functional Teams (CFTs) to cultivate operational excellence and teamwork across departments.\\\\nEnsuring compliance with international standards including ISO 14000 (Environmental Management), OHSAS 18000 (Occupational Health and Safety), TSI 6949, and ISO 27001 (Information Security) through effective calibration, creation of robust Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and work instructions.\\\\nYour role demands a proactive approach to problem solving, leadership in maintenance planning, and fostering collaboration to uphold the highest equipment reliability and workplace safety standards.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"We require candidates with strong technical foundations, specifically holding a Bachelor of Technology (B.Tech) degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or equivalent disciplines.\\\\nThe successful candidate should demonstrate comprehensive academic knowledge relevant to industrial maintenance, utilities management, and engineering fundamentals to effectively manage complex mechanical and electrical systems.\\\\nAdditional certifications or training related to project management, quality management systems (such as ISO standards), energy management, or health and safety regulations will be highly advantageous.\\\\nContinuous learning and professional development aligned with evolving industry standards and technological advancements are encouraged to support career growth and operational excellence.\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"Candidates should bring between 5 to 8 years of solid experience in maintenance management within manufacturing or related heavy industry environments.\\\\nExperience must include hands-on involvement in equipment breakdown analysis, preventive and predictive maintenance strategies, and maintenance planning for utilities encompassing mechanical and electrical systems.\\\\nExposure to managing water treatment plants and utilities complying with environmental legislation is essential.\\\\nPrior engagement in resource conservation initiatives, spares inventory management, and budgetary control within maintenance operations will distinguish applicants.\\\\nExperience working with international standards such as ISO 14000, OHSAS 18000, and ISO 27001, and familiarity with continuous improvement initiatives (Kaizen, 5S) is highly desirable.\\\\nA proven track record in coordinating multi-disciplinary teams and cross-functional maintenance activities under tight business timelines will be crucial.\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"Critical experience for this role includes demonstrated expertise in overseeing complex utility systems and maintenance operations within a manufacturing context.\\\\nProficiency in handling breakdowns and routine maintenance of critical equipment such as DG sets, compressors, air dryers, HVAC, and electrical panels is mandatory.\\\\nStrong capabilities in project planning and execution, especially relating to installation and commissioning of machinery, energy efficiency initiatives, and resource conservation programs are required.\\\\nExperience with Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA) methodology for critical spare parts planning and risk mitigation is essential for success.\\\\nHands-on knowledge of regulatory compliance for water treatment plants such as Effluent Treatment Plants (ETP), Sewage Treatment Plants (STP), and Reverse Osmosis (RO) installations is necessary to maintain environmental governance.\\\\nFamiliarity with implementing and maintaining standards such as ISO 14000, OHSAS 18000, TSI 6949, and ISO 27001, including calibration and development of operational procedures, is critical.\\\\nDemonstrated leadership in continuous improvement and collaborative problem-solving frameworks such as Kaizen, 5S, Quality Circles, and cross-functional teams will enable you to contribute in driving operational excellence and sustainability.\\\\nThe role requires not only technical acumen but also commitment to organizational values and the ability to influence multiple stakeholders towards common goals.\\\", \\\"System Generated Secondary Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nWastewater, Water Treatment, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineer, Electrical, Engineering\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Nagpur\", \"title\": \"Deputy Manager - Utilities\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=520\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Deputy Manager - Utilities\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1390095500\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Nagpur-Deputy-Manager-Utilities-Nagp/1390095500/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Deputy-Manager-Utilities-Nagp/1390095500/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1390095500\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN','Deputy Manager - Utilities'),(5468,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_9cac19c17117','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Body Shop (Electrical)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nTo support planning, execution, commissioning, operation and maintenance of electrical infrastructure and utilities for Body Shop to ensure project readiness during Greenfield development and reliable power availability, safety and operational excellence post SOP.\nRoles and responsibilities:\nGreenfield Project Phase\nSupport execution and monitoring of electrical infrastructure activities for Body Shop, including HT/LT distribution systems, substations, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems, MCCs, PCCs, cable routing and utility power distribution networks as per project schedules and quality requirements.\nCoordinate installation, testing and commissioning of electrical systems and utility infrastructure to ensure readiness for robotic welding lines, conveyors, fixtures, automation systems, equipment installation, trials and Start of Production (SOP).\nWork closely with Electrical, Mechanical, Production, Manufacturing Engineering and contractor teams to ensure timely completion of project activities, commissioning support and closure of punch points.\nEnsure compliance with approved drawings, technical specifications, electrical standards, statutory requirements and safety regulations during project execution and commissioning activities.\nOperations & Facility Management Phase\nSupport preventive and breakdown maintenance of substations, transformers, DG sets, MCCs, PCCs, UPS systems, welding power systems, lighting systems and electrical distribution networks to ensure uninterrupted Body Shop operations.\nMonitor power consumption, equipment health, electrical system performance and utility reliability, and support implementation of energy management and continuous improvement initiatives.\nCoordinate contractor activities, verify work completion and ensure adherence to quality, safety and delivery requirements for maintenance and project works.\nMaintain maintenance records, electrical asset history, statutory inspection records and MIS reports, while supporting expansion projects, infrastructure upgrades, automation enhancements and electrical safety compliance activities.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E./B.Tech Electrical Engineering\nJob Segment:\nElectrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineer, Electrical, Welding, Engineering, Manufacturing, Automotive\nApply Now\nS