lity.\\\\nBuild up the station/cell/line in PS by adding all relevant resources.\\\\nCheck for Gun reachability, apply all kinematics to relevant tools and create robot path with zero collision with basic tools.\\\\nGenerate Basic path (welding, tip dressing, etc) and zoning conditions to avoid any collision.\\\\nCollaborate and Coordinate with Line builders to get the line simulation done and optimize the robot paths, robot zoning and again give feedback for any improvement required in design.\\\\nHands on experience of virtual controller such as- ABB / Fanuc / KUKA etc, generate the OLP with the cycle time accuracy of 99%.\\\\nFind out root causes to achieve cycle time targets if not achieved.\\\\nEnsure Zero error / collision / losses through continuous involvement with execution team.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"Bachelors of Technology in Mechanical / Automobile\\\\nDiploma in Engineering in Mechanical / Automobile\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"2 to 8 years of relevant experience in BIW Manufacturing, Production, Assembly.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nProcess Engineer, Engineering Manager, Welding, Engineer, Engineering, Manufacturing, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chakan, Chakan, IN','Deputy Manager - Process Engineering'),(5470,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_428f641bd5f2','Deputy Manager-R&D',NULL,NULL,'Mohali, R&D Mohali, IN','R&D Mohali','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nCalibration & Development:\n- Lead Mechanical and CRS FIE system calibration across platforms.\n- Drive combustion development and optimize engine performance.\n- Execute engine calibration to meet performance and emission targets for TREM IIIAA, TREM-4 and TREM-5\n- Conduct vehicle calibration to meet drivability and noise targets.\n- Formulate and execute Design of Experiments (DoE) for calibration optimization.\nEmission & Certification:\n- Select and validate engine emission hardware including FIE and EATS systems.\n- Ensure compliance with DSM, NCD, PCD requirements forTREM 3A, TREM 3AA and TREM-4 norms.\n- Coordinate with emission regulation nodal agencies to ensure legal compliance and certification.\nTools & Data Analysis:\n- Utilize advanced tools such as ETAS INCA, AVL Concerto, CAMEO for calibration and data evaluation.\n- Benchmark competitor systems and integrate learnings into development.\nProject Execution & Coordination:\n- Oversee engine build quality and timelines across project stages.\n- Coordinate with manufacturing plant teams for build execution.\n- Liaise with component development teams to ensure timely part availability.\n- Collaborate with testing teams for calibration and functional test execution.\n- Lead troubleshooting of vehicle issues from field/customer feedback.\nTeam Leadership & Collaboration:\n- Mentor junior engineers and foster a culture of technical excellence.\n- Collaborate with cross-functional teams including hardware, software, testing, and regulatory affairs.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mohali-Deputy-Manager-R&D-R&D/1432384200','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=440','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','0452221fdef74030f7437efb42fc1762eaa8483ce5252cec83383eeb4f10c697','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mohali-Deputy-Manager-R&D-R&D/1432384200','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Deputy Manager-R&D\", \"location\": \"Mohali, R&D Mohali, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Education Qualification\", \"General Experience\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-12 01:08:42.004266',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:37.0