CD, PCD requirements forTREM 3A, TREM 3AA and TREM-4 norms.\n- Coordinate with emission regulation nodal agencies to ensure legal compliance and certification.\nTools & Data Analysis:\n- Utilize advanced tools such as ETAS INCA, AVL Concerto, CAMEO for calibration and data evaluation.\n- Benchmark competitor systems and integrate learnings into development.\nProject Execution & Coordination:\n- Oversee engine build quality and timelines across project stages.\n- Coordinate with manufacturing plant teams for build execution.\n- Liaise with component development teams to ensure timely part availability.\n- Collaborate with testing teams for calibration and functional test execution.\n- Lead troubleshooting of vehicle issues from field/customer feedback.\nTeam Leadership & Collaboration:\n- Mentor junior engineers and foster a culture of technical excellence.\n- Collaborate with cross-functional teams including hardware, software, testing, and regulatory affairs.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Calibration & Development:\\\\n- Lead Mechanical and CRS FIE system calibration across platforms.\\\\n- Drive combustion development and optimize engine performance.\\\\n- Execute engine calibration to meet performance and emission targets for TREM IIIAA, TREM-4 and TREM-5\\\\n- Conduct vehicle calibration to meet drivability and noise targets.\\\\n- Formulate and execute Design of Experiments (DoE) for calibration optimization.\\\\nEmission & Certification:\\\\n- Select and validate engine emission hardware including FIE and EATS systems.\\\\n- Ensure compliance with DSM, NCD, PCD requirements forTREM 3A, TREM 3AA and TREM-4 norms.\\\\n- Coordinate with emission regulation nodal agencies to ensure legal compliance and certification.\\\\nTools & Data Analysis:\\\\n- Utilize advanced tools such as ETAS INCA, AVL Concerto, CAMEO for calibration and data evaluation.\\\\n- Benchmark competitor systems and integrate learnings into development.\\\\nProject Execution & Coordination:\\\\n- Oversee engine build quality and timelines across project stages.\\\\n- Coordinate with manufacturing plant teams for build execution.\\\\n- Liaise with component development teams to ensure timely part availability.\\\\n- Collaborate with testing teams for calibration and functional test execution.\\\\n- Lead troubleshooting of vehicle issues from field/customer feedback.\\\\nTeam Leadership & Collaboration:\\\\n- Mentor junior engineers and foster a culture of technical excellence.\\\\n- Collaborate with cross-functional teams including hardware, software, testing, and regulatory affairs.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"B Tech (Mech/Automobile) / MTech (Mech/Automobile/Combustion Development/ECU Calibration)\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"4 to 7 Years\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Mohali\", \"title\": \"Deputy Manager-R&D\", \"location\": \"Mohali, R&D Mohali, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=560\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Deputy Manager-R&D\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1432384200\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Mohali-Deputy-Manager-R&D-R&D/1432384200/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mohali, R&D Mohali, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mohali-Deputy-Manager-R&D-R&D/1432384200/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1432384200\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mohali, R&D Mohali, IN','Deputy Manager-R&D'),(5471,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_27e94deda52c','Deputy Manager - Simulation & Modelling',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore, Banglore CO, IN','Banglore CO','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Roles and Responsibilities\nGenerate and Calibrate Vehicle Pedal maps, Brake maps, Regen Maps and Parameters related to Torque Path, Creep control, Hill Hold Control, Vehicle tip-in/tip-out, Acceleration, Speed limitation, Torque limits etc\nPerform Vehicle level drivability calibration/Torque Path calibration to meet Drivability targets\nPerform Calibration for meeting Range and Energy Consumption Targets both at Inhouse and at Homologation/Certification/Test facilities\nWork on model based calibration methods using pre-simulation of functions and features before actual calibration on vehicles\nWork closely with Simulation and Modelling engineers to gather relevant insights relevant for calibration\nPerform calibration of  Sensors used for SoC measurement\nPerform calibration of Battery management system (BMS) functions\nPerforma Calibration of specific motor control parameters related to driveability\nCoordinate with other departments such as architecture, software development & validation team to ensure achievement of calibration goals\nManage and maintain all calibration changes as applicable to different vehicle variants\nBe able to take test drives of atleast limited driving maneouvres and hold a valid 4wheeler driving license\nFunctional Competencies\nMust have worked in atleast any one ECU/VCU Drivability Calibration Project\nExposure to Calibration tools - ETAS INCA, Visu,VECTOR Cannoe, AVL\nMust have overview of Vehicle compnents and its functionalities\nValid 4 wheeler driving license and ability to carryout atleast simple limited test drives',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Bangalore-Deputy-Manager-Simulation-&-Modelling-Bang/1432348100','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=440','2026-10-13T12:16:02.142859+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','a6cb6a8df933e3de0d9a36f80c2b9e8f9ef8b56b4ecbdd6ea58d4e5c203b3e87','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/j