osystem, we are in a unique position to democratize credit for deserving consumers & merchants and we are committed to it. India\\\\u2019s largest digital lending story is brewing here. It\\\\u2019s your opportunity to be a part of the story!\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"-6+ years of experience in Sales Training, Learning & Development, or Training Delivery within Banking, NBFC, Fintech, or Lending domains.\\\\n-The ideal candidate will be responsible for enhancing product knowledge, sales capabilities, and process adherence through engaging learning interventions and continuous coaching initiatives.\\\\n-Design and deliver training programs for sales teams on lending products, sales processes, compliance requirements, and operational procedures.\\\\n-Develop and maintain training content, including presentations, training manuals, SOPs, assessments, and e-learning modules.\\\\n-Conduct classroom, virtual, and field-based training sessions to ensure effective knowledge transfer and skill development.\\\\n-Collaborate with business stakeholders and subject matter experts to create practical and engaging learning experiences aligned with business objectives.\\\\n-Evaluate trainee performance through assessments, feedback, and performance tracking to identify learning gaps and improvement areas.\\\\n-Provide ongoing coaching and mentoring to sales teams to improve productivity, customer handling, and conversion effectiveness.\\\\n-Monitor training effectiveness and recommend enhancements to training methodologies, content, and delivery mechanisms.\\\\n-Ensure all training programs remain aligned with organizational goals, regulatory guidelines, and evolving business requirements.\\\\n\\\\nMust Have: \\\\n-Should have good networking capabilities and be willing to travel extensively throughout their specified area. Skilled in coaching and mentoring, a quick learner who grasps and puts into application the new learnt ideas and concepts.\\\\n-Strong understanding of lending products, sales processes, and customer acquisition practices.\\\\n-Excellent communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills.\\\\n-Ability to create engaging training content and facilitate interactive learning sessions.\\\\n-Proficiency in Microsoft PowerPoint, Excel, and Learning Management Systems (LMS) is preferred.\\\\n\\\\nEducational Qualification:\\\\n-Graduate/Postgraduate in any discipline.\\\\n-Certification in Training & Development or Learning Facilitation will be an added advantage.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nWhy join us?\\\\nA collaborative output driven program that brings cohesiveness across businesses through technology Improve the average revenue per use by increasing the cross-sell opportunities A solid 360 feedback from your peer teams on your support of their goals. Respect, that is earned, not demanded from your peers and manager\\\\nCompensation: If you are the right fit, we believe in creating wealth for you with enviable 500 mn+ registered users, 21 mn+ merchants and depth of data in our ecosystem, we are in a unique position to democratize credit for deserving consumers & merchants and we are committed to it. India\\\\u2019s largest digital lending story is brewing here. It\\\\u2019s your opportunity to be a part of the story!\\\", \\\"Company Description\\\": \\\"Paytm is India\'s leading mobile payments and financial services distribution company. Pioneer of the mobile QR payments revolution in India, Paytm builds technologies that help small businesses with payments and commerce. Paytms mission is to serve half a billion Indians and bring them to the mainstream economy with the help of technology.\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_lever','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\", \"raw_department\": \"department\", \"raw_employment_type\": \"employment_type\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,'Business','Full-time Employment','Mumbai, Maharashtra','Process Trainer - Manager - Lending (West)'),(5655,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_095_417d3938f414','TA Enabling- Team Lead','HR','Talent Management','Noida, Uttar Pradesh',NULL,'India','onsite','On-roll','3-5 Years of experience','Graduation',NULL,NULL,'Job Description: Talent Acquisition (Enabling Hiring)\n\nLocation: Noida\n\nAbout Paytm\nPaytm is India\'s leading mobile payments and financial services distribution company. Pioneer of the mobile QR payments revolution in India, Paytm builds technologies that help small businesses with payments and commerce. Paytm’s mission is to serve half a billion Indians and bring them to the mainstream economy with the help of technology.\n\nAbout the Team\nThe talent acquisition team is responsible for identifying, sourcing, and securing top talent for various businesses within Paytm.\n\nAbout the Role\nWe are seeking an accomplished Talent Acquisition for Enabling/Corporate hiring function. This critical role will be responsible for defining and executing a robust talent acquisition strategy for Enabling positions across Paytm. You will act as a strategic partner to our executive team, ensuring the attraction, assessment, and successful onboarding of top-tier talent that aligns with our ambitious growth objectives.\n\nExpectations/Requirements\nDraw on extensive knowledge of Talent Acquisition and the functional areas of the business, forging dynamic, trusted relationships with business leaders, and HR business partners.\nUtilize analytics and market intelligence to anticipate roadblocks, identify talent trends, and strategically solve complex executive hiring challenges.\nOptimize operational process flows for executive search, identifying ways to deliver a consistent, scalable, and highly customer-obsessed recruitment experience to all senior stakeholders.\nDrive an exceptional candidate and referee experience for executive hires, delivering on key internal SLAs and maintaining confidentiality and discretion\n.Create and present comprehensive KPI reports and manage strategic dashboards for executive hiring metrics.\n\nSuperpowers/Skills\n3-5 Years of experience in Talent Acquisition with a significant focus on enabling & Corporate roles (Finance, HR, Marketing, PR, Legal, Marketing, Enterprise Sales) hiring, preferably within a fast-paced, high-growth technology.\nExperience in full-cycle recruiting (end-to-end recruitment), sourcing and employment branding.\nCritical stakeholder management is preferred.\nExcellent recruitment reporting & dashboarding skills.\nFamiliarity with a variety of different selection methods and use of social media and job boards with experience with Sourcing and Recruitment Marketing tools preferably with an experience working on any HRIS tool.\nA sense of ownership and pride in your performance and its impact on the company’s success.\nCritical thinker and problem-solving skills.\n\nEducation\nGraduation in any discipline; MBA in HR will be an added advantage.\n\nWhy Join Us\nBe part of a merit-based culture that thrives on self-motivated & driven individuals who are set out to make a successful career in India\'s fastest growing FinTech Organization. Our agile & democratic setup gives space to your creativity, offers opportunity to work at scale coupled with an environment that encourages diverse perspectives at all times. If you are the right fit, we believe in creating wealth for you. With enviable 500 mn+ registered users, 21 mn+ merchants and depth of data in our ecosystem, we are in a unique position to democratize credit for deserving consumers & merchants - and we are committed to it. India\'s largest digital lending story is brewing here. It\'s your opportunity to be a part of the story!\n','1783506887337',NULL,'https://jobs.lever.co/paytm/d57f6e10-2da4-4072-806c-ca66c1966afb/apply','https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/paytm?mode=json','2026-10-13T12:18:22.760462+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_LEVER)','8b50797c75d2865f3e81835245a4b346cce2b797b2a4ab713f47b8424336ea67','COMP_