 to ensure smooth execution of field operations.\nManage and monitor one or two loading vans and the respective BA teams as per directions from the Team Leader/HoG.\nEnsure strict compliance with safety requirements under the Annual Safety Plan, HIRA, JSA, and applicable safety procedures.\nTake primary shutdown wherever required and establish a proper safety zone before commencing work.\nEnsure proper use and maintenance of the PTW (Permit to Work) booklet and adherence to all permit-related requirements.\nImmediately report safety incidents, near misses, unsafe site conditions, unsafe poles, and other hazards through the Suraksha Portal.\nActively participate in safety initiatives and contribute towards building a strong safety culture with a zero-accident objective.\nMonitor field teams to ensure quality, productivity, safety, and adherence to defined processes.\nMaintain proper coordination and communication with internal and external stakeholders for timely resolution of field issues.\nPerform other metering, commercial, or field-related activities assigned by management based on organizational requirements.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Date\\\": \\\"15 Sept 2026\\\", \\\"Location\\\": \\\"TPDDL, DELHI OFFICE, 0, India, 0\\\", \\\"Company\\\": \\\"tatapower\\\", \\\"Key Responsibilities\\\": \\\"Execute smart meter installations for HCB consumers, including Single Phase Whole Current Meters, as per defined SOPs and work instructions.\\\\nEnsure timely execution of PA and Non-PA cases in accordance with Performance Assurance timelines and applicable SLAs.\\\\nConduct daily VAN audits before starting field activities and ensure the availability and proper use of PPEs, tools, testing equipment, and other required resources.\\\\nEnsure proper utilization and compliance of the MMG 2.0 App for field activities, case updates, and operational processes.\\\\nCoordinate effectively with Zones, Business Associates (BAs), CEG, and other stakeholders to ensure smooth execution of field operations.\\\\nManage and monitor one or two loading vans and the respective BA teams as per directions from the Team Leader/HoG.\\\\nEnsure strict compliance with safety requirements under the Annual Safety Plan, HIRA, JSA, and applicable safety procedures.\\\\nTake primary shutdown wherever required and establish a proper safety zone before commencing work.\\\\nEnsure proper use and maintenance of the PTW (Permit to Work) booklet and adherence to all permit-related requirements.\\\\nImmediately report safety incidents, near misses, unsafe site conditions, unsafe poles, and other hazards through the Suraksha Portal.\\\\nActively participate in safety initiatives and contribute towards building a strong safety culture with a zero-accident objective.\\\\nMonitor field teams to ensure quality, productivity, safety, and adherence to defined processes.\\\\nMaintain proper coordination and communication with internal and external stakeholders for timely resolution of field issues.\\\\nPerform other metering, commercial, or field-related activities assigned by management based on organizational requirements.\\\", \\\"Qualification & Experience\\\": \\\"Diploma in Electrical Engineering.\\\\nMinimum 3+ years of relevant experience in electrical metering, smart meter installation, field operations, or a similar role.\\\\nStrong understanding of electrical safety practices, field execution, and team/vendor coordination.\\\", \\\"Location & Mobility\\\": \\\"Location:\\\\nDelhi, with Pan-India mobility as required.\\\\nThe position may involve\\\\ntransfer or deployment to other locations within the Tata Group\\\\n, based on business and organizational requirements.\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-19 12:29:26.260156','{\"href\": \"/TataPowerDelhi/job/TPDDL%2C-DELHI-OFFICE-Field-Engineer-0-0/59791744/\", \"req_id\": \"59791744\"}','ats_api_trusted','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_l