s For Corporate and Financial Institutions. To facilitate senior management to take business decisions and get external finance. By preparing financial statement for next 7 years based on lot many business assumptions.\nProduct Costing To know the product cost and its various elements. To decide selling price By doing valuation of Bills of Material, Calculation of conversion cost per product and per activity.\nProject Capitalisation Of Assets and Equipments procured on site. To comply with statutory requirements and company policy. By preparing proper Additions Schedule and maintaining Fixed Assets Register.\nKnowledge :\nAccounts and Finance Â Accounting standards and Indian GAAP\nStatutory compliances Â legal, taxation\nSkills:\nBusiness understanding,\nAnalytical skills\nCross functional perspective\nDecision making,\nLeader ship\ncommunication\nTeam management',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Apply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mohali, Swaraj Engines Mohali, IN','Management Trainee F&A'),(5837,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_0c66332729e7','Deputy Manager - MES Rudrapur',NULL,NULL,'Rudrapur, Rudrapur, IN','Rudrapur','India',NULL,NULL,'Successful candidates should have robust technical expertise in industrial control systems and MES-IoT environments, com','Bachelor',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. MES team at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will spearhead the ideation and implementation of shop floor automation technologies. This involves conducting thorough studies of machines and processes to identify optimized solutions that enhance operational efficiency and data accuracy. You will be responsible for understanding and leveraging data inputs from IoT sensors, actuators, and embedded controls, ensuring seamless data collection and integrity at the source.\n2.Your role will include developing scenarios for fault prediction and performance enhancement through edge analytics and data normalization techniques. You will drive manufacturing analytics initiatives by designing and consolidating visualization tools and interfaces to facilitate comprehensive machine and process digitization. This requires standardising data collection methods for manufacturing execution systems (MES), enabling efficient integration of supplier process data, and evaluating appropriate technology standards for digital interfaces across hardware, software, and embedded modules.\n3.In addition, you will manage multiple projects concurrently from planning to deployment and sustenance phases, utilising tools such as MS Project for effective scheduling and resource allocation. This entails close coordination with project execution teams, vendors, plant heads, IT infrastructure teams, and digital champions to ensure successful MES and digitisation project rollouts. Budget oversight, milestone tracking, and risk mitigation will be key responsibilities while ensuring the alignment of digital initiatives with overall plant KPIs.\n4. Key deliverables include continuous engagement in project reviews with stakeholders, managing assets in collaboration with Asset Management, and fostering collaboration with IT teams to support compute, storage, and network requirements. You will also be accountable for developing dashboards and reports that monitor benefit realization, highlight deviations, and propose improvements to enhance analytics capabilities and business insights effectively.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nSuccessful candidates should have robust technical expertise in industrial control systems and MES-IoT environments, complemented by practical capabilities in PLC programming and industrial communication networks such as Modbus TCP/IP, Profinet, and Profibus.\nHands-on experience with devices from major vendors like Siemens, Schneider, Rockwell, and Mitsubishi, as well as familiarity with sensor technologies and industrial measurement techniques, is necessary. Functional understanding of data sampling, signal conditioning, and the analysis of both linear and non-linear systems will form the foundation of your daily responsibilities.\nProficiency with data analytics tools, especially in Python including libraries such as Pandas and Matplotlib, is highly desirable to assist in the extraction of actionable insights from manufacturing data. Comfortable documentation skills using MS Visio, Word, and PowerPoint to produce detailed technical schematics and presentations are expected.\nThe ideal candidate will demonstrate initiative, excellent problem-solving aptitude, and strong collaborative abilities. The capacity to quickly interpret user requirements and transform these into technical use cases will contribute significantly to project success. Embracing a continuous learning mindset and enthusiasm for emerging technologies aimed at operational efficiency is essential.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Rudrapur-Deputy-Manager-MES-Rudrapur-Rudr/1439406800','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=20','2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','a7bdad86b7a387e5adde31e6116fc1aab03b05a9e25caf6a7931155bb8f89dad','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Rudrapur-Deputy-Manager-MES-Rudrapur-Rudr/1439406800','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Deputy Manager - MES Rudrapur\", \"location\": \"Rudrapur, Rudrapur, IN\", \"external_id\": \"1439406800\", \"raw_evidence\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Deputy Manager - MES Rudrapur\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1439406800\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Rudrapur-Deputy-Manager-MES-Rudrapur-Rudr/1439406800/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Rudrapur, Rudrapur, IN\\\"}\"}','ATS_API_SUCC