 in more than 100 countries.\" />\n    <meta name=\"title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"adventure aerospace aftermarket automotive boats brand brands business businesses careers change channels clean companies company connect contact contacts counts cultural culture defence directors equipment estate facebook farm finance financial followers formula global good googleapis graph group growth history http https india industry information innovation instagram investors jobs know leadership learn listed mahindra mahindrarise marazzo marketplace media mobility motor news october outreach overview people performance plant presence press previous programmes purpose read real releases reports resources responsibility results rise room services social sport statistics steel stories sustainability tech technology trails twitter users valley video views visit watch wheelers work world youtube\" />\n\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n                <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/fed09ea3-5cdb-4e2b-a362-c.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/customHeader.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/sitebuilderframework.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/BS3ColumnizedSearch.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/fontawesome4.7/css/font-awesome-4.7.0.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n<style>\nbody > .modal-backdrop {\n    display: none !important;\n}\n.menu.desktop .nav > li .dropdown-menu li a{ color : white !important}\n#header .links a{ color: white !important;}\n.dropdown-menu.company-dropdown.headerdropdown.backgroundcolordc8b140b5a119dc3 .menu{ color : black !important}\n.custom-header-menu .nav.nav-pills{ width: 807px !important; }\n.custom-header-signinLanguage .inner.limitwidth{ max-width: 1200px; }\n.customPlugin{ margin-bottom: 0 !important; }\n\n</style>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\"></script></body>\n\n        \n        <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/9349339a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'Rudrapur',1,'2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','1439406800',NULL,NULL,'Successful candidates should have robust technical expertise in industrial control systems and MES-IoT environments, complemented by practical capabilities in PLC programming and industrial communication networks such as Modbus TCP/IP, Profinet, and Profibus.\nHands-on experience with devices from major vendors like Siemens, Schneider, Rockwell, and Mitsubishi, as well as familiarity with sensor technologies and industrial measurement techniques, is necessary. Functional understanding of data sampling, signal conditioning, and the analysis of both linear and non-linear systems will form the foundation of your daily responsibilities.\nProficiency with data analytics tools, especially in Python including libraries such as Pandas and Matplotlib, is highly desirable to assist in the extraction of actionable insights from manufacturing data. Comfortable documentation skills using MS Visio, Word, and PowerPoint to produce detailed technical schematics and presentations are expected.\nThe ideal candidate will demonstrate initiative, excellent problem-solving aptitude, and strong collaborative abilities. The capacity to quickly interpret user requirements and transform these into technical use cases will contribute significantly to project success. Embracing a continuous learning mindset and enthusiasm for emerging technologies aimed at operational efficiency is essential.',NULL,'1. MES team at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will spearhead the ideation and implementation of shop floor automation technologies. This involves conducting thorough studies of machines and processes to identify optimized solutions that enhance operational efficiency and data accuracy. You will be responsible for understanding and leveraging data inputs from IoT sensors, actuators, and embedded controls, ensuring seamless data collection and integrity at the source.\n2.Your role will include developing scenarios for fault prediction and performance enhancement through edge analytics and data normalization techniques. You will drive manufacturing analytics initiatives by designing and consolidating visualization tools and interfaces to facilitate comprehensive machine and process digitization. This requires standardising data collection methods for manufacturing execution systems (MES), enabling efficient integration of supplier process data, and evaluating appropriate technology standards for digital interfaces across hardware, software, and embedded modules.\n3.In addition, you will manage multiple projects concurrently from planning to deployment and sustenance phases, utilising tools such as MS Project for effective scheduling and resource allocation. This entails close coordination with project execution teams, vendors, plant heads, IT infrastructure teams, and digital champions to ensure successful MES and digitisation project rollouts. Budget oversight, milestone tracking, and risk mitigation will be key responsibilities while ensuring the alignment of digital initiatives with overall plant KPIs.\n4. Key deliverables include continuous engagement in project reviews with stakeholders, managing assets in collaboration with Asset Management, and fostering collaboration with IT teams to support compute, storage, and network requirements. You will also be accountable for developing dashboards and reports that monitor benefit realization, highlight deviations, and propose improvements to enhance analytics capabilities and business insights effectively.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"1. MES team at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will spearhead the ideation and implementation of shop floor automation technologies. This involves conducting thorough studies of machines and processes to identify optimized solutions that enhance operational efficiency and data accuracy. You will be responsible for understanding and leveraging data inputs from IoT sensors, actuators, and embedded controls, ensuring seamless data collection and integrity at the source.\\\\n2.Your role will include developing scenarios for fault prediction and performance enhancement through edge analytics and data normalization techniques. You will drive manufacturing analytics initiatives by designing and consolidating visualization tools and interfaces to facilitate comprehensive machine and process digitization. This requires standardising data collection methods for manufacturing execution systems (MES), enabling efficient integration of supplier process data, and evaluating appropriate technology standards for digital interfaces across hardware, software, and embedded modules.\\\\n3.In addition, you will manage multiple projects concurrently from planning to deployment and sustenance phases, utilising tools such as MS Project for effective scheduling and resource allocation. This entails close coordination with project execution teams, vendors, plant heads, IT infrastructure teams, and digital champions to ensure successful MES and digitisation project rollouts. Budget oversight, milestone tracking, and risk mitigation will be key responsibilities while ensuring the alignment of digital initiatives with overall plant KPIs.\\\\n4. Key deliverables include continuous engagement in project reviews with stakeholders, managing assets in collaboration with Asset Management, and fostering collaboration with IT teams to support compute, storage, and network requirements. You will also be accountable for developing dashboards and reports that monitor benefit realization, highlight deviations, and propose improvements to enhance analytics capabilities and business insights effectively.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"We are seeking candidates with 2-5 years of progressive experience in industrial automation and manufacturing digital transformation projects, particularly involving MES and IoT ecosystems. Ideal experience includes hands-on exposure to PLC programming, industrial communication protocols such as Modbus TCP/IP, Profinet, and Profibus, and working with major PLC brands like Siemens, Schneider, Rockwell, and Mitsubishi.\\\\nThe role requires practical knowledge of sensor technologies, industrial device configuration including RFID and wireless systems, and signal conditioning in both linear and non-linear systems. Experience in data analytics using tools such as Python, Pandas, and Matplotlib to analyze manufacturing data and develop predictive scenarios is highly valuable.\\\\nProven capability in managing automation projects end-to-end\\\\u2014right from technology ideation, data acquisition strategy, through deployment and sustained operations\\\\u2014is sought. Strong documentation skills using software such as MS Visio, Word, and PowerPoint to translate technical insights into clear, actionable materials for diverse stakeholders are essential.\\\\nApplicants should demonstrate autonomy in problem solving, debugging manufacturing web and distributed Windows applications, and working collaboratively within cross-functional teams. Prior involvement in digital manufacturing environments and manufacturing analytics projects will be advantageous.\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Preferred candidates will have experience in the automotive manufacturing sector or original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), where precision, automation, and data-driven decision-making are pivotal. Exposure to shop floor digital transformation within automotive plants or equivalent high-volume industrial settings will enable a strong understanding of the complexities and expectations within this industry.\\\\nExperience within industries that emphasize stringent quality management, real-time system monitoring, and predictive maintenance will also be beneficial. Familiarity with automotive production systems and MES integration tailored to large-scale manufacturing will be a significant asset in delivering maximum impact through this role.\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"Essential Qualifications:\\\", \\\"Essential Qualifications\\\": \\\"Bachelor\\\\u2019s Degree in Electrical, Electronics, or Instrumentation Engineering (B.E. / B.Tech.) with a minimum of 60% aggregate marks or equivalent CGPA from a recognised university.\\\\nDesirable Attributes:\\\", \\\"Desirable Attributes\\\": \\\"Additional certifications or training in Industrial Automation, IoT, Data Analytics, or related fields would be advantageous.\\\\nContinuing education relating to programming languages, automation frameworks, and digital manufacturing applications is encouraged to keep pace with evolving technology.\\\", \\\"General Requirements\\\": \\\"Successful candidates should have robust technical expertise in industrial control systems and MES-IoT environments, complemented by practical capabilities in PLC programming and industrial communication networks such as Modbus TCP/IP, Profinet, and Profibus.\\\\nHands-on experience with devices from major vendors like Siemens, Schneider, Rockwell, and Mitsubishi, as well as familiarity with sensor technologies and industrial measurement techniques, is necessary. Functional understanding of data sampling, signal conditioning, and the analysis of both linear and non-linear systems will form the foundation of your daily responsibilities.\\\\nProficiency with data analytics tools, especially in Python including libraries such as Pandas and Matplotlib, is highly desirable to assist in the extraction of actionable insights from manufacturing data. Comfortable documentation skills using MS Visio, Word, and PowerPoint to produce detailed technical schematics and presentations are expected.\\\\nThe ideal candidate will demonstrate initiative, excellent problem-solving aptitude, and strong collaborative abilities. The capacity to quickly interpret user requirements and transform these into technical use cases will contribute significantly to project success. Embracing a continuous learning mindset and enthusiasm for emerging technologies aimed at operational efficiency is essential.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"At Mahindra & Mahindra Limited, we are deeply committed to fostering diversity, equity, and inclusion within our workplace. We celebrate the rich diversity of our team members and believe that it inspires creativity, drives innovation, and enriches our organisation.\\\\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and consider all qualified applicants without regard to any legally protected characteristics including but not limited to age, caste, race, religion, colour, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status, citizenship, ancestry, or financial status.\\\\nOur recruitment process is designed to be accessible and inclusive, encouraging candidates from varied backgrounds to bring their distinct perspectives and experiences. We are dedicated to maintaining an environment where everyone feels respected, valued, and empowered to contribute their best.\\\\nTogether, we aspire to build a workplace culture that reflects the diverse communities we serve and drives sustainable growth through mutual respect and understanding.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nMachinist, Instrumentation, Engineer, Electrical, Manufacturing, Automotive, Engineering\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Rudrapur, Rudrapur, IN','Deputy Manager - MES Rudrapur'),(5838,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_929e69baa2f3','Senior Product Engineer - BI Platform',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN','MUM-KND-AFS(AD)','India',NULL,NULL,'Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent work experience','Bachelor',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nDesign, develop, and maintain robust web applications using React for dynamic, responsive, and user-friendly interfaces\nBuild and optimize backend services and APIs using Node.js to support enterprise business workflows and integrations\nImplement data processing, automation, and application logic using Python\nWork with SQL databases to design efficient schemas, write complex queries, and optimize performance\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams including product managers, engineering leads, architects, and QA to deliver solutions aligned with business goals\nDrive best practices in software design, code quality, testing, performance tuning, and security\nLead technical discussions, provide architectural guidance, and contribute to engineering standards\nTroubleshoot production issues and provide effective, timely resolutions\nMentor junior developers and support team growth through code reviews and technical knowledge sharing\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nStrong expertise in React\nStrong expertise in Node.js\nStrong experience in Python\nSolid working knowledge of SQL and relational database design\nExperience building and consuming REST APIs\nAbility to write clean, scalable, and maintainable code\nExperience with GCP cloud environment and deployment pipelines\nStrong problem-solving, debugging, and communication skills',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-A_O-Senior-Product-Engineer-BI-Platform-MUM/1439406900','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=20','2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','018e1f0a534cde40bf8512aad8203b0acee4f489a700866959a2d77d124fdbfc','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-A_O-Senior-Product-Engineer-BI-Platform-MUM/1439406900','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Senior Product Engineer - BI Platform\", \"location\": \"Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN\", \"external_id\": \"1439406900\", \"raw_evidence\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Senior Product Engineer - BI Platform\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1439406900\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Mumbai-A_O-Senior-Product-Engineer-BI-Platform-MUM/1439406900/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN\\\"}\"}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:01.878053',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:01.873132',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:01.873132',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-