e actions.\\\\nMonitor warranty, field failure, and customer complaint trends.\\\\nDrive defect reduction projects and improve First Time Quality\\\\nCustomer Quality Management\\\", \\\"Customer Quality Management\\\": \\\"Handle customer concerns and quality escalations.\\\\nCoordinate customer audits and assessment activities.\\\\nEnsure timely closure of customer complaints using structured problem-solving methodologies.\\\\nMeasurement & Quality Validation\\\", \\\"Measurement & Quality Validation\\\": \\\"Review dimensional, gap & flush, fitment, and functional quality reports.\\\\nMonitor critical-to-quality characteristics during production.\\\\nEnsure calibration and capability of measurement systems.\\\\nSupport MSA, SPC, and capability studies.\\\\nTeam Management (For Manager Role)\\\", \\\"Team Management (For Manager Role)\\\": \\\"Lead and develop quality engineers, inspectors, and line quality teams.\\\\nConduct training on quality tools and standards.\\\\nEstablish performance objectives and quality targets.\\\\nReview daily quality KPIs and drive accountability.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"5-9 years of experience in Automotive Manufacturing Quality, preferably in TCF operations\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"B.Tech\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"Bachelor\'s Degree in Mechanical / Automobile / Production Engineering.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"At Mahindra and Mahindra Limited, we believe that diversity drives innovation, and inclusion is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to cultivating a workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.\\\\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to age, caste, race, religion, color, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital or domestic partnership status, pregnancy or childbirth, veteran status, citizenship status, ancestry, financial status, or any other personal characteristic protected by applicable law.\\\\nWe actively encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply and bring their unique perspectives to our teams. We are committed to ensuring an accessible and inclusive experience for all applicants.\\\\nTogether, we rise by embracing differences and building a future that reflects the communities we serve.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nEngineer, Automotive, Engineering\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chakan, Chakan, IN','Assistant Manager MQA BEV'),(5844,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_0912d265187d','Deputy Manager-TCF Quality',NULL,NULL,'Chakan, Chakan, IN','Chakan','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1.Handling of Product & Process Audit of Commercial Vehicle & Assembly Line ( TCF ).\n2. Responsible for Outgoing Vehicle Quality level and monitoring the same through Daily work management.\n3. Managing team of Inspectors & Auditors working in Shifts.\n4. Root cause analysis of customer complaints , In-process defects and Line rejections.\n5. Daily MIS generation for all Quality indicators , conducting meeting with stake holders and taking corrective actions.\n6. Monitoring of actions & Escalating nonadherence of actions.\n7. Monitoring of Process Capability through SPC & monitoring of R&R through MSA.\n8. Standardization of all Process Parameters, SOP/SOS & updation of Control Plan & Check sheet.\n9. Product & Process Improvement through Kaizen, Poka-yoke & Detection control (AI based ).\n10. New Product introduction & EN management & Planning for all Quality evaluation.\n11. Horizontal deployment & Lesson learnt preparation.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chakan-Deputy-Manager-TCF-Quality-Chak/1439416700','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=20','2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','69df5762bfc4cc415769c96019c5083ee58ad85bbbb32e2fd2c54cc36774782c','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chakan-Deputy-Manager-TCF-Quality-Chak/1439416700','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Deputy Manager-TCF Quality\", \"location\": \"Chakan, Chakan, IN\", \"external_id\": \"1439416700\", \"raw_evidence\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Deputy Manager-TCF Quality\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1439416700\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Chakan-Deputy-Manager-TCF-Quality-Chak/1439416700/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Chakan, Chakan, IN\\\"}\"}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:02.806210',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:02.797377',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:02.797377',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platform/bootstrap/3.4.8_NES/css/bootstrap.min.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/bootstrapV3.global.responsive.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/navbar-fixed-top.css\" />\n                \n                <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/platform/js/j2w/j2w.fallbacks.js\"></script>\n                