, Agribusiness, Marketing, or related field.\nMBA (Marketing/Agribusiness) preferred.\n5-8 years of sales experience in Seeds, Crop Protection, Agri Inputs, or related agri-business sector.\nMinimum 2-3 years of experience managing a territory independently.\nKnowledge of Field Crop markets and agronomic practices in Madhya Pradesh region will be preferred.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,'To drive sales growth, market penetration, and business development for the Field Crops portfolio within the assigned territory. The role is responsible for achieving sales targets, strengthening the dealer-distributor network, executing market development activities, and ensuring effective implementation of sales strategies to maximize revenue and market share.','\"{\\\"Area Sales Manager (ASM) \\\\u2013 Field Crops\\\": \\\"Location:\\\\nRewa, Madhya Pradesh\\\\nDepartment:\\\\nSales \\\\u2013 Field Crops\\\\nReporting To:\\\\nRegional Sales Manager / Zonal Sales Manager\\\", \\\"Location\\\": \\\"Rewa, Madhya Pradesh Department: Sales \\\\u2013 Field Crops Reporting To: Regional Sales Manager / Zonal Sales Manager\\\", \\\"Job Purpose\\\": \\\"To drive sales growth, market penetration, and business development for the Field Crops portfolio within the assigned territory. The role is responsible for achieving sales targets, strengthening the dealer-distributor network, executing market development activities, and ensuring effective implementation of sales strategies to maximize revenue and market share.\\\", \\\"Sales & Business Development\\\": \\\"Achieve monthly, quarterly, and annual sales targets for assigned products and territory.\\\\nDevelop and execute territory sales plans aligned with business objectives.\\\\nIdentify growth opportunities and increase market share across the assigned region.\\\\nMonitor market trends, competitor activities, pricing, and product performance.\\\\nDrive primary and secondary sales through effective channel management.\\\", \\\"Channel Management\\\": \\\"Appoint, develop, and manage distributors and dealers within the territory.\\\\nEnsure channel partner profitability and business sustainability.\\\\nMonitor distributor stock levels, sales performance, and collections.\\\\nResolve channel partner concerns and maintain healthy business relationships.\\\", \\\"Market Development\\\": \\\"Plan and execute farmer meetings, field demonstrations, crop shows, field days, and promotional campaigns.\\\\nWork closely with the technical and marketing teams to demonstrate product performance and benefits.\\\\nCollect market intelligence and customer feedback for continuous product improvement.\\\\nEnhance brand visibility and product awareness among farmers and influencers.\\\", \\\"Customer Relationship Management\\\": \\\"Establish strong relationships with farmers, progressive growers, distributors, dealers, and key influencers.\\\\nAddress customer complaints and provide timely solutions.\\\\nEnsure high levels of customer satisfaction and retention.\\\", \\\"Collection & Compliance\\\": \\\"Ensure timely collection of outstanding payments from channel partners.\\\\nMaintain compliance with company policies, sales processes, and reporting requirements.\\\\nSubmit accurate sales forecasts, market reports, and business updates.\\\", \\\"Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)\\\": \\\"Achievement of sales targets and revenue growth.\\\\nMarket share growth in assigned territory.\\\\nDealer and distributor productivity.\\\\nCollections and receivables management.\\\\nExecution of promotional and market development activities.\\\\nNew dealer appointments and territory expansion.\\\\nTeam productivity and customer engagement.\\\", \\\"Qualifications & Experience\\\": \\\"Bachelor\'s degree in Agriculture, Agribusiness, Marketing, or related field.\\\\nMBA (Marketing/Agribusiness) preferred.\\\\n5-8 years of sales experience in Seeds, Crop Protection, Agri Inputs, or related agri-business sector.\\\\nMinimum 2-3 years of experience managing a territory independently.\\\\nKnowledge of Field Crop markets and agronomic practices in Madhya Pradesh region will be preferred.\\\", \\\"Required Competencies\\\": \\\"Strong sales and negotiation skills.\\\\nChannel partner management.\\\\nTerritory planning and execution.\\\\nMarket development and farmer engagement.\\\\nTeam leadership and people management.\\\\nAnalytical and problem-solving skills.\\\\nCommunication and stakeholder management.\\\\nProficiency in MS Office and sales reporting systems.\\\", \\\"Travel Requirement\\\": \\\"Extensive travel within assigned territory (80-90% of working time).\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Rewa, Rewa, IN','Area Sales Manager'),(5847,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_caccc20e4e73','Assistant Manager - MQA (Heavy Engine)',NULL,NULL,'Chakan, Chakan, IN','Chakan','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nResolving Customer complaints, failed part analysis, ICA/PCA identification, Verification & Implementation\nResolving daily line concerns, analysis, ICA/PCA identification, Verification & Implementation. Rework procedure finalization & approval\nEnsuring adherence of assembly processes as per drawing and SOP to deliver defect free product\nPro-actively identify process gaps, concerns,  and executing corrective measures along with CFT\nChange Management- FTR Approval (Fitment Verification jointly with CFT), APQP activities & documentation\nOn time closure of project quality gateway deliverables for new models\nAttend Daily Quality meeting, Analysis, ICA/PCA. Quality MIS data Preparation and report release\nEstablish and sustain Quality Management System as per ISO 9001:2015 / IATF 16949 standard\nProcess & product Audit engine 