39a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'Chennai',1,'2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','1439166400',NULL,NULL,'• Self driven and result oriented\n• Quick learner\n• Presentation skills\n• Innovative & CAB mindset\n• Should have good analytical skill while analyzing technical data / information\n• knowledge of Tractor systems & its functionality\n• Good knowledge of MS-Office utilities like: Word, Power point, Excel.\nFunctional Requirements\n:\nExpert in Sheet metal, plastic and Rubber part design and development.\nExpertise in UG- NX software and surface modelling.',NULL,'• Knowledge of complete new product development.\n• Should have Knowledge of tractor cabin / vehicle systems and its applications.\n• Functional understanding & experience in designing the parts for tractor.\n• Design experience of Sheetmetal, Plastic/Trims, Rubbers parts etc.\n• Knowledge of design, testing and validation of tractor Cabin.\n• Expertise in UG NX & Team Centre Engineering\n• Knowledge & should have worked in 1 complete project with design tools like DFMEA, DFM,DFA, DFS & GD&T\n• knowledge of manufacturing process of sheet metal, Rubber and plastic parts.\n•  3-D layout preparation, 2-D drawing preperation.\n• Review & monitoring techincal documnets like vitrual simualtion, Standards & homologation requirments to meet the design spec\'s.\n• Understanding Assembly and Serviceability requirement  in tractor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"\\\\u2022 Knowledge of complete new product development.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Should have Knowledge of tractor cabin / vehicle systems and its applications.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Functional understanding & experience in designing the parts for tractor.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Design experience of Sheetmetal, Plastic/Trims, Rubbers parts etc.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Knowledge of design, testing and validation of tractor Cabin.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Expertise in UG NX & Team Centre Engineering\\\\n\\\\u2022 Knowledge & should have worked in 1 complete project with design tools like DFMEA, DFM,DFA, DFS & GD&T\\\\n\\\\u2022 knowledge of manufacturing process of sheet metal, Rubber and plastic parts.\\\\n\\\\u2022 \\\\u00a03-D layout preparation, 2-D drawing preperation.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Review & monitoring techincal documnets like vitrual simualtion, Standards & homologation requirments to meet the design spec\'s.\\\\n\\\\u2022 Understanding Assembly and Serviceability requirement \\\\u00a0in tractor.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"3-5 years with relevant experience in sheetmetal, plastic and rubber parts design & development.\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Tractor / \\\\u00a0Automotive\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E /\\\\u00a0B. Tech in Automotive/Mechanical\\\", \\\"General Requirements\\\": \\\"\\\\u2022 Self driven and result oriented\\\\n\\\\u2022 Quick learner\\\\n\\\\u2022 Presentation skills\\\\n\\\\u2022 Innovative & CAB mindset\\\\n\\\\u2022 Should have good analytical skill while analyzing technical data / information\\\\n\\\\u2022 knowledge of Tractor systems & its functionality\\\\n\\\\u2022 Good knowledge of MS-Office utilities like: Word, Power point, Excel.\\\\nFunctional Requirements\\\\n:\\\\nExpert in Sheet metal, plastic and Rubber part design and development.\\\\nExpertise in UG- NX software and surface modelling.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nSystems Engineer, Manufacturing Engineer, Engineer, Automotive, Engineering\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV(FD), IN','Engineer - Body Integrated Systems'),(5857,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_33dd236a8ae6','Deputy Manager - Internal Audit',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai - Worli, Mumbai - Worli, IN','Mumbai - Worli','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'CA 1st/2nd attempt',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nChecklist preparation\n- Data collection & analysis\n- Participate in opening meetings & closing meetings\n- Prepare draft reports\n- Get action plans from Auditees\n- Present findings to Mentor/CIA\n- Maintain post audit documentation\n- Peer review\n- Participate in other departmental activities such as investigations, meetings, presentations, departmental budget etc.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nFamiliarity with SAP modules relevant to finance, procurement, and inventory management to enable effective audit testing and data extraction.\nA proven team-oriented approach, with the ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders and contribute constructively within audit teams.\nStrong analytical skills and attention to detail, capable of identifying subtle control gaps and risk signals.\nEffective communication skills, both verbal and written, to articulate complex audit findings clearly and persuasively.\nSelf-motivated, with a commitment to maintaining the highest ethical standards and confidentiality.\nAdaptability to shifting priorities and capability to manage multiple audit assignments concurrently.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-Worli-Deputy-Manager-Internal-Audit-Mumb/1360287800','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=60','2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','eb4c858caa3db799bea0b2773d3647c179fbf00a2db82426c8befbfa07238b39','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mu