approach, with the ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders and contribute constructively within audit teams.\\\\nStrong analytical skills and attention to detail, capable of identifying subtle control gaps and risk signals.\\\\nEffective communication skills, both verbal and written, to articulate complex audit findings clearly and persuasively.\\\\nSelf-motivated, with a commitment to maintaining the highest ethical standards and confidentiality.\\\\nAdaptability to shifting priorities and capability to manage multiple audit assignments concurrently.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd is deeply committed to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workplace where all individuals feel valued and empowered. We actively encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.\\\\nOur recruitment practices are designed to eliminate bias and promote equal opportunities, ensuring a fair hiring process. We believe diversity enriches innovation and business performance, and we strive to cultivate a culture of respect, collaboration, and continuous learning.\\\\nWe support accommodations and provide inclusive resources throughout the employment lifecycle to enable everyone to thrive professionally and personally.\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mumbai - Worli, Mumbai - Worli, IN','Deputy Manager - Internal Audit'),(5858,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_5ba07486a85e','Manager - MCU HW Design Development',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore, Banglore CO, IN','Banglore CO','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Roles, Responsibilities, & Key Deliverables\nHands on experience in 48V systems for Motor drive/Inverter application (Power level- 5KW, 8KW, 10KW, 12KW, 15KW)\nExperience in analysing different topologies of power electronics converters (Inverters for Traction systems, dc-dc converters)\nExperience in hardware system design for analog & digital circuit\nUnderstanding all electronic components and high power devices (MOSFET[Si, SiC], DC Link capacitor, Gate drivers, Microcontroller)\nDevice characterisations of Mosfet with Double pulse test (DPT)\nManufacturing line readiness for new products (PCBA assembly process, EOL testing procedure, Calibration setup and Supplier interactions)\nModelling, simulation analysis experience with tools like MATLAB/Simulink, SPICE, PSIM, tools for time & frequency domain, tolerance, derating analysis\nUnderstanding on Digital Communication protocols like CAN, LIN, RS232, SPI, I2C etc.\nThrough understanding, experience and knowledge on testing of EMI / EMC standards (AIS-004, CISPR25, ISO11452, ISO 7637-2, ISO 7637-3, ISO 10605)\nPCB layout, component placement and guidelines experience as per standards (IPC 2221, IPC 6012, IPC-A-610)\nCollaborate with mechanical, layout and firmware engineers to validate the designs\nUtilizes the support of automated testing, verification & validation tools (Oscilloscope, Power analyser, Power supplies)\nExcellent interpersonal, written, oral communication skills, enthusiasm to perform and learn new activities\nSelf-motivated and able to work independently, strong analytical & problem-solving skills\nPerform Dyno test validations for functional and reliability of Motor control unit.\nDocumentation of test activities, procedure, test setup arrangements\nWillingness to travel across test facilities, manufacturing plant and vendor assembly locations',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Bangalore-Manager-MCU-HW-Design-Development-Bang/1385995300','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=60','2026-10-13T10:46:22.237111+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','acb62ed0521f939ecb7b4d13f3ac01b77d8df00790f19b2db60d45e4fab02e