nd collections\\\\n.\\\\nPrepare\\\\nsales, variance and segment-wise reports\\\\n.\\\\nCoordinate with\\\\nStatutory, Internal and Process Auditors\\\\non sales and debtor-related matters.\\\\nReview/process\\\\ncredit notes for institutional sales\\\\n.\\\\nDrive\\\\nIT automation initiatives\\\\nto streamline credit, debtor ageing, MIS and reconciliation processes, reducing manual effort and improving data accuracy.\\\\nLeverage\\\\nAI and advanced analytics\\\\nfor early identification of credit risks, collection prioritisation, debtor behaviour analysis and management decision-making.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"Fresher / 2\\\\u20134 years\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"CA / ICWA\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Apply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(FD), IN','Deputy Manager - Credit Management'),(5867,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_b3417950e81a','Dy. Manager - NPME Engine',NULL,NULL,'Pune, Nagpur Plant, IN','Nagpur Plant','India',NULL,NULL,'Exp in machine procurement & REQ','BE',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nOverall Layout Planning. Knowledge of Layout making on Auto Cad with various options to optimize and facility planning for each line stations and sub assembly stations.\nMaterial movement finalization along with trolleys design approvals. Installation and commissioning of assembly line equipment such sub assembly station, Pressing machines, Main line conveyors, Assembly tooling’s, Testing, Tightening, Sealant dispensing, Riveting.  Filtration, Low-cost automations, POKAYOKES, Material handling trolleys, Tightening tool & Cleaning machine.\nProvide Design Inputs to Engineering Team for ease of Manufacturing.\nPlanning for Optimum Utilization of Existing Facility.\nProcess improvement with model specific add on engines in test beds\nAware of Final assembly lines of Automobiles/Farm machinery along with Engine Lines experience is must.\nKnowledge of Basic assembly process like Tightening, floats, sealant application, Alignment, Bearing pressing, Various testing equipment along with conceptualization for any special requirements\nBasic knowledge of Industrial engineering like Line balancing, Work content measurement, Takt, NVA identification, VSM, Productivity improvement, Manpower estimation.\nPrepare, execute & impart training to manufacturing/QA for new model assembly process.\nEstablish & monitor assembly process during Gen-1/Gen-2/Seeding/Pilot batches.\nAudits of processes and system during SOVP & support for APPAP closure\nPlanning & Execution of New hot testing set up. should have worked in Engine MFG line in either- Farm equipment’s, or Supplier, Special Knowledge of CRDI technology and testing practices is must.\nPreparation of RFQ, scope, Technical Finalization of testing Equipment.\nPreparation of Budget, RFQ, Comparison of suppliers, Requisition documents preparation, Planning and coordinating of Trials at supplier end and commissioning in House.\nCreation of gateway documents. Hands on experience on making of Process sheets, PFA, SOP PFMEA, and digitization of assembly process along with various assembly tools like DC nut runners, preload measurement, Oil seal and bearing pressing etc. Preparation of Process FMEA, PFD, Control Plans & SOP for new models\nProject Management for Engine Testing Readiness.\nEngine Test bed proving out with co-relation trials & handover to the user.\nSupport Production Team for Ramp Up.\nGreen & Brown field experience of facility required\nTesting Equipment & Practices:\nCNG/CRDI system testing and conceptualization of special requirements\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nShould have knowledge of Manufacturing process design Plant layouts preparation, Design & development of assembly processes.\nExp in machine procurement & REQ\nShould have knowledge of Installation and commissioning of assembly, testing Equipment.\nSound Knowledge of Engine MFG processes, Designing & Planning\nExperience in DCP preparation, PFMEA updation & review mechanism, RPN reduction\nKnowledge of Advanced technologies\nBOM handling\nHands on experience in SAP, Team centre handling',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Pune-Dy_-Manager-NPME-Engine-Nagp/1418089300','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=100','2026-10-13T12:16:06.790508+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','879501d236ce5c8b20b2fceb5d2e3d043219a84d579d1958ea99731055028d1c','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Pune-Dy_-Manager-NPME-Engine-Nagp/1418089300','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Dy. Manager - NPME Engine\", \"location\": \"Pune, Nagpur Plant, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\", \"General Requirements\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:14.182346',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:14.181064',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:14.181064',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platform/bootstrap/3.4.8_NES/css/bootstrap.min.css\" />\n                            <link type