is & benchmarking\\\\nVehicle System wise NC\\\\nProcess refinement based on field inputs\\\\nRecord all product & process deviation\\\\nShortage Management system establishment\\\\nPokyoke, Traceability, Traveller card adherence, Data management system\\\\nCompliance & Quality Systems\\\", \\\"Compliance & Quality Systems\\\": \\\"Ensure compliance with IATF 16949, ISO 9001, VDA, IMS, QMS or applicable quality standards.\\\\nSupport internal, customer, and certification audits.\\\\nMaintain audit records and documentation.\\\\nData Analysis & Reporting\\\", \\\"Data Analysis & Reporting\\\": \\\"Analyze audit findings and quality trends.\\\\nPrepare management reports and audit scorecards.\\\\nRecommend process improvements based on audit outcomes.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"3-8 years of experience in Process Quality, Internal Audits, Manufacturing Quality, or Supplier Quality\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Experience in automotive/manufacturing industry preferred.\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"Process auditing techniques\\\\nRoot Cause Analysis (5 Why, Fishbone, 8D)\\\\nCAPA management\\\\nStatistical tools and quality methodologies\\\\nReport writing and documentation\\\\nMS Excel and PowerPoint proficiency\\\\nStrong communication and stakeholder management skills\\\\nAnalytical thinking\\\\nAttention to detail\\\\nProblem-solving ability\\\\nIntegrity and objectivity\\\\nTeam collaboration\\\\nContinuous improvement mindset\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"At Mahindra and Mahindra Limited, we believe that diversity drives innovation, and inclusion is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to cultivating a workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.\\\\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to age, caste, race, religion, color, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital or domestic partnership status, pregnancy or childbirth, veteran status, citizenship status, ancestry, financial status, or any other personal characteristic protected by applicable law.\\\\nWe actively encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply and bring their unique perspectives to our teams. We are committed to ensuring an accessible and inclusive experience for all applicants.\\\\nTogether, we rise by embracing differences and building a future that reflects the communities we serve.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nAutomotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chakan, Chakan, IN','Manager BEV Chakan'),(5874,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_5ecb88acc560','Lead Engineer - Gasoline Calibration',NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Chennai-MRV-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\na) Gasoline engine Optimization involving activities like, steady state performance and emission developement, including but not limited to combustion system, injection system, exhaust after-treatment system.\nb) Gasoline vehicle calibration involving, vehicle emission developement, vehicle calibration, drivability, environmental corrections, cold start and OBD\nc)  Emission & Performance Robustness and homologation trials for engines type approval.\nd) Develop competency  on methologies and tools calibration development\ne) Laise with EMS supplier and other key system suppliers for system selection and optimization.\nf) Laise with CFT like Vehicle Integration, NVH, Electricals, Performance simulation, Engine development centre, Reliability and Service for engineering targets delivery.\ng) Plan for the day-today calibration activities and maintain a project tracker.\n