ad, Hyderabad, IN','Deputy Manager Sales'),(5878,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_bb298efec321','Manager - Civil Infrastructure',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN','Nagpur Plant','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nMaintenance of Equipment:\nOversee the maintenance and repair of shop equipment such as conveyors, belts, motors, DC tools, presses, filtration systems, test beds, dispensary units, and cleaning machines.\nEnsure all equipment operates efficiently with minimal downtime.\nConduct routine inspections and preventive maintenance to avoid breakdowns.\nPLC Knowledge:\nUtilize knowledge of Programmable Logic Controllers (PLC) from Mitsubishi and Siemens for troubleshooting and programming.\nPerform diagnostics and ensure smooth operation of automated systems.\nCollaborate with automation experts to optimize PLC-based systems.\nProject Management:\nWork on projects related to installation, modification, and optimization of shop equipment.\nCoordinate with vendors and suppliers for procurement and installation of new machinery or upgrades.\nEnsure timely completion of maintenance projects within budget.\nTeam Leadership & Coordination:\nLead a team of maintenance technicians and allocate tasks effectively.\nCollaborate with production and quality teams to ensure seamless operations.\nProvide technical guidance to the team and train them on equipment handling and maintenance procedures.\nCompliance & Safety:\nEnsure all maintenance activities comply with safety regulations and company standards.\nPromote a safe working environment and enforce safety protocols.\nAddress any hazards or risks associated with equipment promptly.\nDocumentation & Reporting:\nMaintain accurate records of maintenance schedules, repairs, and equipment downtime.\nPrepare reports for management on equipment performance, maintenance activities, and improvement plans.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Manager-Civil-Infrastructure-Nagp/1377270100','https://