", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=360\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Manager - Civil Infrastructure\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1377270100\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Nagpur-Manager-Civil-Infrastructure-Nagp/1377270100/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Manager-Civil-Infrastructure-Nagp/1377270100/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1377270100\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur Plant, IN','Manager - Civil Infrastructure'),(5879,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_b6a51ceda0e2','Senior Engineer',NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Chennai-MRV-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1) Integrating various system designs in a vehicle while ensuring optimal cost, quality and performance.\n2) Developing preliminary system design concepts to meet interface, functional, durability and performance requirements.\n3) Working Collaboratively with various system design teams, simulation team, safety team, homologation team and others to ensure all systems get integrated optimally in vehicle package.\n4) to conduct benchmarking from interface design, system design and integration perspective and get best practices adopted in vehicle systems\n5) To verify, monitor and resolve vehicle package interface open points and Bill of materials (BOM).\n6) To verify, monitor and resolve potential vehicle build/assembly concerns using CATIA/TC-Visualization/other DMU tools in collaboration with manufacturing team.To verify 7) Serviceability, accessibility & maintainability (SAM)of system designs using CATIA/TC-Visualization/other DMU tools\n8) Carrying out DR’s, Interface-DFMEA with CFT\n11) To prepare system design change content for complete vehicle, technical report detailing various options along with decision matrices, periodic updates for project team and management.\n9) To ensure that through out project execution, overall vehicle architecture, ergonomics, cost, weight, quality is not compromised.\n10) To study the product change requests from product planning and prepare design options, change matrix to help management take decisions.\n12) to work with costing and component development team to verify over all product cost and investments with respect to proposed design changes.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E/B.Tech/M.Tech Mechanical/Automobile Engineering',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Senior-Engineer-Chen/1424794000','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=240','2026-10-13T12:16:09.690616+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','575adce84315a2ebf91fecad30608230a5bc4c74e951c23ff1fd92b7b2731c73','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Senior-Engineer-Chen/1424794000','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Senior Engineer\", \"location\": \"Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\", \"Functional Competencies\", \"Behavioural Competencies\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:25.230803',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:25.226151',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:25.226151',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-