y http https india industry information innovation instagram investors jobs know leadership learn listed mahindra mahindrarise marazzo marketplace media mobility motor news october outreach overview people performance plant presence press previous programmes purpose read real releases reports resources responsibility results rise room services social sport statistics steel stories sustainability tech technology trails twitter users valley video views visit watch wheelers work world youtube\" />\n\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta prefix=\"og: http://ogp.me/ns#\" property=\"og:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Mahindra Careers\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd is a billion-dollar global enterprise headquartered in India with operations spanning over 21 industries in more than 100 countries.\" />\n                <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/fed09ea3-5cdb-4e2b-a362-c.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/customHeader.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/sitebuilderframework.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/BS3ColumnizedSearch.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/fontawesome4.7/css/font-awesome-4.7.0.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n<style>\nbody > .modal-backdrop {\n    display: none !important;\n}\n.menu.desktop .nav > li .dropdown-menu li a{ color : white !important}\n#header .links a{ color: white !important;}\n.dropdown-menu.company-dropdown.headerdropdown.backgroundcolordc8b140b5a119dc3 .menu{ color : black !important}\n.custom-header-menu .nav.nav-pills{ width: 807px !important; }\n.custom-header-signinLanguage .inner.limitwidth{ max-width: 1200px; }\n.customPlugin{ margin-bottom: 0 !important; }\n\n</style>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\"></script></body>\n\n        \n        <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/9349339a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'Chennai',1,'2026-10-13T12:16:09.690616+00:00','1424794000',NULL,NULL,'B.E/B.Tech/M.Tech Mechanical/Automobile Engineering',NULL,'1) Integrating various system designs in a vehicle while ensuring optimal cost, quality and performance.\n2) Developing preliminary system design concepts to meet interface, functional, durability and performance requirements.\n3) Working Collaboratively with various system design teams, simulation team, safety team, homologation team and others to ensure all systems get integrated optimally in vehicle package.\n4) to conduct benchmarking from interface design, system design and integration perspective and get best practices adopted in vehicle systems\n5) To verify, monitor and resolve vehicle package interface open points and Bill of materials (BOM).\n6) To verify, monitor and resolve potential vehicle build/assembly concerns using CATIA/TC-Visualization/other DMU tools in collaboration with manufacturing team.To verify 7) Serviceability, accessibility & maintainability (SAM)of system designs using CATIA/TC-Visualization/other DMU tools\n8) Carrying out DR’s, Interface-DFMEA with CFT\n11) To prepare system design change content for complete vehicle, technical report detailing various options along with decision matrices, periodic updates for project team and management.\n9) To ensure that through out project execution, overall vehicle architecture, ergonomics, cost, weight, quality is not compromised.\n10) To study the product change requests from product planning and prepare design options, change matrix to help management take decisions.\n12) to work with costing and component development team to verify over all product cost and investments with respect to proposed design changes.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"1) Integrating various system designs in a vehicle while ensuring optimal cost, quality and performance.\\\\n2) Developing preliminary system design concepts to meet interface, functional, durability and performance requirements.\\\\n3) Working Collaboratively with various system design teams, simulation team, safety team, homologation team and others to ensure all systems get integrated optimally in vehicle package.\\\\n4) to conduct benchmarking from interface design, system design and integration perspective and get best practices adopted in vehicle systems\\\\n5) To verify, monitor and resolve vehicle package interface open points and Bill of materials (BOM).\\\\n6) To verify, monitor and resolve potential vehicle build/assembly concerns using CATIA/TC-Visualization/other DMU tools in collaboration with manufacturing team.To verify 7) Serviceability, accessibility & maintainability (SAM)of system designs using CATIA/TC-Visualization/other DMU tools\\\\n8) Carrying out DR\\\\u2019s, Interface-DFMEA with CFT\\\\n11) To prepare system design change content for complete vehicle, technical report detailing various options along with decision matrices, periodic updates for project team and management.\\\\n9) To ensure that through out project execution, overall vehicle architecture, ergonomics, cost, weight, quality is not compromised.\\\\n10) To study the product change requests from product planning and prepare design options, change matrix to help management take decisions.\\\\n12) to work with costing and component development team to verify over all product cost and investments with respect to proposed design changes.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"Minimum 3+ years in field of Vehicle Integration/vehicle Architecture/Ergonomics/DMU\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\">OEM\'s dealing in Passenger Cars & SUV\'s\\\\n>Service Providers to OEM\'s\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E/B.Tech/M.Tech Mechanical/Automobile Engineering\\\", \\\"Functional Competencies\\\": \\\"1) \\\\u00a0 \\\\u00a0 Must have prior experience in Vehicle integration or Vehicle Architecture of passenger cars/SUV\'s\\\\n2) Basic knowledge of regulatory requirements related to passenger vehicles\\\\n3) Basic knowledge of vehicle architecture and ergonomics\\\\n4) \\\\u00a0 \\\\u00a0 Knowledge of Interface DFMEA/DVP/DFM/DFA/DFS, GD&T\\\\n5) \\\\u00a0 \\\\u00a0 knowledge of critical design/functional requirements of powertrain and other vehicle systems\\\\n6) \\\\u00a0 \\\\u00a0 Basic knowledge on FEA,CFD and NVH tools/techniques required to optimize vehicle systems\\\\n7) \\\\u00a0 \\\\u00a0 Basic knowledge of manufacturing processes (blow moulding, injection moulding, extrusion, plastic welding;Sheet metal working, welding, metal casting, metal forging and prototyping techniques)\\\\n8) \\\\u00a0 \\\\u00a0 Knowledge of basics of cost and investment drivers to enable vehicle/system optimization\\\\n9) Skills in benchmarking and competitive analysis\\\\n10) Preferable to possess passenger car driving skills and valid license\\\\n11) must proficiency in CATIA/3DS, TC-Visualization and equivalent CAD tools.\\\", \\\"Behavioural Competencies\\\": \\\"1. Good communication skills & Good team player\\\\n2. Ability to work effectively in cross functional team.\\\\n3. Comfortable with multitasking and prioritizing tasks\\\\n4. Should be proactive, be open minded and with positive attitude.\\\\n4. Self driven, willingness to learn new skills.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"At Mahindra and Mahindra Limited, we believe that diversity drives innovation, and inclusion is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to cultivating a workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.\\\\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to age, caste, race, religion, color, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital or domestic partnership status, pregnancy or childbirth, veteran status, citizenship status, ancestry, financial status, or any other personal characteristic protected by applicable law.\\\\nWe actively encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply and bring their unique perspectives to our teams. We are committed to ensuring an accessible and inclusive experience for all applicants.\\\\nTogether, we rise by embracing differences and building a future that reflects the communities we serve.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nManufacturing Engineer, CAD, Welding, Drafting, Engineering, Manufacturing, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Senior Engineer'),(5880,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_13fbc1cde325','Strategic Sourcing - Vehicle Proprietary',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN','MUM-KND-AFS(A