ments.\nLead and coordinate regular safety inspections, audits, and workplace walkthroughs to identify areas of improvement and enforce corrective actions.\nInvestigate all accidents, incidents, and near misses promptly, perform root cause analysis, and recommend preventive measures to avoid recurrence.\nOrganise and deliver frequent health, safety, and environment training sessions to all employees, fostering a proactive safety culture and raising awareness of SHE protocols.\nDrive behavioural safety initiatives encouraging employees to safely report unsafe acts, unsafe conditions, and near misses without fear of reprisal.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to establish and achieve sustainability targets focusing on energy conservation, waste minimisation, and water usage reduction.\nOversee and verify adherence to the Permit to Work (PTW) system for all maintenance and production activities requiring formal permission.\nPartner with operational teams to perform ongoing risk assessments of new and existing processes, ensuring all changes undergo Management of Change (MOC) procedures before implementation.\nDevelop, review, and update Safety Operating Procedures (SOPs) aligned with current regulatory standards and operational best practices.\nIdentify, assess, and help prevent hazards specific to plant operations and manufacturing activities.\nMaintain accurate safety documentation including records of inspections, audits, training, incident investigations, and compliance reports.\nCompile and analyse safety performance data, metrics and statistics to generate reports supporting continuous improvement initiatives.\nPromote open communication and employee engagement in safety matters at all levels within the organisation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Support the ongoing development and enhancement of the Health, Safety and Environment (HSE) management systems to ensure compliance with OHSAS 18001 and ISO 14001 standards.\\\\nAssist in implementing the HSE strategy across the manufacturing project to promote a safe and healthy workplace.\\\\nConduct comprehensive risk assessments to identify potential hazards and implement mitigation measures across all operational processes.\\\\nEnsure strict compliance with all statutory safety regulations as well as client-specific safety guidelines and requirements.\\\\nLead and coordinate regular safety inspections, audits, and workplace walkthroughs to identify areas of improvement and enforce corrective actions.\\\\nInvestigate all accidents, incidents, and near misses promptly, perform root cause analysis, and recommend preventive measures to avoid recurrence.\\\\nOrganise and deliver frequent health, safety, and environment training sessions to all employees, fostering a proactive safety culture and raising awareness of SHE protocols.\\\\nDrive behavioural safety initiatives encouraging employees to safely report unsafe acts, unsafe conditions, and near misses without fear of reprisal.\\\\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to establish and achieve sustainability targets focusing on energy conservation, waste minimisation, and water usage reduction.\\\\nOversee and verify adherence to the Permit to Work (PTW) system for all maintenance and production activities requiring formal permission.\\\\nPartner with operational teams to perform ongoing risk assessments of new and existing processes, ensuring all changes undergo Management of Change (MOC) procedures before implementation.\\\\nDevelop, review, and update Safety Operating Procedures (SOPs) aligned with current regulatory standards and operational best practices.\\\\nIdentify, assess, and help prevent hazards specific to plant operations and manufacturing activities.\\\\nMaintain accurate safety documentation including records of inspections, audits, training, incident investigations, and compliance reports.\\\\nCompile and analyse safety performance data, metrics and statistics to generate reports supporting continuous improvement initiatives.\\\\nPromote open communication and employee engagement in safety matters at all levels within the organisation.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"Applicants should possess a relevant educational background, typically a Diploma or Bachelor\'s degree in Mechanical or Electrical Engineering disciplines. Qualifications include but are not limited to:\\\\nDiploma in Mechanical Engineering\\\\nBachelor of Technology (B.Tech) in Mechanical Engineering\\\\nDiploma in Electrical Engineering\\\\nBachelor of Technology (B.Tech) in Electrical Engineering or related field\\\\nAcademic credentials reflecting a solid understanding of engineering fundamentals are essential to effectively comprehend and address the technical and safety challenges encountered in a manufacturing and industrial production environment.\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"The ideal candidate will have between 3 to 5 years of professional experience, with a minimum of 2 years in large-scale manufacturing or chemical industry settings. This experience should demonstrate the ability to apply health, safety, and environmental best practices in complex industrial operations.\\\\nExperience working within safety management frameworks such as OHSAS 18001 and ISO 14001 is highly beneficial, as is familiarity with conducting hazard analyses, risk assessments, and incident investigations on an operational scale.\\\\nProven capability to collaborate effectively with multidisciplinary teams in a fast-paced manufacturing environment is expected.\\\\nExposure to sustainability initiatives including energy efficiency, waste reduction, and resource conservation will be considered advantageous.\\\", \\\"Critical Experience\\\": \\\"There are no specific critical experience requirements identified beyond the general experience criteria. However, a strong commitment to continuous learning and compliance with evolving health and safety legislation is essential for success in this role.\\\\nCandidates demonstrating adaptability, attention to detail, and proactive safety leadership will be highly regarded.\\\", \\\"System Generated Secondary Skills\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nElectrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineer, Electrical, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Zaheerabad\", \"title\": \"Safety Officer\", \"location\": \"Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-FD, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=400\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Safety Officer\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1434266700\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Zaheerabad-Safety-Officer-Zahe/1434266700/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-FD, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Zaheerabad-Safety-Officer-Zahe/1434266700/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1434266700\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-FD, IN','Safety Officer'),(5887,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_0229f6408f66','Asst. Manager-Paint PU-Production',NULL,NULL,'Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-AD, IN','Zaheerabad-AD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nResponsible for:',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Zaheerabad-Asst_-Manager-Paint-PU-Production-Zahe/1434241900','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=280','2026-10-13T12:16:13.032974+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','d506e4c6958b9f69130368f34caddb85178b1b3a2416180ce15544c31ad0e8fe','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Zaheerabad-Asst_-Manager-Paint-P