, IN','MUM-KND-AFS(AD)','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ROLE & PURPOSE:\nTo manage freight rate masters, route evaluation, and cost analysis for finished vehicle outbound logistics, ensuring accurate SAP data maintenance, budget planning, and MIS reporting to support cost-effective and efficient vehicle distribution across India.\nKey Responsibilities\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nManage freight rate masters, route evaluations, and commercial approvals.\nAnalyze freight costs and support budgeting for freight, revenue, and logistics capex.\nMonitor freight spend, transit performance, and operational KPIs through MIS and dashboards.\nSupport vehicle dispatch planning and coordinate with Sales Planning, Plant, and Stockyard teams for timely deliveries.\nReview transit times, identify delays, and drive route and network optimization initiatives.\nTrack and monitor transporter SLAs covering TAT, vehicle availability, damages, and compliance.\nConduct transporter performance reviews and support vendor empanelment, renewals, and negotiations.\nEvaluate road, rail, and multimodal transport options to improve cost and service efficiency.\nManage transit damage claims, statutory compliance, and audit documentation.\nCoordinate with stockyards and C&F partners on inventory ageing, space utilization, and dispatch priorities.\nPrepare management reports on freight spend, budget variances, SLA performance, and logistics metrics.Maintain data integrity and master records in SAP, Power BI, and operational databases.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-A_O-Deputy-Manager-Outbound-Logistics%2C-HO-MUM/1434313600','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=280','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','98aaad00aae3fe1b89d5398e33137d9c53aafedc2343f898cae47379463ff8c8','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-A_O-Deputy-Manager-Outbound-Logistics%2C-HO-MUM/1434313