nd support budgeting for freight, revenue, and logistics capex.\nMonitor freight spend, transit performance, and operational KPIs through MIS and dashboards.\nSupport vehicle dispatch planning and coordinate with Sales Planning, Plant, and Stockyard teams for timely deliveries.\nReview transit times, identify delays, and drive route and network optimization initiatives.\nTrack and monitor transporter SLAs covering TAT, vehicle availability, damages, and compliance.\nConduct transporter performance reviews and support vendor empanelment, renewals, and negotiations.\nEvaluate road, rail, and multimodal transport options to improve cost and service efficiency.\nManage transit damage claims, statutory compliance, and audit documentation.\nCoordinate with stockyards and C&F partners on inventory ageing, space utilization, and dispatch priorities.\nPrepare management reports on freight spend, budget variances, SLA performance, and logistics metrics.Maintain data integrity and master records in SAP, Power BI, and operational databases.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,'To manage freight rate masters, route evaluation, and cost analysis for finished vehicle outbound logistics, ensuring accurate SAP data maintenance, budget planning, and MIS reporting to support cost-effective and efficient vehicle distribution across India.\nKey Responsibilities','\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Job Purpose\\\", \\\"Job Purpose\\\": \\\"To manage freight rate masters, route evaluation, and cost analysis for finished vehicle outbound logistics, ensuring accurate SAP data maintenance, budget planning, and MIS reporting to support cost-effective and efficient vehicle distribution across India.\\\\nKey Responsibilities\\\", \\\"Key Responsibilities\\\": \\\"Manage freight rate masters, route evaluations, and commercial approvals.\\\\nAnalyze freight costs and support budgeting for freight, revenue, and logistics capex.\\\\nMonitor freight spend, transit performance, and operational KPIs through MIS and dashboards.\\\\nSupport vehicle dispatch planning and coordinate with Sales Planning, Plant, and Stockyard teams for timely deliveries.\\\\nReview transit times, identify delays, and drive route and network optimization initiatives.\\\\nTrack and monitor transporter SLAs covering TAT, vehicle availability, damages, and compliance.\\\\nConduct transporter performance reviews and support vendor empanelment, renewals, and negotiations.\\\\nEvaluate road, rail, and multimodal transport options to improve cost and service efficiency.\\\\nManage transit damage claims, statutory compliance, and audit documentation.\\\\nCoordinate with stockyards and C&F partners on inventory ageing, space utilization, and dispatch priorities.\\\\nPrepare management reports on freight spend, budget variances, SLA performance, and logistics metrics.Maintain data integrity and master records in SAP, Power BI, and operational databases.\\\", \\\"Education Qualification\\\": \\\"Graduate/Postgraduate in Supply Chain, Logistics, Commerce, or related field\\\\n3 years of experience in outbound/finished vehicle logistics in automotive or related industry\\\\nPrior exposure to SAP and Power BI is mandatory/preferred\\\", \\\"General Experience\\\": \\\"Advanced Excel skills\\\\nStrong proficiency in Power BI (dashboard creation, DAX, data modeling)\\\\nWorking knowledge of SAP, particularly logistics/freight-related modules\\\\nSound understanding of Indian geography (states, districts, regional transport corridors) relevant to vehicle dispatch planning\\\\nIndustry knowledge of outbound automotive/vehicle logistics (carriers, modes \\\\u2014 rail/road, transporter ecosystem)\\\\nAnalytical mindset with attention to detail for cost computations and SLA tracking\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nAutomotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Mumbai A.O\", \"title\": \"Deputy Manager - Outbound Logistics, HO\", \"location\": \"Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=400\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Deputy Manager - Outbound Logistics, HO\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1434313600\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Mumbai-A_O-Deputy-Manager-Outbound-Logistics%2C-HO-MUM/1434313600/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-A_O-Deputy-Manager-Outbound-Logistics%2C-HO-MUM/1434313600/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1434313600\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mumbai A.O, MUM-KND-AFS(AD), IN','Deputy Manager - Outbound Logistics, HO'),(5889,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_e66bffd6ee13','Dy.Manager - ER & D  FD ZHB',NULL,NULL,'Zaheerabad, Zaheerabad-FD, IN','Zaheerabad-FD','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\n1. Build cordial industrial relations with Union and Plant ER Teams.\n2. Ensure ER network and strong communication channels in the interest of Organization.\n3. Coordinate with plants in implementation of policies and procedures rolled out from Central Team.\n4. Readiness on Monthly review presentation, Policy drafting, Process Audit preparation and need based routine work\n5. In planning and execution of annual compliance audits at plant and Area Offices for process improvements measures and ensure compliances.\n6. Planning and execution of various employee engagement events arranged by Central ER team.\n7. Manage Compliances and extend support for AO locations (Pan India) on compliance issues to Commercial staff, as well as closure of notices / inspections reports issued by Govt. authorities.\n8. Compliances - Collation of data from respective stake holders and signoff of compliance certificate within time lines.\n9. Data Management - Collation of data from various stakeholder from plant location and analysis of the same as per need (LTS, Bonus negotiation, Benchmarking etc.).\n10. Analysis of new amendments / Draft amendments in Labour laws and its impact on business and keep DH informed of same.\n11. Liaison with Govt. authorities and external vendors for compliance and ER issues.\n12. To keep a track of changing IR Landscape as a proactive measure.\n13. Budgeting and other activities connected thereof.\n14. Team up with DH during LTS discussions, building scenarios and making out various required drafts.\nExperience\n5 to 7 yrs.\nIndustry Preferred\nQualifications\nMaster of Labour Studies/ Post Graduation in Industrial Relations (LLB will be an added advantage)\nGeneral Requirements\nOur commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\nAt Mahindra and Mahindra Limited, we believe that diversity drives innovation, and inclusion is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to cultivating a workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.\nWe are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to age, caste, race, religion, color, ethnic origin, gender identity, nationality, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, educational background, marital or domestic partnership status, pregnancy or childbirth, veteran status, citizenship status, ancestry, financial status, or any other personal characteristic protected by applicable law.\nWe actively encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply and bring their unique perspectives to our teams. We are committed to ensuring an accessible and inclusive experience for all applicants.\nTogether, we rise by embracing differences and building a future that reflects the communities we serve.'