 href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/fed09ea3-5cdb-4e2b-a362-c.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/customHeader.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/sitebuilderframework.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/BS3ColumnizedSearch.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/fontawesome4.7/css/font-awesome-4.7.0.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n<style>\nbody > .modal-backdrop {\n    display: none !important;\n}\n.menu.desktop .nav > li .dropdown-menu li a{ color : white !important}\n#header .links a{ color: white !important;}\n.dropdown-menu.company-dropdown.headerdropdown.backgroundcolordc8b140b5a119dc3 .menu{ color : black !important}\n.custom-header-menu .nav.nav-pills{ width: 807px !important; }\n.custom-header-signinLanguage .inner.limitwidth{ max-width: 1200px; }\n.customPlugin{ margin-bottom: 0 !important; }\n\n</style>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\"></script></body>\n\n        \n        <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/9349339a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai - Worli',1,'2026-10-13T12:16:35.248223+00:00','1433773700',NULL,NULL,'Financial Acumen:\nExpertise in financial modelling, valuation techniques, and strategic analysis.\nCommunication Skills:\nExceptional communication and presentation skills to articulate complex ideas effectively to leadership and stakeholders.\nLeadership & Project Management:\nStrong leadership, project management, and cross-functional collaboration abilities.\nAdaptability:\nAbility to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic business environment with shifting priorities.\nIndustry Knowledge:\nDeep understanding of competitive landscapes, market trends, and industry dynamics.',NULL,'We are seeking a dynamic leader to drive Mahindra Group’s growth through strategic acquisitions, partnerships, and alliances. This role will involve identifying high-value opportunities, structuring deals, and performing thorough due diligence. As DGM, you will work closely with senior leadership to align deals with long-term business objectives and ensure seamless execution with internal and external stakeholders.\nKey Responsibilities:\nM&A Strategy Development:\nFormulate and drive the group’s M&A strategy, aligning with long-term business goals and growth priorities.\nOpportunity Identification:\nScout for acquisition targets, partnership prospects, and divestiture opportunities that align with strategic priorities.\nDeal Lifecycle Management:\nLead the complete deal process—due diligence, financial modelling, valuation, negotiations, and deal closure.\nCross-Functional Collaboration:\nCoordinate with internal teams (strategy, finance, legal, HR, and operations) to ensure smooth evaluation, execution, and integration.\nStrategic Insights:\nProvide actionable insights to executive leadership on market trends, competitive landscapes, and new business opportunities.\nExternal Stakeholder Management:\nBuild strong relationships with external advisors, investment banks, legal teams, and consultants to streamline deals.\nMarket Research & Business Intelligence:\nStay on top of industry trends and emerging opportunities to shape M&A strategies and corporate investments.\nCorporate Strategy Support:\nAssist with broader strategic initiatives, including joint ventures, strategic investments, and alliances beyond M&A.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"We are seeking a dynamic leader to drive Mahindra Group\\\\u2019s growth through strategic acquisitions, partnerships, and alliances. This role will involve identifying high-value opportunities, structuring deals, and performing thorough due diligence. As DGM, you will work closely with senior leadership to align deals with long-term business objectives and ensure seamless execution with internal and external stakeholders.\\\\nKey Responsibilities:\\\\nM&A Strategy Development:\\\\nFormulate and drive the group\\\\u2019s M&A strategy, aligning with long-term business goals and growth priorities.\\\\nOpportunity Identification:\\\\nScout for acquisition targets, partnership prospects, and divestiture opportunities that align with strategic priorities.\\\\nDeal Lifecycle Management:\\\\nLead the complete deal process\\\\u2014due diligence, financial modelling, valuation, negotiations, and deal closure.\\\\nCross-Functional Collaboration:\\\\nCoordinate with internal teams (strategy, finance, legal, HR, and operations) to ensure smooth evaluation, execution, and integration.\\\\nStrategic Insights:\\\\nProvide actionable insights to executive leadership on market trends, competitive landscapes, and new business opportunities.\\\\nExternal Stakeholder Management:\\\\nBuild strong relationships with external advisors, investment banks, legal teams, and consultants to streamline deals.\\\\nMarket Research & Business Intelligence:\\\\nStay on top of industry trends and emerging opportunities to shape M&A strategies and corporate investments.\\\\nCorporate Strategy Support:\\\\nAssist with broader strategic initiatives, including joint ventures, strategic investments, and alliances beyond M&A.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"7+ years of experience in corporate development, M&A, front-end investment banking, private equity, or similar fields.\\\\nProven success in leading the full M&A process\\\\u2014deal sourcing, due diligence, financial modelling, valuation, and integration.\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"CA or Bachelor\\\\u2019s degree in finance, Business, or a related field (MBA or equivalent advanced degree preferred).\\\", \\\"General Requirements\\\": \\\"Financial Acumen:\\\\nExpertise in financial modelling, valuation techniques, and strategic analysis.\\\\nCommunication Skills:\\\\nExceptional communication and presentation skills to articulate complex ideas effectively to leadership and stakeholders.\\\\nLeadership & Project Management:\\\\nStrong leadership, project management, and cross-functional collaboration abilities.\\\\nAdaptability:\\\\nAbility to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic business environment with shifting priorities.\\\\nIndustry Knowledge:\\\\nDeep understanding of competitive landscapes, market trends, and industry dynamics.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Apply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mumbai - Worli, Mumbai - Worli, IN','DGM - Partnerships & Alliances'),(5895,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_818040ae5ed7','DGM - Content, Storytelling & Thought Leadership',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai - Worli, Mumbai - Worli, IN','Mumbai - Worli','India',NULL,NULL,'Be comfortable engaging with CEOs, senior executives, journalists and subject-matter experts.','Be',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nGroup Storytelling & Media\nDevelop a strong understanding of Mahindra’s businesses, strategies, innovations and impact.\nProactively identify differentiated, newsworthy stories across Group companies.\nPartner with CEOs, leadership and communications teams to build compelling narratives linked to the broader Mahindra purpose.\nDevelop media pitches, story angles, backgrounders and briefing materials, working with media teams to drive earned coverage.\nTrack media and industry conversations to position Mahindra perspectives on relevant issues.\nThought Leadership & Executive Writing\nDevelop compelling thought leadership for Group and business leaders across articles, speeches, interviews, social media and other platforms.\nBuild distinctive leadership voices and perspectives based on individual expertise and communication styles.\nTranslate complex business, technology, economic and societal topics into clear, engaging narratives.\nPrepare leaders for high-profile media interactions and speaking engagements.\nBusiness Narrative Building\nPartner with businesses to understand strategic priorities and articulate what differentiates them.\nDevelop narrative frameworks for businesses, launches, milestones and strategic announcements.\nElevate business stories into broader industry conversations relevant to India, global markets and society.\nResearch & Intelligence\nStay abreast of business, economic, technology, policy and industry developments.\nStrengthen narratives with relevant data, insights, case studies and global perspectives.\nIdentify emerging conversations where Mahindra leaders and businesses can credibly participate.\nEditorial Excellence\nServe as an editorial gatekeeper for Group Communications, sharpening content developed internally and by agencies.\nEnsure communication is\nclear, credible, concise and compelling\n, with minimal corporate jargon.\nMaintain high standards of factual accuracy, grammar and storytelling quality.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nWe are looking for someone who is first and foremost a brilliant writer and storyteller, but who also understands business and media.The ideal candidate will:\nWrite exceptionally well.\nHave a natural instinct for a good story and a strong headline.\nBe able to look at a business development and ask: “So what? Why should anyone care?”\nBe curious enough to understand businesses beyond their press releases and presentations.\nBe able to find the human story behind the corporate story.\nKnow the difference between a communication opportunity and a genuine news story.\nBe comfortable engaging with CEOs, senior executives, journalists and subject-matter experts.\nHave strong editorial judgement and the confidence to challenge weak narratives.\nBe able to simplify complex subjects without losing their substance.\nBe equally comfortable writing a 1,500-word thought-leadership article, a 500-word media pitch, a CEO speech or a 100-word LinkedIn post.\nBe proactive, entrepreneurial and comfortable working in a fast-paced, multi-business environment.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-Worli-DGM-Content%2C-Storytelling-&-Thought-Leadership-Mumb/1433773800','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=320','2026-10-13T12:16:37.205216+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','2dcab8df951c6a0b6aa938a9bb3e18521e289c5ba2ed636098dc02e5e6cccecd','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Mumbai-Worli-DGM-Content%2C-Storytelling-&-Thought-Leadership-Mumb/1433773800','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"DGM - Content, Storytelling & Thought Leadership\", \"location\": \"Mumbai - Worli, Mumbai - Worli, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Key Responsibilities\", \"Experience\", \"General Requirements\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:29.186173',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:29.180333',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:29.180333',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"tex