uild & validation issues\\\\nManaging and tracking of design release, development, validation & field failures\\\\nKnowledge in Optics & CAE Thermal, Vibration & Condensations\\\\nShould have additional knowledge in Wiring harness, Electronics\\\\nReview & release technical specifications & other documentations\\\\nShould have detail knowledge in Optics, CAD packaging & design, DFMEA and GD&T\\\\nMust demonstrate a high degree of problem solving ability, especially in the field of expertise. Usage of \\\\u00a0tools used in \\\\u00a0DFMEA, problem solving tools and techniques and project management tools ,\\\\nFluent in use of personal computer programs such as Access, Excel, Word, Power Point, project etc.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"3 to 5 yrs.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Job Segment:\\\\nElectronics Engineer, Thermal Engineering, CAD, Drafting, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Senior Engineer- VES'),(5911,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_a91fa60a9b19','Senior Lead Engineer- VES',NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Chennai-MRV-AD','India',NULL,NULL,'Deep knowledge and expertise in lighting technologies: Halogen, LED, MFR, Light Guides, Light Blades, Projection systems','Bachelor',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\'Product Ownership & Road mapping\n- Lead the Lighting System\'s Engineering function for assigned vehicle platforms - Own lighting product strategy for assigned platform(s): technology roadmap (LED/micro‑LED, adaptive/matrix, projection, dynamic animations, light signatures), cost, weight, sustainability, and serviceability.\n- Define system architecture (electro‑optical, thermal, mechanical, sealing, EMC/EMI, diagnostics) and interface control (CAN/LIN, power, thermal paths, package space, styling surfaces).\n- Mentor the engineering team fostering innovation and accountability\nDesign & Development\n- Lead the end-to-end product lifecycle for lighting systems – concept, design, validation, industrialization, and launch.\n- Lead concept freeze, package studies, and feasibility with Styling/Vehicle Architecture.\n- Direct detailed design (optics, PCB, heat sinks, lenses, housings, gaskets, vents, brackets) in CATIA, ensuring DfX (DfM/DfA/DfS), tolerance stack‑ups, VA/VE, and design robustness.\n- Oversee photometry & other performance compliance; define target light distributions, performance margins, and derating strategies.\nValidation & Homologation\n- Ensure compliance with global automotive standards (AIS, ECE, SAE, FMVSS).\n- Develop and execute DVP&R for environmental, optical, electrical, EMC/EMI, durability, corrosion, vibration, sealing, thermal and vehicle‑level integration (CAN/LIN comms, diagnostics).\n- Ensure global regulatory compliance (e.g., UNECE, AIS/BIS, SAE/ISO etc.)\nQuality & Risk\n- Drive APQP/PPAP, DFMEA/PFMEA, Control Plan, and 8D resolution; ensure lessons learned reuse and robust problem prevention.\n- Champion traceability for critical components (LED binning, lens material lots, PCB revisions).\nSupplier & Sourcing Leadership\n- Manage supplier partnerships to achieve cost, quality, and delivery targets.\n- Manage Tier‑1/Tier‑2 suppliers; negotiate technology, cost, and timing; define SOW and acceptance criteria.\n- Conduct design reviews, audits, and process capability checks; support tooling and gauge development.\nProgram & Cross‑Functional Leadership\n- Own timelines, budgets, and BOM for lighting commodities; manage EBOM/MBOM alignment.\n- Collaborate with Manufacturing Engineering for line readiness, PFMEA, jigs/fixtures, EOL testing.\n- Interface with After‑Sales for service parts strategy, diagnostics, and repairability.\nInnovation & IP\n- Drive innovation in lighting technologies (LED, Light Projection, OLED, laser, adaptive Lighting, matrix Lighting, smart lighting).\n- Incubate new features (Welcome/Goodbye animations, ADB/Matrix, logo projection, adaptive signatures, OTA‑capable diagnostics) and file patents/IP where applicable.\nSustainability & Compliance\n- Embed recyclability and drive weight and cost reduction.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\n\'Lighting Engineering\n- Deep knowledge and expertise in lighting technologies: Halogen, LED, MFR, Light Guides, Light Blades, Projection systems, adaptive, matrix systems.\n- Lighting Electronics: deep knowledge of driver circuits, control modules, sensors, microcontrollers, LED selection/binning, thermal derating, PCBs, ESD/EMI design and integration with vehicle electrical architecture (CAN/LIN/Ethernet communication, diagnostics, software calibration & EOL test strategies.).\n- Knowledge of optical design -  reflector/projector, light guides, micro‑optics, photometry (luminous flux, intensity, distributions), glare control\n- Knowledge of Thermal & Mechanical design : CFD for heat dissipation, heat sink design, material selection, sealing/venting, vibration and durability.\n- Knowledge of Standards: AIS/BIS, UNECE & FMVSS/SAE standards.\nMethods & Tools\n- Familiarity in CAD tools: CATIA V5/V6; GD&T, tolerance analysis.\n- Familiarity in CAE analysis tools: thermal simulation, basic optical simulation exposure (Ansys Speos, Lucid).\n- Quality: DFMEA/PFMEA, PPAP, Control Plans.\n- Program tools: PLM (Teamcenter, 3DX), requirements management, Jira/MS Project, dashboards.\nManufacturing & Industrialization\n- Injection moulding (optical‑grade lenses, surface quality/flow), coating & metallization (aluminium vacuum metallization).\n- Welding techniques - Laser welding, ultrasonic welding & Hotplate Welding. Sealing/venting processes, potting, conformal coating, PCB assembly.\n- Assembly line design, EOL optical & leakage tests, poka‑yoke.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Senior-Lead-Engineer-VES-Chen/1432843300','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=380','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','9bb9310fa110e70ff029ed90c5b9d0634bbe3be4c3448ffaf0f5526fdaa1f02e','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Senior-Lead-Engineer-VES-Chen/1432843300','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Senior Lead Engineer- VES\", \"location\": \"Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\", \"General Requirements\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:33.105933',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:33.098140',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-8\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n                <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n                        <link type=\"text/css\" class=\"keepscript\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/platform/bootstrap/3.4.8_NES/css/bootstrap.min.css\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/css/j2w/min/bootstrapV3.global.responsive.min.css?h=275f70e9\" />\n                            <link type=\"text/css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/platform/csb/css/navbar-fixed-top.css\" />\n                \n                <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/platform/js/j2w/j2w.fallbacks.js\"></script>\n         