t:\\\\nCAD, Drafting, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN','Sr. Engineer-VIPTIS'),(5913,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_f4e7b11d9df7','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Paint Shop (Civil)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nLead planning, execution, commissioning and operational readiness of civil infrastructure for Paint Shop during the Greenfield project phase and ensure reliable operation, maintenance, compliance and future expansion support of civil assets throughout the facility lifecycle.\nRoles and responsibilities:\nLead planning, execution and commissioning of civil infrastructure works for Paint Shop during the Greenfield project phase, ensuring alignment with project timelines, budget targets and SOP requirements.\nDrive execution of paint shop buildings, chemical storage facilities, ETP/STP interface structures, utility trenches, ventilation support structures, corrosion-resistant civil works, roads, drainage systems and associated infrastructure required for manufacturing operations.\nReview civil layouts, construction drawings, technical specifications and engineering deliverables to ensure compliance with project requirements, statutory regulations and future expansion plans.\nCoordinate with Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Process Engineering, Civil, Mechanical and Electrical teams to ensure infrastructure readiness for equipment installation, commissioning and production ramp-up activities.\nManage consultants, contractors and vendors to achieve project objectives related to safety, quality, cost and delivery while ensuring compliance with approved construction standards and schedules.\nMonitor project progress, construction quality, budget utilization and execution risks, and drive corrective actions to ensure timely completion of project milestones and operational readiness.\nSupport statutory approvals, inspections, environmental compliance requirements, commissioning activities and infrastructure handover prior to Start of Production (SOP).\nEstablish preventive maintenance, asset management and infrastructure reliability systems for buildings, trenches, drainage systems, chemical handling areas and utility structures to support long-term operational requirements.\nDrive civil modifications, facility enhancement projects, capacity expansion initiatives and infrastructure improvements to support future business growth and manufacturing requirements.\nEnsure compliance with safety, environmental and statutory requirements while fostering a culture of operational excellence, cost optimization and continuous improvement.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E./B.Tech Civil Engineering\nJob Segment:\nCivil Engineer, Manufacturing Engineer, Engineer, Process Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager%C2%A0-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Paint-Shop-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422514000','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=400','2026-10-13T12:16:41.032882+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','e8bf5465314b0f15820672d8162499c0cd4de5607e0a39083ae36ff5355bd272','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager%C2%A0-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Paint-Shop-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422514000','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Sr. Manager\\u00a0- Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Paint Shop (Civil)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Re