'India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nLead planning, execution, commissioning and operational readiness of common electrical infrastructure for the Greenfield Automotive Manufacturing Facility and ensure reliable operation, maintenance, compliance, energy efficiency and future expansion support of electrical assets throughout the plant lifecycle.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\nLead planning, execution and commissioning of plant-wide common electrical infrastructure projects during the Greenfield phase, ensuring alignment with project timelines, budget targets and operational readiness requirements.\nDrive development of substations, HT/LT power distribution systems, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems, synchronization systems, street lighting networks and utility power infrastructure across the manufacturing facility.\nReview electrical designs, load calculations, single line diagrams (SLDs), technical specifications and engineering deliverables to ensure compliance with project requirements, statutory regulations and future expansion plans.\nCoordinate with Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Civil, Mechanical, Industrial Engineering and Project teams to ensure seamless integration of common electrical infrastructure and utility systems.\nManage consultants, contractors, vendors and utility service providers to achieve project objectives related to safety, quality, cost and delivery.\nMonitor project progress, budget utilization, installation quality and execution risks, and drive corrective actions to ensure timely completion of project milestones and SOP readiness.\nEstablish preventive maintenance, TPM and reliability improvement systems for substations, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems and power distribution assets to ensure long-term operational reliability.\nMonitor energy consumption, power quality, electrical asset performance and utility KPIs, and drive energy conservation, cost optimization and continuous improvement initiatives.\nEnsure compliance with electrical safety requirements, statutory regulations, inspections, audits and utility-related approvals throughout project and operational phases.\nSupport infrastructure modernization, capacity expansion, utility augmentation and future business growth requirements while ensuring reliable and sustainable power availability across the plant.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E. / B.Tech Electrical Engineering\nJob Segment:\nManufacturing Engineer, Industrial Engineer, Engineer, Electrical Engineering, Engineering, Automotive\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infrastructure-for-Common-Infra-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422520000','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=400','2026-10-13T12:16:42.521484+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','270107a35eb627a3e3a6629c4f2de9d1aaae5336cdd19a39fdff7ec511594329','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infrastructure-for-Common-Infra-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422520000','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for Common Infra (Electrical)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:35.378097',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:35.372722',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:35.372722',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n            <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html;charset=UTF-