ng\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nMachinist, Mechanical Engineer, Engineer, Manufacturing, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Agrregate Shop (Mechanical)'),(5917,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_68d3dd632fba','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for TCF Shop (Mechanical)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nTo support planning, execution, commissioning and maintenance of building, utilities and infrastructure systems for Trim, Chassis & Final (TCF) assembly operations during Greenfield project implementation and plant operations.\nRoles and responsibilities:\nGreenfield Project Phase:\nSupport execution and monitoring of TCF building construction, utility installation and infrastructure development activities, ensuring compliance with project schedules, quality standards and safety requirements.\nCoordinate installation and commissioning of compressed air systems, power distribution interfaces, HVAC systems, water systems, firefighting systems and associated utility infrastructure required for equipment installation and Start of Production (SOP).\nWork closely with Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, Manufacturing Engineering, Production and contractor teams to ensure timely completion of project activities, manufacturing readiness and closure of punch points.\nEnsure adherence to approved drawings, technical specifications, statutory requirements, EHS guidelines and quality standards during project execution and commissioning activities.\nOperations & Facility Management Phase:\nSupport maintenance and upkeep of TCF buildings, utility systems and infrastructure to ensure safe, reliable and uninterrupted manufacturing operations.\nExecute preventive maintenance activities, coordinate breakdown restoration, facility modifications and utility improvement initiatives to enhance equipment availability and operational efficiency.\nMonitor utility consumption, equipment performance, maintenance KPIs and contractor performance, and support implementation of energy management, reliability improvement and cost optimization initiatives.\nCoordinate vendors and AMC service providers, maintain maintenance records and MIS reports, and support expansion projects, statutory compliance activities and EHS requirements.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E./B.Tech Mechanical Engineering\nJob Segment:\nManufacturing Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Construction, Engineer, Electrical, Engineering\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-TCF-Shop-%28Mechanical%29-Nagp/1422517600','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=420','2026-10-13T12:16:41.855826+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','7adb495fdbf410b5ff864a03a8cd62c3e9362fa8beb5ca4485a0e68ae2ed238c','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-TCF-Shop-%28Mechanical%29-Nagp/1422517600','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for TCF Shop (Mechanical)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:35.708142',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:35.704068',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:35.704068',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xht