and TPM systems to ensure uninterrupted utility support after SOP.\nMonitor utility performance, energy consumption and asset reliability and implement improvement initiatives.\nEnsure compliance with statutory requirements, safety standards and environmental regulations.\nSupport future capacity expansion, debottlenecking and utility enhancement projects while developing team capability and continuous improvement culture.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Purpose of the role:\\\\nLead planning, execution, commissioning and operational readiness of Mechanical Utilities, Building Services and Infrastructure for Paint Shop during Greenfield project phase and ensure reliable utility operations, maintenance and capacity enhancement post SOP.\\\\nRoles & Responsibilities:\\\\nLead planning, execution and commissioning of Mechanical Utilities and Infrastructure for Paint Shop.\\\\nEnsure utility readiness for equipment installation, trials, commissioning and SOP.\\\\nCoordinate with Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Quality, Civil and Electrical teams for timely project execution.\\\\nManage contractors, consultants and vendors to achieve project targets related to quality, cost, delivery and safety.\\\\nDrive installation and commissioning of HVAC systems, paint booth utilities, chilled water systems, compressed air systems and utility piping networks.\\\\nEnsure environmental control systems meet process, quality and sustainability requirements of Paint Shop operations.\\\\nEstablish maintenance, reliability and TPM systems to ensure uninterrupted utility support after SOP.\\\\nMonitor utility performance, energy consumption and asset reliability and implement improvement initiatives.\\\\nEnsure compliance with statutory requirements, safety standards and environmental regulations.\\\\nSupport future capacity expansion, debottlenecking and utility enhancement projects while developing team capability and continuous improvement culture.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"10-15 Years in relevant field\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automotive OEM / Auto Component / Industrial Manufacturing /EPC Projects\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E. / B.Tech Mechanical Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nManufacturing Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Electrical, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"job_title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infrastructure for Paint Shop (Mechanical)'),(5919,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_8a5b1e6f5acd','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Electrical)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nTo support planning, execution, commissioning, operation and maintenance of centralized electrical utilities and infrastructure for a Greenfield Automotive Manufacturing Plant, ensuring safe, reliable and energy-efficient power distribution across Press Shop, Body Shop, Paint Shop, TCF, Aggregates, Warehouse and Common Facilities.\nRoles & Responsibilities:\nGreenfield Project Phase:\nSupport planning, execution and monitoring of Common Electrical Infrastructure activities including substations, HT/LT distribution systems, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems, synchronization panels, PCC/MCC panels, cable laying, street lighting and utility power distribution networks.\nCoordinate with consultants, contractors, equipment suppliers and internal stakeholders for utility load planning, installation, testing and commissioning activities to ensure infrastructure readiness for Start of Production (SOP).\nSupport implementation and integration of SCADA, EMS (Energy Management 