MIS reports, while supporting plant expansion projects, infrastructure upgrades and electrical safety compliance activities.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"Purpose of the role:\\\\nTo support planning, execution, commissioning, operation and maintenance of centralized electrical utilities and infrastructure for a Greenfield Automotive Manufacturing Plant, ensuring safe, reliable and energy-efficient power distribution across Press Shop, Body Shop, Paint Shop, TCF, Aggregates, Warehouse and Common Facilities.\\\\nRoles & Responsibilities:\\\\nGreenfield Project Phase:\\\\nSupport planning, execution and monitoring of Common Electrical Infrastructure activities including substations, HT/LT distribution systems, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems, synchronization panels, PCC/MCC panels, cable laying, street lighting and utility power distribution networks.\\\\nCoordinate with consultants, contractors, equipment suppliers and internal stakeholders for utility load planning, installation, testing and commissioning activities to ensure infrastructure readiness for Start of Production (SOP).\\\\nSupport implementation and integration of SCADA, EMS (Energy Management Systems), energy metering systems and other electrical monitoring solutions across the plant infrastructure.\\\\nEnsure adherence to approved drawings, technical specifications, project schedules, statutory requirements, electrical standards and safety guidelines during execution and commissioning activities.\\\\nOperations & Facility Management Phase\\\\nSupport preventive, predictive and breakdown maintenance of substations, transformers, DG sets, UPS systems, switchgear, PCC/MCC panels, street lighting and power distribution systems to ensure uninterrupted utility availability.\\\\nMonitor energy consumption, power quality and equipment health parameters, and support energy conservation, reliability improvement and operational excellence initiatives.\\\\nCoordinate AMC vendors, contractors and service providers, monitor work execution and ensure compliance with quality, safety and delivery requirements.\\\\nMaintain electrical asset records, statutory inspection reports, maintenance history and MIS reports, while supporting plant expansion projects, infrastructure upgrades and electrical safety compliance activities.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"5+ years in electrical utilities, industrial infrastructure, facilities management or plant engineering with exposure to Greenfield automotive, manufacturing or large industrial projects. Experience in Central Utility and Substation operations preferred.\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automobile OEMs, Auto Component Manufacturing, Heavy Engineering, Industrial Manufacturing, EPC Organizations, Utility Infrastructure Companies\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E./B.Tech Electrical Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nElectrical Engineering, Electrical, Warehouse, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive, Manufacturing\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Nagpur\", \"title\": \"Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Electrical)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=520\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Electrical)\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1422515700\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Common-Infra-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422515700/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Dy_-Manager-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Common-Infra-%28Electrical%29-Nagp/1422515700/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1422515700\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Dy. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Electrical)'),(5920,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_30de2659f0d7','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Press & Body Shops (Civil)',NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Nagpur','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,'B.E',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nPurpose of the role:\nLead planning, execution, commissioning and operational readiness of civil infrastructure for Press Shop and Body Shop during the Greenfield project phase and ensure reliable operation, maintenance, compliance and future expansion support of civil assets throughout the facility lifecycle.\nRoles and responsibilities:\nLead planning, execution and commissioning of civil infrastructure works for Press Shop and Body Shop during the Greenfield project phase, ensuring alignment with project timelines, quality standards, budget targets and SOP requirements.\nDrive execution of industrial buildings, press foundations, heavy equipment foundations, crane girder structures, utility trenches, roads, drainage systems and associated infrastructure required for manufacturing operations.\nReview civil designs, layouts, construction drawings, technical specifications and engineering deliverables to ensure compliance with project requirements, statutory regulations and future expansion needs.\nCoordinate with Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Civil, Mechanical, Electrical and Project teams to ensure infrastructure readiness for equipment installation, commissioning and production ramp-up activities.\nManage consultants, contractors and vendors to achieve project objectives related to safety, quality, cost and delivery while ensuring adherence to approved schedules and construction standards.\nMonitor project progress, construction quality, budget utilization and execution risks, and drive corrective actions to ensure timely completion of project milestones.\nSupport statutory approvals, inspections, audits, commissioning activities and infrastructure handover prior to Start of Production (SOP).\nEstablish preventive maintenance, asset management and infrastructure reliability systems for buildings, foundations, roads, drainage systems and utility corridors to support long-term operational requirements.\nDrive civil modifications, facility enhancement projects, debottlenecking initiatives and infrastructure expansion activities in line with future business growth requirements.\nEnsure compliance with safety, environmental and statutory requirements while fostering a culture of operational excellence, cost optimization and continuous improvement.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nB.E./B.Tech Civil Engineering\nJob Segment:\nCivil Engineer, Manufacturing Engineer, Engineer, Electrical, Engineering, Automotive\nApply Now\nStart apply with LinkedIn\nStart\nPlease wait...',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager%C2%A0-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Press-&-Body-Shops-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422514300','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=420','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','d4a61e567e5b8b7b1f8ba856a847967d25073764f04d6deefc20c25dabda8474','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager%C2%A0-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Press-&-Body-Shops-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422514300','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Sr. Manager\\u00a0- Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Press & Body Shops (Civil)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\