s to achieve project objectives related to safety, quality, cost and delivery.\\\\nMonitor project schedules, budgets and execution progress, identify risks and implement corrective actions to ensure timely completion of infrastructure projects.\\\\nCoordinate with Manufacturing Engineering, Production, Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, Industrial Engineering and Project teams to ensure seamless infrastructure integration and operational readiness.\\\\nSupport statutory approvals, regulatory inspections, commissioning activities and infrastructure handover prior to Start of Production (SOP).\\\\nEstablish maintenance, asset management and TPM systems for common infrastructure facilities and utilities to ensure reliability, safety, cost optimization and long-term operational effectiveness after SOP.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"10 - 12 years in industrial construction, infrastructure development and greenfield automotive projects.\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Automobile OEMs, Auto Components, EPC, Industrial Construction, Manufacturing\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"B.E./B.Tech Civil Engineering\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nCivil Engineer, Industrial Engineer, Manufacturing Engineer, Engineer, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"Nagpur\", \"title\": \"Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Civil)\", \"location\": \"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=540\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Sr. Manager\\\\u00a0- Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Civil)\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1422513400\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager%C2%A0-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Common-Infra-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422513400/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"Nagpur, Nagpur, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Nagpur-Sr_-Manager%C2%A0-Building%2C-Utilities-&-Other-Infra-for-Common-Infra-%28Civil%29-Nagp/1422513400/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1422513400\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nagpur, Nagpur, IN','Sr. Manager - Building, Utilities & Other Infra for Common Infra (Civil)'),(5922,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_820a3879ec54','Engineer - PSL',NULL,NULL,'CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN','Cheyyar-MSPT','India',NULL,NULL,'Successful candidates will demonstrate strong communication skills to effectively engage with internal teams and externa','Diploma',NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nAs an Engineer in the Crash Lab at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will be responsible for ensuring optimal uptime and operational readiness of all test equipment critical to automotive testing processes.\nYour key duties will include planning and executing scheduled maintenance, managing calibration cycles in coordination with Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs) and external agencies, and proactively addressing any equipment issues in collaboration with suppliers to ensure timely resolutions.\nYou will oversee procurement planning for essential spares and consumables, ensuring seamless availability to avoid disruption.\nPreparation and configuration of crash instruments and data acquisition systems for various vehicle test scenarios will be a significant aspect of your role.\nFurthermore, you will support suppliers during Installation and Commissioning (I&C) activities, providing technical guidance and ensuring strict adherence to project timelines and quality standards.\nThe role demands a comprehensive understanding of test measuring instruments specific to automotive testing, strong knowledge of automation and electronics, and detailed insights into engine and vehicle components and subsystems.\nA thorough grasp of relevant safety and quality standards, crash regulations, and National Accreditation Board for Testing and Calibration Laboratories (NABL) requirements is essential to maintaining compliance and operational excellence.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS & REQUIREMENTS:\nSuccessful candidates will demonstrate strong communication skills to effectively engage with internal teams and external agencies. A customer-centric approach is essential for managing stakeholder expectations and delivering quality outcomes.\nKey behavioural competencies include sound decision-making capabilities, effective teamwork in multidisciplinary settings, and aptitude for handling and mentoring manpower resources within the lab environment. Adaptability and a proactive approach to problem-solving will support success in this role.',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/CHEYYAR-CC-Engineer-PSL-Chey/1432365200','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=440','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','1d44daa0ee2c4bc526539e8b0fccb46cc0473c44315e23bebf46042810573a53','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/CHEYYAR-CC-Engineer-PSL-Chey/1432365200','d745b4b7d7619bb600dcbb9abbe6fe63',NULL,'{\"title\": \"Engineer - PSL\", \"location\": \"CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN\", \"date\": null, \"function\": null, \"pay_band\": null, \"sections_extracted\": [\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\", \"Experience\", \"Industry Preferred\", \"Qualifications\", \"General Requirements\", \"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\"]}','ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS','2026-10-13 05:21:36.566372',NULL,'2026-10-13 05:21:36.560651',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257',NULL,'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html class=\"html5\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" lang=\"en-GB\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n        <head>\n            <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" />\n      