yle>\nbody > .modal-backdrop {\n    display: none !important;\n}\n.menu.desktop .nav > li .dropdown-menu li a{ color : white !important}\n#header .links a{ color: white !important;}\n.dropdown-menu.company-dropdown.headerdropdown.backgroundcolordc8b140b5a119dc3 .menu{ color : black !important}\n.custom-header-menu .nav.nav-pills{ width: 807px !important; }\n.custom-header-signinLanguage .inner.limitwidth{ max-width: 1200px; }\n.customPlugin{ margin-bottom: 0 !important; }\n\n</style>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\"></script></body>\n\n        \n        <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/9349339a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'CHEYYAR CC',1,'2026-10-13T12:16:43.147029+00:00','1432365200',NULL,NULL,'Successful candidates will demonstrate strong communication skills to effectively engage with internal teams and external agencies. A customer-centric approach is essential for managing stakeholder expectations and delivering quality outcomes.\nKey behavioural competencies include sound decision-making capabilities, effective teamwork in multidisciplinary settings, and aptitude for handling and mentoring manpower resources within the lab environment. Adaptability and a proactive approach to problem-solving will support success in this role.',NULL,'As an Engineer in the Crash Lab at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will be responsible for ensuring optimal uptime and operational readiness of all test equipment critical to automotive testing processes.\nYour key duties will include planning and executing scheduled maintenance, managing calibration cycles in coordination with Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs) and external agencies, and proactively addressing any equipment issues in collaboration with suppliers to ensure timely resolutions.\nYou will oversee procurement planning for essential spares and consumables, ensuring seamless availability to avoid disruption.\nPreparation and configuration of crash instruments and data acquisition systems for various vehicle test scenarios will be a significant aspect of your role.\nFurthermore, you will support suppliers during Installation and Commissioning (I&C) activities, providing technical guidance and ensuring strict adherence to project timelines and quality standards.\nThe role demands a comprehensive understanding of test measuring instruments specific to automotive testing, strong knowledge of automation and electronics, and detailed insights into engine and vehicle components and subsystems.\nA thorough grasp of relevant safety and quality standards, crash regulations, and National Accreditation Board for Testing and Calibration Laboratories (NABL) requirements is essential to maintaining compliance and operational excellence.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"As an Engineer in the Crash Lab at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, you will be responsible for ensuring optimal uptime and operational readiness of all test equipment critical to automotive testing processes.\\\\nYour key duties will include planning and executing scheduled maintenance, managing calibration cycles in coordination with Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs) and external agencies, and proactively addressing any equipment issues in collaboration with suppliers to ensure timely resolutions.\\\\nYou will oversee procurement planning for essential spares and consumables, ensuring seamless availability to avoid disruption.\\\\nPreparation and configuration of crash instruments and data acquisition systems for various vehicle test scenarios will be a significant aspect of your role.\\\\nFurthermore, you will support suppliers during Installation and Commissioning (I&C) activities, providing technical guidance and ensuring strict adherence to project timelines and quality standards.\\\\nThe role demands a comprehensive understanding of test measuring instruments specific to automotive testing, strong knowledge of automation and electronics, and detailed insights into engine and vehicle components and subsystems.\\\\nA thorough grasp of relevant safety and quality standards, crash regulations, and National Accreditation Board for Testing and Calibration Laboratories (NABL) requirements is essential to maintaining compliance and operational excellence.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"The ideal candidate will have substantial experience in automotive testing environments, with 3 to 4 years of relevant experience for degree holders (BE) and a minimum of 7 years for diploma holders in a similar domain. Experience should encompass hands-on involvement with test equipment maintenance, calibration processes, and supplier interactions.\\\\nPrior exposure to R&D, design, or calibration in the automotive sector adds significant value. Proven competency in managing complex instrumentation systems and familiarity with safety and quality assurance protocols in a vehicle testing context will be advantageous.\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"Preferred industry experience includes roles within the automotive sector, particularly in R&D centres, design studios, or calibration teams specializing in vehicle testing and evaluation. Candidates from vehicle testing agencies or recognised automotive research organisations will find this role aligns well with their expertise.\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"Applicants should possess a Diploma or a Bachelor of Engineering (BE) degree majoring in Electronics, Electrical Engineering, or Instrumentation. Academic background must be complemented by practical skills in maintaining and calibrating sophisticated testing equipment within automotive environments.\\\", \\\"General Requirements\\\": \\\"Successful candidates will demonstrate strong communication skills to effectively engage with internal teams and external agencies. A customer-centric approach is essential for managing stakeholder expectations and delivering quality outcomes.\\\\nKey behavioural competencies include sound decision-making capabilities, effective teamwork in multidisciplinary settings, and aptitude for handling and mentoring manpower resources within the lab environment. Adaptability and a proactive approach to problem-solving will support success in this role.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd is committed to fostering an equitable and inclusive workplace where diverse perspectives are valued and nurtured. We actively encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds, regardless of race, gender identity, sexual orientation, ethnicity, disability, or age.\\\\nOur inclusive culture promotes respect, collaboration, and equal opportunities for career growth. We believe diversity stimulates innovation and enriches our collective ability to solve complex automotive challenges while reflecting the diverse communities we serve globally.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nElectronics Engineer, Instrumentation, Electrical Engineering, Electrical, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"CHEYYAR CC\", \"title\": \"Engineer - PSL\", \"location\": \"CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=560\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Engineer - PSL\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1432365200\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/CHEYYAR-CC-Engineer-PSL-Chey/1432365200/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/CHEYYAR-CC-Engineer-PSL-Chey/1432365200/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1432365200\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN','Engineer - PSL'),(5923,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_5e2f09d75832','Sales Manager ILCV & Bus',NULL,NULL,'Rohtak, MTBD-Rohatak, IN','MTBD-Rohatak','India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\nResponsible for Sales Volumes and Market Share of Light Commercial vehicles through local dealers in respective territory.\nTo identify and engage with strategic customers / Fleet owners.To conduct activities of this segment customers like transporters, influencers and to materialize deals by working out group deals.\nTo map sub territories segment wise, application wise and working on conversion plan.Should be able to do sales forecasting for existing range of models / products.To guide channel partners to develop secondary sales network.\nTo act as an interface between the Product development / PMG team and the end customers.To gauge and give inputs regarding the customer expectations through timely reports to product development / PMG team.To know competitors activities, new product plans and prepare strategy to counter the same.\nTo train, motivate and develop the channel partners and their sales team.To develop the market through host of BTL activities most suited for that market and segment',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Rohtak-Sales-Manager-ILCV-&-Bus-MTBD/1432443400','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=440','2026-10-13T12:16:43.870346+00:00','EXPIRED',0.98,'PUBLISHED',NULL,'Crawler (ATS_API_SUCCESSFACTORS)','c93fee034cfc0eac3432de1075ff3a9cc316a650b906c9f4e8de4d55ec9b9c97','COMP_