n#header .links a{ color: white !important;}\n.dropdown-menu.company-dropdown.headerdropdown.backgroundcolordc8b140b5a119dc3 .menu{ color : black !important}\n.custom-header-menu .nav.nav-pills{ width: 807px !important; }\n.custom-header-signinLanguage .inner.limitwidth{ max-width: 1200px; }\n.customPlugin{ margin-bottom: 0 !important; }\n\n</style>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\"></script></body>\n\n        \n        <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"//rmkcdn.successfactors.com/1bf0fd1f/9349339a-5cfe-46bb-98d8-3.png\" type=\"image/x-icon\" />\n            <style id=\"antiClickjack\" type=\"text/css\">body{display:none !important;}</style>\n            <script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"antiClickJackScript\">\n                if (self === top) {\n                    var antiClickjack = document.getElementById(\"antiClickjack\");',NULL,'All populated fields verified against raw source evidence.','STALE',NULL,'SuccessFactors',NULL,NULL,'CHEYYAR CC',1,'2026-10-13T12:16:44.574038+00:00','1432365100',NULL,NULL,'This role requires a well-rounded set of professional and interpersonal skills to ensure effective operation and collaboration within the team and with external stakeholders. Essential general requirements include:\nExcellent communication skills, enabling clear interaction with colleagues, suppliers, and external test agencies.\nStrong customer focus, maintaining responsiveness to internal and external stakeholders for superior service delivery.\nSound decision-making abilities, particularly when resolving technical challenges or operational issues within tight timelines.\nEffective teamwork skills to foster a collaborative work environment and drive collective success.\nExperience in manpower handling and team supervision to manage daily lab operations efficiently.\nRobust time management skills to prioritize multiple tasks and meet stringent deadlines associated with testing schedules.\nThe combination of these skills will empower the candidate to contribute positively to Mahindra & Mahindra’s safety testing initiatives.',NULL,'As an Engineer within the Product Development division at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, based at the Cheyyar-MSPT location, you will play a crucial role in supporting the crash lab operations and ensuring high standards of testing and safety compliance. Your key responsibilities will include:\nProviding technical support to suppliers during Installation and Commissioning (I&C) activities, ensuring smooth transitions and adherence to project timelines.\nUnderstanding and interpreting detailed test requirements to effectively prepare various types of vehicles and components for crash testing.\nOverseeing and maintaining the crash test area, ensuring all procedures follow safety protocols and industry regulations.\nSupporting NABL accreditation processes by meticulously documenting procedures and ensuring compliance with established standards.\nEnsuring continuous uptime of the crash lab facilities by proactively managing equipment maintenance schedules and rapid troubleshooting.\nMonitoring and maintaining the operational readiness of all test equipment, optimizing functionality for reliable test results.\nManaging procurement of spare parts and consumables necessary for the seamless operation of the lab while maintaining budget oversight.\nLiaising with suppliers and external agencies to promptly address any technical issues and facilitate issue resolution.\nPreparing detailed budgets for facility enhancement projects and incorporating emerging technologies to keep the lab at the forefront of automotive safety testing.\nThis role demands proactive collaboration, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to maintaining world-class testing infrastructure to uphold Mahindra & Mahindra\'s reputation for excellence.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FETCHED',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\"{\\\"Responsibilities & Key Deliverables\\\": \\\"As an Engineer within the Product Development division at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, based at the Cheyyar-MSPT location, you will play a crucial role in supporting the crash lab operations and ensuring high standards of testing and safety compliance. Your key responsibilities will include:\\\\nProviding technical support to suppliers during Installation and Commissioning (I&C) activities, ensuring smooth transitions and adherence to project timelines.\\\\nUnderstanding and interpreting detailed test requirements to effectively prepare various types of vehicles and components for crash testing.\\\\nOverseeing and maintaining the crash test area, ensuring all procedures follow safety protocols and industry regulations.\\\\nSupporting NABL accreditation processes by meticulously documenting procedures and ensuring compliance with established standards.\\\\nEnsuring continuous uptime of the crash lab facilities by proactively managing equipment maintenance schedules and rapid troubleshooting.\\\\nMonitoring and maintaining the operational readiness of all test equipment, optimizing functionality for reliable test results.\\\\nManaging procurement of spare parts and consumables necessary for the seamless operation of the lab while maintaining budget oversight.\\\\nLiaising with suppliers and external agencies to promptly address any technical issues and facilitate issue resolution.\\\\nPreparing detailed budgets for facility enhancement projects and incorporating emerging technologies to keep the lab at the forefront of automotive safety testing.\\\\nThis role demands proactive collaboration, meticulous attention to detail, and a commitment to maintaining world-class testing infrastructure to uphold Mahindra & Mahindra\'s reputation for excellence.\\\", \\\"Experience\\\": \\\"The ideal candidate will bring 3 to 4 years of practical experience in a related field if holding a Bachelor of Engineering degree, or a minimum of 7 years if holding a Diploma, particularly within automotive crash testing or automotive safety validation domains.\\\\nEssential technical expertise and knowledge areas include:\\\\nComprehensive understanding of vehicle architecture and the integration of mechanical systems within modern automotive platforms.\\\\nProfound knowledge of hydraulic systems relevant to crash testing and vehicle safety mechanisms.\\\\nFamiliarity with NABL accreditation standards and the processes involved in maintaining accreditation compliance.\\\\nHands-on experience with the tools and equipment commonly used in vehicle workshops and crash laboratories to conduct accurate and safe testing.\\\\nAwareness and application of automotive safety and quality standards to ensure all procedures and outputs meet regulatory and company benchmarks.\\\\nIn-depth knowledge of crash safety regulations, ensuring that all testing aligns with national and international requirements.\\\\nDirect experience with Crash and SLED testing methodologies, including test setup, execution, and data analysis.\\\\nAdditional competencies such as problem-solving skills, analytical thinking, and adaptability to evolving safety technologies are highly valued.\\\", \\\"Industry Preferred\\\": \\\"We prefer candidates with backgrounds in the following industries, where specialized knowledge of vehicle safety, testing protocols, and automotive design is paramount:\\\\nAutomotive Industry with experience in Research & Development (R&D), Design, or Calibration departments.\\\\nAutomotive Testing Agencies such as Automotive Research Association of India (ARAI) and International Centre for Automotive Technology (ICAT), where rigorous testing standards are maintained.\\\\nCandidates from these sectors will bring valuable insights into industry best practices and a strong understanding of vehicle safety testing standards.\\\", \\\"Qualifications\\\": \\\"Applicants should possess the following educational qualifications to be considered for this position:\\\\nA Diploma or Bachelor of Engineering (BE) degree, majoring in Mechanical or Automotive Engineering from a recognized institution.\\\\nThe educational foundation should equip the candidate with core engineering principles, supplemented by specialized knowledge in automotive systems and safety engineering.\\\", \\\"General Requirements\\\": \\\"This role requires a well-rounded set of professional and interpersonal skills to ensure effective operation and collaboration within the team and with external stakeholders. Essential general requirements include:\\\\nExcellent communication skills, enabling clear interaction with colleagues, suppliers, and external test agencies.\\\\nStrong customer focus, maintaining responsiveness to internal and external stakeholders for superior service delivery.\\\\nSound decision-making abilities, particularly when resolving technical challenges or operational issues within tight timelines.\\\\nEffective teamwork skills to foster a collaborative work environment and drive collective success.\\\\nExperience in manpower handling and team supervision to manage daily lab operations efficiently.\\\\nRobust time management skills to prioritize multiple tasks and meet stringent deadlines associated with testing schedules.\\\\nThe combination of these skills will empower the candidate to contribute positively to Mahindra & Mahindra\\\\u2019s safety testing initiatives.\\\", \\\"Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion\\\": \\\"At Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, we are deeply committed to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workplace where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to contribute to their fullest potential.\\\\nWe actively promote hiring practices that attract a broad spectrum of talent, reflecting a wide array of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We believe that diversity drives innovation and excellence and are dedicated to creating an environment free from discrimination, bias, and barriers.\\\\nOur policies support equal opportunity for all applicants and employees, encouraging applications from candidates of all identities, abilities, and communities. Joining our team means becoming part of an organisation that values collaboration, transparency, and social responsibility at every level.\\\\nWe continuously invest in diversity and inclusion initiatives, training, and community engagement programs to ensure our workplace evolves into an even more welcoming and supportive space for everyone.\\\\nJob Segment:\\\\nR&D Engineer, Engineer, Safety Engineer, Hydraulics, Engineering, Automotive\\\\nApply Now\\\\nStart apply with LinkedIn\\\\nStart\\\\nPlease wait...\\\"}\"',NULL,NULL,'OWNED',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-17 12:30:19.260257','{\"city\": \"CHEYYAR CC\", \"title\": \"Engineer - PSL\", \"location\": \"CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN\", \"source_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/search/?q=&startrow=560\", \"ats_platform\": \"SuccessFactors\", \"evidence_text\": \"{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Engineer - PSL\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"1432365100\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"/job/CHEYYAR-CC-Engineer-PSL-Chey/1432365100/\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\"CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN\\\"}\", \"detail_fetched\": false, \"application_url\": \"https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/CHEYYAR-CC-Engineer-PSL-Chey/1432365100/\", \"external_job_id\": \"1432365100\", \"detail_fetch_status\": \"NOT_FETCHED\"}','ats_direct_successfactors','DIRECT',NULL,'{\"raw_title\": \"raw_metadata.title\", \"raw_location\": \"location\"}',NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,NULL,'CHEYYAR CC, Cheyyar-MSPT, IN','Engineer - PSL'),(6170,'JOB_COMP_TOP200_011_507b6468617e','Manager - Build',NULL,NULL,'Chennai, Chennai-MRV-AD, IN',NULL,'India',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,NULL,'https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Manager-Build-Chen/1436579600','https://www.mahindra.com/career','2026-10-17T12:30:19.260257+00:00','EXPIRED',0,'VERIFIED_HTTP_200',NULL,NULL,'df7504270189fbc6bbf5c53176e2800ca4998d30112734d50348fdbc2bf88103','COMP_TOP200_011','https://jobs.mahindracareers.com/job/Chennai-Manager-Bu